hadiths[965]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10998","Haddathana Hushaym, haddathana Abu Bishr from Abu al-Mutawakkil from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that people from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were on a journey and passed a tribe from the tribes of the Arabs and sought hospitality from them, but they refused to host them. Then a man among them was afflicted in his mind or stung. They said to the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Is there among you one who charms? A man among them said: Yes. He came to their companion and charmed him with the Opening of the Book, so he recovered, and he was given a flock of sheep, but he refused to accept until he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Him Who sent you with the truth, I charmed him only with the Opening of the Book. He smiled and said: How did you know it is a charm? He said: Then he said: Take, and strike for me a share with you."
"10999","Haddathana Hushaym, haddathana Mansur, meaning Ibn Zadahn, from al-Walid ibn Muslim from Abu al-Mutawakkil or from Abu al-Siddiq from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri he said: We used to estimate the standing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr and Asr. We estimated the standing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Zuhr in the first two rak'ahs as much as the recitation of thirty verses, as much as the recitation of Surat Tanzil al-Sajdah. We estimated his standing in the last two as half of that. We estimated his standing in Asr in the first two rak'ahs as half of that. We estimated his standing in the last two as half of the first two."
"11000","Haddathana Hushaym, haddathana Ali ibn Zayd from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Resurrection, without boasting; I am the first for whom the earth splits on the Day of Resurrection, without boasting; and I am the first intercessor on the Day of Resurrection, without boasting."
"11001","Haddathana Hushaym from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: Ma'iz ibn Malik came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him that he had committed an immorality, and he turned him away repeatedly. He said: Then he ordered concerning him and he was stoned. He said: So we set out and stoned him. He said: We set out to al-Harrah and stoned him, then we turned back to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him. When evening came, he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: What is the matter with people, a word dropped on my father."
"11002","Haddathana Hushaym, haddathana Abu Bishr from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id that a man from the Ansar was in need, and his family said to him: Go to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ask him. So he came to him while he was preaching and saying: Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste, and whoever seeks sufficiency, Allah will enrich him, and whoever asks us and we find something for him, we give him. He said: So he went away and did not ask."
"11003","Haddathana Hushaym, akhbarana Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nu'm al-Bajali from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked what the muhrim kills. He said: The snake, the scorpion, the vicious little mouse, and he throws at the crow but does not kill it, and the vicious dog, the kite, and the predatory beast."
"11004","Haddathana Mu'tamir who said: Haddathana my father, akhbarana Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade the jar to make nabidh in, and dates and unripe dates, and dates and raisins to be mixed together."
"11005","Haddathana Mu'tamir from his father who said: Abu Nadrah informed me from Abu Sa'id that the keeper of dates came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a date and he disapproved of it. He said: How did you get this. He said: We bought a sa' for two sa's of our dates. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have engaged in riba."
"11006","Haddathana Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, haddathana Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah from Yahya ibn Umarah who said: I heard Abu Sa'id say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Prompt your dying ones with the saying: There is no god but Allah."
"11007","Haddathana Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr, haddathana Zuhayr meaning Ibn Muhammad from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not point you to that by which Allah expiates sins and increases good deeds. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Performing wudu fully despite hardship, and many steps to these mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer. There is none of you who leaves his house in purification and prays with the Muslims, then sits in the gathering waiting for the next prayer, except the angels say: O Allah forgive him, O Allah have mercy on him. When you stand for prayer, straighten your rows and establish them and close the gaps, for I see you from behind my back. When your imam says Allah is Greatest, say Allah is Greatest, and when he bows, bow, and when he says Allah hears whoever praises Him, say O Allah our Lord to You is praise. The best rows of men are the front and the worst are the back, and the best rows of women are the back and the worst are the front. O company of women, when men prostrate, lower your gaze, do not see the nakedness of men because of the tightness of waist-wrappers."
"11008","Haddathana Abd al-Malik ibn Amr, haddathana Abbad meaning Ibn Rashid from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: You do deeds which are finer in your eyes than hair; we used to count them at the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among the destructive sins."
"11009","Haddathana Abu Amir, haddathana al-Zubayr ibn Abdullah, haddathani Rubayh ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri from his father who said: We said on the day of al-Khandaq: O Messenger of Allah, is there anything we can say, for hearts have reached throats. He said: Yes. O Allah cover our nakedness and secure our fears. He said: So Allah, mighty and majestic, struck the faces of His enemies with wind, and Allah defeated them with wind."
"11010","Haddathana Abu Amir, haddathana Abd al-Malik ibn Hasan al-Harithi, haddathana Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Sulaym who said: I heard a man from us, Abd al-Malik said I forgot his name but his name is Mu'awiyah or Ibn Mu'awiyah, narrating from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The dead person knows who carries him and who washes him and who lowers him into his grave. Ibn Umar, who was in the gathering, said: From whom did you hear this. He said: From Abu Sa'id. So Ibn Umar went to Abu Sa'id and said: O Abu Sa'id, from whom did you hear this. He said: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"11011","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Hammam, haddathana Qatadah from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id: Our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to recite the Opening of the Book and what is easy."
"11012","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri, haddathana Yazid ibn Mardanubah who said: Haddathana Ibn Abi Nu'm from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youths of Paradise."
"11013","Haddathana Abu Amir, haddathana Abbad meaning Ibn Rashid from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: I attended a funeral with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O people, this nation will be tested in their graves. When a man is buried and his companions disperse from him, an angel comes to him with a hammer in his hand and sits him up and says: What do you say about this man. If he was a believer he says: I bear witness there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He says: You have spoken truthfully. Then a door to Hell is opened for him and he says: This would have been your abode had you disbelieved in your Lord, but since you believed, this is your abode. Then a door to Paradise is opened for him and he wants to rise toward it, and he says to him: Stay still, and his grave is made spacious for him. If he was a disbeliever or hypocrite, he says to him: What do you say about this man. He says: I do not know, I heard people saying something. He says: You did not know, nor did you recite, nor were you guided. Then a door to Paradise is opened for him and he says: This would have been your abode had you believed in your Lord, but since you disbelieved in Him, Allah, mighty and majestic, has exchanged this for you. And a door to Hell is opened for him, then he strikes him a blow with the hammer which all Allah's creation hears except the two heavy ones. Some people said: O Messenger of Allah, there is no one over whom an angel stands with a hammer in his hand except he is terrified at that. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word."
"11014","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, haddathana Hammam, haddathana Yahya from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Witr is at night."
"11015","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Hammad, haddathana al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked Ibn Sa'id about the soil of Paradise. He said: Fine white flour, pure musk. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He spoke truthfully."
"11016","Haddathana Rawh, haddathana Malik ibn Anas from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman that Hafs ibn Asim informed him from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is between my house and my pulpit is a garden from the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon my Pond."
"11017","Haddathana Aswad ibn Amir, haddathana Abu Bakr from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard so-and-so and so-and-so praising well, mentioning that you gave them two dinars. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: But by Allah, so-and-so is not like that; I gave him from ten to a hundred, yet he does not say that. Indeed, by Allah, one of you takes his asking from me, clutching it under his arm, meaning it will be under his armpit, meaning fire. He said: Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you give it to them. He said: What should I do, they refuse except that, and Allah refuses for me miserliness."
"11018","Haddathana Rib'i ibn Ibrahim, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mu'awiyah from al-Harith, freedman of Ibn Siba', from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sings for sufficiency Allah will enrich him, and whoever seeks chastity Allah will make him chaste."
"11019","Haddathana Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, haddathana Ayyub from Nafi' who said: Umar said: Do not sell gold for gold and silver for silver except like for like, and do not give preference of one over the other, and do not sell something absent among them for something present, for I fear for you Rama, and Rama is riba. He said: A man narrated this hadith to Ibn Umar from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he had not finished his statement before he entered with him to Abu Sa'id, and I was with him, and said: This one narrated to me from you a hadith claiming you narrate it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; did you hear it. He said: My eye saw and my ear heard; I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Do not sell gold for gold nor silver for silver except like for like, and do not give preference of one over the other, and do not sell something absent among them for something present."
"11020","Haddathana Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, akhbarana Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The believer is not afflicted by fatigue, nor weariness, nor grief, nor sickness, nor harm, even worry that worries him, except Allah expiates thereby some of his sins."
"11021","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa' from Ibn Abi Nu'm from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: Ali sent from Yemen to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gold in tanned leather not yet separated from its soil, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divided it among four: among Zayd al-Khayr, al-Aqra' ibn Habis, Uyaynah ibn Hisn, and Alqamah ibn Ulathah or Amir ibn al-Tufayl, Umarah doubted. Some of his companions, the Ansar and others, resented that. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Will you not trust me when I am the trustee of Him who is in heaven; news comes to me from heaven morning and evening. Then a man came to him with sunken eyes, prominent cheeks, raised forehead, thick beard, raised waist-wrapper, shaven head, and said: Fear Allah, O Messenger of Allah. He raised his head to him and said: Woe to you, am I not the most deserving of the people of earth to fear Allah. Then he turned away. Khalid said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not strike his neck. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Perhaps he prays. He said: There are many who pray saying with their tongues what is not in their hearts. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was not ordered to search the hearts of people nor to split their bellies. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, looked at him as he turned away and said: Indeed, from the offspring of this one a people will emerge who recite the Quran and it does not pass their throats; they pass through religion as the arrow passes through the game."
"11022","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Fudayl, haddathana Dirar meaning Ibn Murrah Abu Sinan from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, mighty and majestic, says: Fasting is Mine and I reward for it. The fasting person has two joys: when he breaks fast he rejoices, and when he meets Allah and He rewards him he rejoices. By Him in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the changed smell of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasant to Allah than the scent of musk."
"11023","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Adi from Shu'bah from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father that he heard Abu Sa'id asked about the waist-wrapper. He said: You have come upon one well-informed. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Muslim's waist-wrapper is to the middle of the shins; there is no sin or no harm on him in what is between that and the ankles; what is lower than that is in the Fire. Allah does not look at one who drags his wrapper out of pride."
"11024","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Dawud from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered us to build the mosque, so we carried brick by brick, while Ammar carried two bricks at a time and his head became dusty. He said: My companions narrated to me, and I did not hear it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he began to shake his head and say: Woe to you, O son of Sumayyah, the transgressing party will kill you."
"11025","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Dawud from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will be at the end of time a caliph who gives wealth and does not count it."
"11026","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Dawud from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of lizards, so what do you command us or what do you rule for us. He said: It was mentioned to me that a nation from the Children of Israel was transformed, and he neither ordered nor forbade. Abu Sa'id said: After that Umar said: Allah benefits more than one by it, and it is the food of most shepherds; had it been with me I would have eaten it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only found it distasteful."
"11027","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Dawud from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shouting loudly with Hajj, until when we circumambulated the House he said: Make it Umrah except whoever has the sacrificial animal with him. He said: So we made it Umrah and exited ihram, and when the day of Tarwiyah came we shouted with Hajj and went to Mina."
"11028","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Adi from Dawud from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: We waited for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night for Isha prayer until about half the night had gone. He said: He came and prayed with us, then said: Take your seats, for people have taken their beds, and you will remain in prayer since you waited for it. Were it not for the weakness of the weak, the sickness of the sick, and the need of the one with need, I would have delayed this prayer to half the night."
"11029","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Sulayman meaning al-Taymi from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for the people of Hell who are its people, they neither die nor live. As for people whom Allah intends mercy for, He causes them to die in Hell, then intercessors enter upon them, and a man takes his supporters and scatters them, or he said they grow on the river of shyness, or he said al-Hayawan, or he said al-Hayah, or he said the river of Paradise, and they grow like the growth of grain in the flood's debris. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you not see the tree, it is green then it is yellow, or he said it is yellow then it is green. He said: Some of them said: As if the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was in the desert."
"11030","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Sulayman from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let not fear of people prevent one of you from speaking truth when he sees it or witnesses it or hears it. Abu Sa'id said: I wish I had not heard it."
"11031","Haddathana Ibn Abi Adi from Sulayman from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned a people who will be in his nation, emerging amid a division of people, their mark is shaving; they are the worst of creation or among the worst of creation; the nearer of the two parties to truth will kill them. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, struck a parable for them, or he said a saying: A man shoots at game, or he said at a target, and looks at the arrowhead and sees no trace, and looks at the shaft and sees no trace, and looks at the notch and sees no trace. Abu Sa'id said: And you killed them, O people of Iraq."
"11032","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Abi Adi from Sa'id meaning Ibn Abi Arubah who said: Haddathani Sulayman al-Naji from Abu al-Mutawakkil from Abu Sa'id that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with his companions, then he came and the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who will trade with this one or give charity to this one and pray with him. He said: So a man prayed with him."
"11033","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi who said: Haddathana Malik from al-Zuhri from Ata ibn Yazid from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you hear the call, say as the caller says."
"11034","Abdullah said: Abd Allah ibn Awn al-Kharraz and Mus'ab al-Zubayri narrated it to us, they said: Haddathana Malik ibn Anas from al-Zuhri, and he mentioned the same equally."
"11035","Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, he is Ibn Mahdi, haddathana Malik from Dawud ibn al-Husayn from Abu Sufyan from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade muzabanah and muhaqalah. Muzabanah is buying fruit on palm tops with dates by measure, and muhaqalah is renting land."
"11036","Haddathana Sufyan ibn Uyaynah from al-Zuhri from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade two garments and two sales. As for the two sales, mulamasah and munabadhah. The two garments are wrapping the samma and sitting with knees up in one garment with nothing of it over his private part."
"11037","Haddathana Hashim, haddathana Layth, haddathani Ibn Shihab from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wrapping the samma and that a man sit with knees up in one garment with nothing of it over his private part."
"11038","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, haddathana Ma'mar from al-Zuhri who said: Ata ibn Yazid said, and Hajjaj narrated it to us from Ibn Jurayj who said: Akhbarani Ibn Shihab from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade, and he mentioned the same, meaning the same hadith."
"11039","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw spit in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it with a pebble, then forbade a man to spit in front of him or to his right, and said: Let him spit to his left or under his left foot."
"11040","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Zuhri from Ubayd Allah from Abu Sa'id that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade drinking by bending waterskins."
"11041","Haddathana Sufyan from Safwan ibn Sulaym from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Sa'id as a narration, and once he said raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Bathing on Friday, he said it is obligatory on every adult."
"11042","Haddathana Sufyan from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub from his father who said: I asked Abu Sa'id: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the waist-wrapper. He said: Yes, learn. I heard him say: The believer's wrapper is to the middle of his shins; there is no sin in what is between that and the ankles, and what is below the ankles is in the Fire, saying it three times."
"11043","Haddathana Sufyan, haddathana Yazid ibn Khusayfah from Busr ibn Sa'id from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: I was in a circle of the Ansar's circles, and Abu Musa came to us as if frightened. He said: Umar ordered me to come to him, so I came and asked permission three times and was not permitted, so I returned, though the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had said that: Whoever asks permission three times and is not permitted, let him return. He said: You must bring proof of what you say, or I will hurt you. Abu Sa'id said: So Abu Musa came to us frightened, or he said alarmed, and said: I call you to witness. Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: None will stand with you except the youngest of the people. Abu Sa'id said: And I was the youngest of them, so I stood with him and testified that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever asks permission three times and is not permitted, let him return."
"11044","Haddathana Sufyan from Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah from his father from Abu Sa'id as a narration, and he mentioned in it the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There is no charity in less than five uqiyahs, nor charity in less than five camels, nor charity in less than five wasqs."
"11045","Haddathana Sufyan, haddathani Ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father who said: Abu Sa'id said to me, and he was in a room, and said to me: O my son, when you call adhan, raise your voice with the call, for I heard the Messenger of Allah say: Nothing hears it except it testifies for him, jinn, nor man, nor stone. And once he said: O my son, when you are in the deserts, raise your voice with the call, for I heard the Messenger of Allah say: No jinn, nor man, nor stone, nor anything hears it except it testifies for him. My father said: Sufyan errs in his name, and the correct is Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah."
"11046","Haddathana Sufyan from Ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah, a shaykh from the Ansar, from his father from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: It is near that the best wealth of the Muslim man will be sheep with which he follows mountain peaks and places of rain, fleeing with his religion from trials."
"11047","Haddathana Sufyan from Damrah from Abu Sa'id, my father said I said Sufyan heard it, he claimed: The Messenger of Allah forbade prayer after Asr until sunset and after dawn until sunrise."
"11048","Haddathana Sufyan, haddathana Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu Salamah, and Ibn Abi Labid from Abu Salamah, I heard Abu Sa'id, and Ibn Jurayj from Sulayman al-Ahwal from Abu Salamah from Abu Sa'id: He observed i'tikaf in the middle ten, and we observed i'tikaf with him, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. When it was the morning of twenty, he passed by us while we were moving our belongings, and said: Whoever was in i'tikaf, let him be in his place of i'tikaf. I saw this night and it was made forgotten to me, and I saw myself prostrating in water and mud. The roof of the mosque was palm branches, then the sky rained, and I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with traces of water and mud on his nose and forehead."
"11049","Haddathana Sufyan from Ibn Ajlan from Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh, he heard Abu Sa'id say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said while on the pulpit: What I fear most for you is what Allah brings forth of the vegetation of earth and the bloom of the world. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, does good bring evil. He fell silent until we saw he was receiving revelation. He was covered with labored breathing and sweat. He said: Where is the questioner. He said: Here I am, and I intended only good. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Good brings only good, good brings only good, good brings only good. But the world is green and sweet, and what spring grows kills by overeating or nearly, except the eater of greens, for it ate until its flanks extended and faced the sun, then dropped dung and urinated, then returned and ate. Whoever takes it rightfully is blessed in it, and whoever takes it wrongfully is not blessed, and is like one who eats and is not satisfied. Sufyan said: Al-A'mash used to ask me about this hadith."
"11050","Haddathana Sufyan from Asim from Abu al-Mutawakkil from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: He performs wudu when he has intercourse and when he wants to return. Sufyan said: Abu Sa'id lived through al-Harrah. He said."
"11051","Yazid ibn Harun said from Hisham from Yahya from Hilal from Abu Sa'id: It kills by overeating or by confusion, but it is by overeating."
"11052","I heard Sufyan say: Allah, mighty and majestic, will make you successors in it and see how you act. Indeed every treacherous person will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection at his buttocks according to his treachery."
"11053","And it was read to Sufyan: I heard Ali ibn Zayd from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"11054","Haddathana Sufyan from Mutarrif from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: How can I enjoy when the master of the Trumpet has grasped the Trumpet, bent his forehead, and inclined his hearing, waiting when he will be ordered. The Muslims said: O Messenger of Allah, what shall we say. He said: Say: Allah suffices us and He is the best Disposer, upon Allah we rely."
"11055","Haddathana Sufyan from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Qaza'ah from Abu Sa'id as a narration raising it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: A woman does not travel three days except with a mahram. He forbade fasting the Fitr and the day of Sacrifice, and forbade two prayers: prayer after Asr until sunset, and after dawn until sunrise. Saddles are not tied except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and al-Aqsa Mosque."
"11056","Haddathana Sufyan from Amr, he heard Jabir narrating from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will come upon people a time when a group of people go to war and it is said: Is there among you one who accompanied the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They say: Yes, and victory is given them. Then a group goes to war and it is said: Is there among you one who accompanied one who accompanied the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They say: Yes, and victory is given them. Then a group goes to war and they say: Is there among you one who accompanied one who accompanied the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. They say: Yes, and victory is given them."
"11057","Haddathana Sufyan, he heard Amr from Attab ibn Hunayn narrating from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, and Sufyan said I do not know who Attab is: If Allah withheld rain from people seven years then sent it, a party would become disbelievers thereby, saying: We were rained by the rising of al-Mijdah."
"11058","Haddathana Abu Sa'id freedman of Banu Hashim, haddathana Sulayman ibn Bilal, haddathana Sharik ibn Abi Namir from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id from his father who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on Monday to Quba."
"11059","Haddathana Abu Sa'id, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal, haddathana Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever asks and he has the value of an uqiyah has begged importunately."
"11060","Haddathana Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il who said: Haddathana Hammad meaning Ibn Salamah, haddathana al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you comes to a walled garden and wants to eat, let him call: O owner of the garden, three times. If he answers him, otherwise let him eat. When one of you passes by camels and wants to drink from their milk, let him call: O owner of camels, or O shepherd of camels. If he answers him, otherwise let him drink. Hospitality is three days, and what is beyond is charity."
"11061","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Isa who said: Haddathani Layth who said: Haddathani Imran ibn Abi Anas from Ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri from his father that he said: Two men disputed about the mosque founded on piety from the first day. One man said: It is the mosque of Quba. Another said: It is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is my mosque."
"11062","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ja'far, haddathana Sa'id that Muhammad narrated that Dhakwan Abu Salih narrated from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and Jabir ibn Abdullah and Abu Hurayrah that they were forbidden money exchange, and two men among them raised it to the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"11063","Haddathana Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf, haddathana Sa'id from Matar from Muhammad ibn Sirin that Dhakwan Abu Salih said, and he praised him well, narrated from Jabir ibn Abdullah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah that they were forbidden money exchange; two men among them raised it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"11064","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id from Ash'ath from Muhammad from Abu Salih Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id and Jabir, two of these three, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade money exchange."
"11065","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ghaylan, haddathana Rishdin who said: Haddathana Amr ibn al-Harith from Abu al-Samh from Abu al-Haytham from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Believers in this world are of three parts: Those who believe in Allah and His Messenger then do not doubt and strive with their wealth and selves in Allah's path; and one whom people trust with their wealth and selves; then one who, when he faces greed, leaves it for Allah, mighty and majestic."
"11066","Haddathana Sa'id ibn Mansur, haddathana Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad who said: Akhbarani Rubayh ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sacrificed a horned ram and said: This is from me and from whoever of my nation did not sacrifice."
"11067","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Idris meaning al-Shafi'i who said: Anba'ana Malik from Dawud ibn al-Husayn from Abu Sufyan freedman of Abu Ahmad from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade muzabanah and muhaqalah. Muzabanah is buying dates with dates on palm tops, and muhaqalah is renting land for wheat."
"11068","Haddathana Abdullah ibn Muhammad, Abu Abd al-Rahman said and I heard it myself from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, haddathana Abu Khalid al-Ahmar from al-A'mash from al-Dahhak al-Mashriqi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Quran in a night. That was hard on his companions and they said: Who can do that. He said: Recite Say He is Allah One, for it is a third of the Quran."
"11069","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, haddathana Bakr ibn Mudar from Ibn al-Had from Abdullah ibn Khabbab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When one of you sees a dream he loves, it is only from Allah, so let him praise Allah for it and narrate it. When he sees other than that which he dislikes, it is only from Satan, so let him seek refuge in Allah from its evil and not mention it to anyone, for it will not harm him."
"11070","Haddathana Qutaybah, haddathana Bakr ibn Mudar from Ibn al-Had from Abdullah ibn Khabbab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Do not fast continuously. Whoever of you wants to fast continuously, let him continue only to dawn. They said: You fast continuously. He said: I am not like you; I spend night with One who feeds me and gives me drink."
"11071","Haddathana Qutaybah, haddathana Abdullah ibn Wahb from Amr ibn al-Harith from Darraj from Abu al-Haytham from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no forbearing except one with honor, and no wise except one with experience."
"11072","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, haddathana Layth from Ibn al-Had from Yuhannas freedman of Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at al-Arj, a poet appeared reciting, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seize the devil, or hold the devil. For a man's belly to be filled with pus is better for him than to be filled with poetry."
"11073","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, haddathana Layth meaning Ibn Sa'd from Ibn al-Had from Abdullah ibn al-Khabbab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was reminded of his uncle Abu Talib, and said: Perhaps my intercession will benefit him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will be placed in a shallow part of Fire reaching his ankles, from which his brain boils."
"11074","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, haddathana Layth from Khalid ibn Yazid from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal from Abu Ya'qub al-Khayyat who said: I attended al-Fitr with Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr in Medina, and he sent to Abu Sa'id and asked him how the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to do. Abu Sa'id informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray before preaching, so he prayed that day before the sermon."
"11075","Haddathana Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, haddathana Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri from his father who said: My mother sent me to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to ask him. I came and sat. He faced me and said: Whoever seeks sufficiency, Allah will enrich him, and whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste, and whoever seeks enough, Allah will suffice him. Whoever asks and he has the value of an uqiyah has begged importunately. He said: I said: My she-camel al-Yaqutah is better than an uqiyah. So I returned and did not ask him."
"11076","Haddathana al-Hakam ibn Musa, haddathana Ibn Abi al-Rijal similarly."
"11077","Haddathana Qutaybah, haddathana Ya'qub meaning the reciter, haddathana Suhayl from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not sell gold for gold nor silver for silver except weight for weight, like for like, equal for equal."
"11078","And he said: When heat intensifies, cool with prayer, for intense heat is from the breath of Hell."
"11079","Haddathana Ali ibn Abdullah, haddathana Mu'adh ibn Hisham who said: Haddathani my father from Amir al-Ahwal from Abu al-Siddiq from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the believer desires a child in Paradise, his carrying, delivery, and age will be in one hour as he desires."
"11080","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id, haddathana Ibn Ajlan, haddathani Iyad ibn Abdullah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to love palm stalks to hold in his hand. He entered the mosque and saw spit in the qiblah of the mosque, so he scraped it with it until he cleaned it."
"11081","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id who said: Haddathana Sulayman al-Taymi, haddathana Abu Nadrah who said: Haddathani Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he forbade the jar to make nabidh in, and dates and raisins to be mixed together, and unripe dates and dates to be mixed together."
"11082","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah and Muhammad ibn Ubayd who said: Haddathana al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of Hell enter Hell, death will be brought as if a white-spotted ram and made to stand between Paradise and Hell. It will be said: O people of Paradise, do you know this. He said: They will crane and look and say: Yes, this is death. He said: It will be said: O people of Hell, do you know this. He said: They will crane and look and say: Yes, this is death. He said: It will be ordered and slaughtered. He said: And it will be said: O people of Paradise, eternity without death, and O people of Hell, eternity without death. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited: And warn them of the Day of Regret when the matter is decided while they are in heedlessness. He said: And he signaled with his hand. Muhammad ibn Ubayd said in his hadith: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of Hell enter Hell, death will be brought as if a white-spotted ram."
"11083","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: My parable and the parable of the prophets before me is like a man who built a house and completed it except one brick. I came and completed that brick."
"11084","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about His saying mighty and majestic: And thus We made you a middle nation, he said: Just."
"11085","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana al-A'mash from Sa'd al-Ta'i from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned the master of the Trumpet and said: On his right is Jibril and on his left is Mika'il, upon them be peace."
"11086","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana al-A'mash from Ja'far ibn Iyas from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us in an expedition of thirty riders. He said: We stopped with an Arab tribe. He said: We asked them to host us and they refused. He said: Their master was stung. He said: They came to us and said: Is there among you one who charms from the scorpion. He said: I said: Yes, I, but I will not do until you give us something. They said: We will give you thirty sheep. He said: So I recited over him Praise be to Allah seven times. He said: He recovered. When we took the sheep, doubt entered our minds about it. He said: We refrained until we came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: We mentioned that to him. He said: Did you know it is a charm. Divide it and strike for me a share with you."
"11087","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed on a mat."
"11088","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in one garment placing its ends on his shoulders."
"11089","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana al-A'mash from Isma'il ibn Raja from his father and from Qays ibn Muslim from Tariq ibn Shihab, both from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: Marwan brought out the pulpit on Eid day, though it was not brought out, and began with the sermon before prayer, though it was not begun with. A man stood and said: O Marwan, you opposed the Sunnah; you brought out the pulpit on Eid day though it was not brought out on Eid day, and you began with the sermon before prayer though it was not begun with. He said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: Who is this. They said: So-and-so son of so-and-so. He said: Abu Sa'id said: As for this one, he has fulfilled what was upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever of you sees evil, if he can change it with his hand let him do, and once he said let him change it with his hand; if he cannot with his hand, with his tongue; if he cannot with his tongue, with his heart, and that is the weakest of faith. Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about His saying: While they are in heedlessness, he said: In this world."
"11090","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana Ubayd Allah ibn al-Walid al-Wassafi from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever says when he goes to his bed: I seek forgiveness from Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer, and I repent to Him, three times, Allah forgives his sins though they be like sea foam, though like the sand of Alij, though like the number of tree leaves."
"11091","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Abu Nadrah who said: I said to Abu Sa'id: Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about gold for gold and silver for silver. He said: I will inform you what I heard from him. His date-keeper came to him with good dates, and the dates of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were called al-Lawn. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Where did you get these good dates. He said: I went with two sa's of our dates and bought a sa' of these. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: You engaged in riba. Abu Sa'id then said: Are dates for dates more usurious, or silver for silver and gold for gold."
"11092","Haddathana Isma'il ibn Ibrahim from Sa'id al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, observed i'tikaf in the middle ten of Ramadan seeking Laylat al-Qadr before it was shown to him. When they ended, he ordered his structure removed and it was removed, then it was shown to him that it is in the last ten, so he ordered the structure returned and it was returned, then observed i'tikaf in the last ten. Then he came out to people and said: O people, Laylat al-Qadr was shown to me and I came out to inform you of it, but two men came disputing with Satan with them, and it was made forgotten to me. Seek it in the ninth, seventh, and fifth. I said: O Abu Sa'id, you know counting better than us. He said: I am more entitled to that than you. What are the ninth, seventh, and fifth. He said: Leave what you call twenty-one, and what follows it is the ninth; leave what you call twenty-three, and what follows it is the seventh; leave what you call twenty-five, and what follows it is the fifth."
"11093","Haddathana Isma'il, akhbarana Sa'id ibn Yazid from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: As for the people of Hell who are its people, they do not die in it nor live. But people, or as he said, Fire afflicts them for their sins, or he said for their faults, and causes them death until when they become coal, permission is given for intercession. They are brought in bundles upon bundles and grow upon the rivers of Paradise. It is said: O people of Paradise, pour upon them. They grow like the growth of grain in flood debris. He said: A man among the people then said: As if the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had been in the desert."
"11094","Haddathana Isma'il, akhbarana Ibn Awn from Muhammad from Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn Mas'ud who said: He returned the hadith until he returned it to Abu Sa'id who said: That was mentioned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: What is that. They said: A man has a wife who nurses and he has intercourse with her but dislikes that she become pregnant from him, and a man has a slave girl and has intercourse with her but dislikes that she become pregnant from him. He said: It does not matter if you do that, for it is only decree. Ibn Awn said: I narrated it to al-Hasan and he said: It does not matter, as if this is a rebuke."
"11095","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not revile my companions, for if one of you spent like Uhud in gold, it would not reach a mudd of one of them nor half of it."
"11096","Haddathana Abu Mu'awiyah, haddathana al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id, or from Abu Hurayrah, al-A'mash doubted, who said: When it was the Tabuk expedition, people suffered hunger and said: O Messenger of Allah, if you permitted us we would slaughter our water camels and eat and take oil. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: Do. Umar came and said: O Messenger of Allah, if they do, mounts will be few, but call them with the surplus of their provisions, then pray for blessing upon it; perhaps Allah will place blessing in that. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called for a leather mat and spread it, then called them with the surplus of their provisions. A man brought a handful of corn, another a handful of dates, another a piece of bread, until a little of that gathered on the mat. Then he prayed for blessing upon it, then said to them: Take in your vessels. He said: They took in their vessels until they left no vessel in the camp except they filled it, and ate until satisfied, and surplus remained. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I bear witness there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah; no servant meets Allah with them without doubt but Paradise is not veiled from him."
"11097","Haddathana Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, haddathana Muhammad ibn Ishaq who said: Haddathani Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Mu'ayqib from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Utwari, one of Banu Layth, and he was an orphan in the care of Abu Sa'id, Sulayman ibn Umar, and he is Abu al-Haytham who narrates from Abu Sa'id, who said: I heard Abu Sa'id say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Bridge is placed between the backs of Hell, upon it thorns like the thorns of al-Sa'dan. Then people cross: saved delivered, scratched by it then saved, held back by it thrown down in it. When Allah, mighty and majestic, finishes judgment among servants, believers miss men who were with them in the world praying their prayer, paying their zakat, fasting their fast, performing their Hajj, fighting their battles. They say: O our Lord, servants from Your servants were with us in the world praying our prayer, paying our zakat, fasting our fast, performing our Hajj, fighting our battles; we do not see them. He says: Go to Hell, and whomever you find therein among them, bring them out. He said: They find them taken by Fire according to their deeds: among them taken to his feet, among them taken to half his shins, among them taken to his knees, among them belted, among them taken to his breasts, among them taken to his neck, but faces are not covered. They bring them out and cast them into the water of life. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the water of life. He said: The washing of Paradise people. They grow like the growth of a plant, and once he said therein as a plant grows in flood debris. Then prophets intercede for everyone who testified there is no god but Allah sincerely, and bring them out. He said: Then Allah bestows with His mercy upon whoever is therein, and leaves no servant with a grain's weight of faith in his heart except He brings him out."
"11098","Haddathana Isma'il, haddathana al-Dastuwai, haddathani Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, haddathana Iyad who said: I said to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: One of us prays and does not know how many he prayed. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you prays and does not know how many he prayed, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting. When Satan comes to one of you and says: You have broken wudu, let him say: You lie, except what he finds its smell with his nose or hears its sound with his ear."
"11099","Haddathana Isma'il, akhbarana al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: We used to go to war with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; among us the fasting and among us the breaking. The fasting did not blame the breaking, nor the breaking the fasting. They saw that whoever found strength and fasted, that is good, and saw that whoever found weakness and broke fast, that is good."
"11100","Haddathana Isma'il, akhbarana al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: No sooner was Khaybar opened than we fell upon those greens and ate from them severely, and people were hungry. Then we traveled to the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, found the smell and said: Whoever eats anything of this foul tree, let him not approach us in the mosque. People said: It was forbidden, it was forbidden. That reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O people, I have no right to forbid what Allah made lawful, but it is a tree whose smell I dislike."
"11101","Ismail narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not write from me anything besides the Quran, and whoever wrote anything besides the Quran, let him erase it."
"11102","Ismail narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Rifaa, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The suhur meal, eating it is blessing, so do not leave it, even if one of you takes a sip of water, for Allah Almighty and His angels send blessings upon those who take suhur."
"11103","Shuayb ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammam informed us, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam informed us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not write from me anything, so whoever wrote from me anything, let him erase it."
"11104","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, he said: I asked Jabir about a man drinking while standing. Jabir said: We used to dislike that."
"11105","Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri testifying that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked that, and rebuked facing the qiblah for urination."
"11106","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Hisham, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that Abdullah ibn Umar opened a small door of his, and Abu Said al-Khudri was with him, when a snake came out upon them. Abdullah ibn Umar ordered killing it, so Abu Said said: Did you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that they be warned before killing them."
"11107","Shuayb ibn Harb narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever practices patience, Allah will make him patient, and whoever seeks independence, Allah will make him independent, and whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste, and I do not find for you a provision wider than patience."
"11108","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: We were sitting writing what we heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came out to us and said: What is this you are writing. We said: What we hear from you. He said: A book alongside the Book of Allah. We said: What we hear. He said: Write the Book of Allah, purify the Book of Allah, a book other than the Book of Allah, purify the Book of Allah, or make it pure. He said: So we gathered what we had written in one open ground, then burned it with fire. We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we narrate from you. He said: Yes, narrate from me, no harm, and whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hell. He said: So we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we narrate from Bani Israil. He said: Yes, narrate from Bani Israil, no harm, for you will not narrate from them anything except that there was among them something more astonishing than it."
"11109","Rawh narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing at Arafah supplicating thus, and he raised his hands level with his upper chest, and made the insides of his palms toward the ground."
"11110","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wrapping in a single garment with no opening, and that a man sit in ihtiba in a single garment with nothing of it over his private part."
"11111","Rawh narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers will be saved on the Day of Resurrection from the Fire, then detained on a bridge between Paradise and Hell, then retaliation will be taken for some of them from others for wrongs that were between them in this world, until when they are refined and purified, they are permitted to enter Paradise. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, one of them will be more guided to his dwelling in Paradise than he was to his dwelling in this world."
"11112","Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Shayban Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Firas ibn Yahya al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man entered Paradise who never did any good at all. He said to his family when death came to him: When I die, burn me, then crush me, then scatter half of me in the sea and half of me on land. So Allah commanded the land and the sea and they gathered him, then said: What carried you to do what you did. He said: Fear of You. He said: So He forgave him for that."
"11113","Hashim narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Nadrah al-Awfi, that Abu Said al-Khudri informed him, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about witr, so he said: Pray witr before dawn."
"11114","Husayn narrated to us, in the tafsir of Shayban, from Qatadah, he said: Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers will be saved from the Fire, then he mentioned the hadith."
"11115","Hasan and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise and Hell boasted. Hell said: O Lord, the tyrants, the arrogant, kings and nobles enter me. Paradise said: O Lord, the weak, poor and needy enter me. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says to Hell: You are My punishment, I afflict with you whom I will. And He said to Paradise: You are My mercy, encompassing everything, and each one of you will have its fill. So its people will be cast into Hell, and it will say: Is there more. He said: And they will be cast into it, and it will say: Is there more. And they will be cast into it, and it will say: Is there more, until He, Blessed and Exalted, comes to it and places His foot upon it, so it will be drawn together and say: Enough, enough. As for Paradise, its people will remain in it as long as Allah wills them to remain, then Allah will create for it a creation as He wills."
"11116","Hasan and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lightest in punishment among the people of Hell is a man with two sandals on his feet from which his brain boils, and among them is one in Hell up to his ankles with the punishment taking effect, and among them one in Hell up to his knees with the punishment taking effect, and among them one immersed in Hell up to his groin with the punishment taking effect, and among them one in Hell up to his chest with the punishment taking effect, and among them one immersed in Hell. Affan said: With the punishment taking effect, immersed."
"11117","Hasan narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Sad Abu al-Mujahid al-Tai, from Atiyyah ibn Sad al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, I think he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Any believer who gives a thirsty believer a drink, Allah will give him to drink on the Day of Resurrection from sealed nectar, and any believer who feeds a hungry believer, Allah will feed him from the fruits of Paradise, and any believer who clothes a naked believer with a garment, Allah will clothe him from the green garments of Paradise."
"11118","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and said: O Abu Said, three things, whoever says them will enter Paradise. I said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Whoever is pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad as Messenger. Then he said: O Abu Said, and the fourth has excellence like between heaven and earth, and it is jihad in the cause of Allah."
"11119","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafah supplicating thus, making the insides of his palms toward the ground."
"11120","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Israil, meaning Ismail ibn Abi Ishaq al-Mulai, informed us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am leaving among you the two weighty things, one greater than the other: the Book of Allah, a rope extended from heaven to earth, and my progeny, my household, and they will not separate until they return to me at the Basin."
"11121","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about hijrah. He said: Woe to you, hijrah is a grave matter. Do you have camels. He said: Yes. He said: Do you pay their charity. He said: Yes. He said: Do you lend from them. He said: Yes. He said: Do you milk them on the day they come to water. He said: Yes. He said: Then work from beyond the seas, for Allah will not diminish anything of your work."
"11122","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Qarm narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn al-Asbahani, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sends forth three of his children, they will shield him from the Fire."
"11123","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Sad al-Tai, from Atiyyah ibn Sad, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The companion of five will not enter Paradise: an addict of wine, a believer in magic, a severer of kinship, a soothsayer, and a reminder of favors."
"11124","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that a Bedouin asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about hijrah. He said: Woe to you, hijrah is a grave matter. Do you have camels. He said: Yes. He said: Do you not pay their charity. He said: Yes. He said: Do you not lend from them. He said: Yes. He said: Do you not milk them on the day they come to water. He said: Yes. He said: Then work from beyond the seas as you wish, for Allah will not diminish anything of your work."
"11125","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, that Abu al-Najib, mawla of Abdullah ibn Sad, narrated to him, that Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to him, that a man came from Najran to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a gold ring, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him and did not ask him about anything. The man returned to his wife and told her, so she said: You have some affair, return to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he returned to him, threw away his ring and a jubbah he was wearing. When he sought permission, he was permitted, and greeted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who returned the greeting. He said: O Messenger of Allah, you turned away from me before when I came to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You came to me with a coal of fire in your hand. He said: O Messenger of Allah, then I came with many coals, for he had come with ornaments from Bahrayn. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What you brought does not avail us anything, except as the stones of the Harrah avail, but it is the enjoyment of worldly life. The man said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, excuse me among your companions, lest they think you were angry with me for something. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and excused him, and informed that what was from him was only on account of his gold ring."
"11126","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Yazid ibn Abi Said, mawla of al-Mahri, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Bani Lihyan that one man out of every two men should go out, then said to the one who stays: Whichever of you succeeds the one who goes out among his family and wealth with good will have like half the reward of the one who goes out."
"11127","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, from Hanash ibn Abdullah, from Abu Said al-Khudri. My father said: It is not marfu. He said: Advance payment is not proper in wheat, barley and sult until it is threshed, nor in grapes, olives and the like until it ripens, nor gold cash for silver on credit, nor silver on credit for gold cash."
"11128","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu Said al-Khudri: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When one of you finishes his prayer in the mosque, then returns to his house then, let him pray in his house two rakahs, and let him make for his house a share of his prayer, for Allah will place in his house good from his prayer."
"11129","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah: I heard Abu al-Haytham say: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: I saw the whiteness of the side of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was prostrating."
"11130","Musa, he is Ibn Dawud, narrated it to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: As if I look at the whiteness of the side of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was prostrating."
"11131","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah informed us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: Qatadah ibn al-Numan spent the night reciting all night: Say, He is Allah, One. That was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, it equals half the Quran or a third of it."
"11132","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Habban ibn Wasi, from his father, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays in a garment, let him place its end over his shoulders."
"11133","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, Jabir informed me, that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri testifying that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked him for that, and rebuked him for facing the qiblah for urination."
"11134","And this follows the hadith of Ibn Lahiah from Abu al-Zubayr, who said: I asked Jabir about a man drinking while standing, and he said: We used to dislike that. Then he mentioned the hadith of Abu Said."
"11135","Bakr ibn Isa narrated to us, Jami ibn Matar al-Habati narrated to us, Abu Rubah Shaddad ibn Imran al-Qaysi narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that Abu Bakr came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I passed by such-and-such valley, and there was a humble devout man of good appearance praying. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go to him and kill him. Abu Bakr went to him, and when he saw him in that state, he disliked killing him, so he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Umar: Go and kill him. Umar went and saw him in that state in which Abu Bakr had seen him. He said: So he disliked killing him. He said: So he returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw him praying humbly and disliked killing him. He said: O Ali, go and kill him. He said: So Ali went and did not see him. Ali returned and said: O Messenger of Allah, he was not seen. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This man and his companions recite the Quran not passing their throats, they pass out of religion as an arrow passes out of game, then they do not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch, so kill them, they are the worst of creation."
"11136","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Mutarrif narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abi Nawf, from Sulayt ibn Ayyub, from Ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was performing ablution from the well of Budaah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you perform ablution from it while filth that is thrown is thrown into it. He said: Water, nothing makes it impure."
"11137","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will see your Lord Almighty. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we see our Lord. He said: So he said: Do you suffer difficulty in seeing the sun at midday. They said: No. He said: Do you suffer difficulty in seeing the moon on the night of full moon. They said: No. He said: Then you will not suffer difficulty in seeing Him except as you suffer difficulty in that. Al-Amash said: La tudarun means: you do not dispute."
"11138","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best rows of men are the first row, and the worst are the last row, and the best rows of women are the last, and the worst are the first. And he said: O assembly of women, do not raise your heads when you prostrate, lest you see the private parts of men due to the tightness of waist-wrappers."
"11139","Musab ibn al-Miqdam and Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, they said: Israil narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ismah al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the banner and shook it, then said: Who will take it with its right. So-and-so came and said: I. He said: Step aside. Then a man came and he said: Step aside. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him Who honored the face of Muhammad, I shall give it to a man who does not flee. Take it, O Ali. So he went until Allah gave victory over Khaybar and Fadak, and he came with their Ajwah dates and dried meat. Musab said: With its Ajwah and dried meat."
"11140","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard so-and-so speaking good, mentioning that you gave him two dinars. He said: But so-and-so does not say that nor praises with it, though I gave him between ten to a hundred, or he said to two hundred. One of them asks me a request, so I give it to him, and he goes out carrying it under his arm, and it is for them nothing but Fire. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you give them. He said: They refuse except to ask me, and Allah refuses for me miserliness."
"11141","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Uthman, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said, then he mentioned similar."
"11142","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Numan narrating from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and he was asked which people are best: A believer striving with his wealth and self in the cause of Allah. He said: Then who. He said: A believer in a mountain pass, fearing Allah and sparing people his evil."
"11143","He said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Fudayl narrated to us, from Atiyyah, Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first group to enter Paradise on the Day of Resurrection, their faces like the moon on the night of full moon, and the second group of a color better than a brilliant star in the sky. For each man among them two wives, over each wife seventy garments, the marrow of her leg seen from behind their flesh, blood and garments."
"11144","Ribi ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so we said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Do you suffer difficulty in seeing the sun with no cloud below it. He said: We said: No. He said: Do you suffer difficulty in seeing the moon on the night of full moon with no cloud below it. He said: We said: No. He said: Then you will see your Lord likewise on the Day of Resurrection. Allah will gather people on the Day of Resurrection in one open ground. He said: It will be said: Whoever worshipped something, let him follow it. Those who worshipped the sun will follow the sun and fall into Hell, those who worshipped the moon will follow the moon and fall into Hell, those who worshipped idols will follow idols and those who worshipped images will follow images and fall into Hell. He said: And all who were worshipped besides Allah, until they fall into Hell. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers remain, with their hypocrites among them, and remnants of the People of the Book, and he made them few with his hand. He said: Allah Almighty comes to them and says: Will you not follow what you worshipped. They say: We worshipped Allah and did not see Allah. Then the shin will be uncovered, and none who prostrated to Allah remains except falls prostrating, and none who prostrated for show and repute remains except falls on his back. He said: Then the bridge will be placed over Hell, with the prophets at its sides, their words: O Allah, save, save, O Allah, save, save. It is slippery, with hooks and pincers. Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know, perhaps he said: snatching people. And a thorn growing in Najd called al-Sadan. He said: And he described it to them. He said: I and my nation will be the first to pass, or the first to cross. They will pass over it like lightning, like wind, like fine horses and camels. Saved secure, scratched wounded, and piled into Hell. When they cross it, or when they pass it, none of you disputing concerning a right he knows is his right is more insistent than them concerning their brothers who fell into Hell, saying: O Lord, we raided together, performed Hajj together, performed Umrah together, so how are we saved today while they perished. He said: Allah Almighty says: Look, whoever had in his heart the weight of a dinar of faith, bring him out. They will be brought out. Then He says: Whoever had in his heart the weight of a qirat of faith, bring him out. They will be brought out. Then He says: Whoever had in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith, bring him out. They will be brought out. Then Abu Said said: Between me and you is the Book of Allah. Abd al-Rahman said: I think he means His saying: Even if it be the weight of a mustard seed, We shall bring it, and We suffice as reckoners. So they will be brought out of Hell and thrown into a river called the River of Life, sprouting as a seed sprouts in flood debris. Do you not see what grows toward the sun is green, and what grows toward shade is yellow. They said: O Messenger of Allah, as if you herded sheep. He said: Yes, I herded sheep."
"11145","Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Shayban Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Firas ibn Yahya al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man entered Paradise who never did any good at all. He said to his family when death came to him: When I die, burn me, then crush me, then scatter half of me in the sea and half of me on land. So Allah commanded the land and the sea and they gathered him, then said: What carried you to do what you did. He said: Fear of You. He said: So he was forgiven for that."
"11146","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Layth, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hearts are four: a bare heart with a lamp shining in it, an enveloped heart bound upon its cover, an inverted heart, and a two-faced heart. The bare heart is the believer's heart, its lamp is its light. The enveloped heart is the disbeliever's heart. The inverted heart is the hypocrite's heart, he knew then denied. The two-faced heart is a heart with faith and hypocrisy. Faith in it is like a herb nourished by good water, and hypocrisy in it is like an ulcer nourished by pus and blood. Whichever nourishment overcomes the other overcomes it."
"11147","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah Shayban narrated to us, from Matar ibn Tahman, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until a man from my household rules, broad forehead, prominent nose, filling the earth with justice as it was filled before him with injustice, for seven years."
"11148","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Talhah, narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I am about to be called and answer, and I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah Almighty and my progeny. The Book of Allah is a rope extended from heaven to earth, and my progeny, my household. The Gentle, All-Aware informed me that they will not separate until they return to me at the Basin. So watch me in how you succeed me concerning them."
"11149","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ali ibn Ali narrated to us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) planted a stick before him, then planted another beside it, then planted a third and placed it far, then said: Do you know what this is. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: This is man, this is his term, and this is his hope. He pursues hope, while the term snatches him before that."
"11150","Abu Amir narrated to us, Ali narrated to us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim supplicates with a supplication with no sin nor severing of kinship except Allah gives him one of three: hasten his supplication for him, store it for him in the Hereafter, or avert from him evil like it. They said: Then we will increase. He said: Allah is Greater."
"11151","Abu Amir narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Busr ibn Said, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed people and said: Allah Almighty gave a servant choice between this world and what is with Him. That servant chose what is with Allah. Abu Bakr, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, wept. We wondered at his weeping that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed of a servant given choice, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the one given choice, and Abu Bakr knew most of us of it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most favored of people upon me in his companionship and wealth is Abu Bakr. If I were taking from people a close friend besides my Lord, I would take Abu Bakr, but brotherhood of Islam, or its love. No door in the mosque remains except closed, except the door of Abu Bakr."
"11152","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Salim Abu al-Nadr, from Ubayd ibn Hunayn and Busr ibn Said, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed, then he mentioned the hadith."
"11153","Surayj narrated it to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Ubayd ibn Hunayn, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he narrated to him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed people, then he mentioned the hadith."
"11154","Abu Amir narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawali narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah al-Ansari narrated to me, he said: Abu Said was informed of a funeral, so he stayed behind until people took their seats, then he came. When the people saw him, they scattered from him, and some stood to seat him in his seat. He said: No, I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best sittings are the widest. Then he withdrew and sat in a wide sitting."
"11155","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from Hamzah ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say on this pulpit: What is with men saying the kinship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will not benefit his people. Yes indeed, by Allah, my kinship is joined in this world and the Hereafter, and I, O people, am your forerunner at the Basin. When you come, a man will say: O Messenger of Allah, I am so-and-so son of so-and-so, and his brother will say: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so. He says to them: As for lineage, I knew it, but you innovated after me and turned back on your heels."
"11156","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Hamzah ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the pulpit say, then he mentioned its meaning."
"11157","Abu Amir narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Harith, he said: Abu Hurayrah complained or was absent, so Abu Said al-Khudri led us in prayer, raising his voice with takbir when opening prayer, when bowing, when saying Allah hears whoever praises Him, when raising his head from prostration, when prostrating, and when standing between the two rakahs, until he finished his prayer thus. When he prayed, it was said to him: People disagreed over your prayer. So he went out and stood at the pulpit and said: O people, by Allah I do not care whether your prayer disagreed or not, thus I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray."
"11158","Abu Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No fatigue, illness, worry, sorrow, grief, nor harm befalls a Muslim man, even a thorn he is pricked with, except Allah Almighty expiates thereby some of his sins."
"11159","Mansur ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab al-Utaridi narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Follow me, those after you will follow you, for people will keep lagging until Allah Almighty delays them."
"11160","Yazid ibn Harun and Affan narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us after Asr until sunset. Those of us who memorized it memorized it, and those who forgot it forgot it. So he praised Allah. Affan said: And Hammad said: Most of my memory is that he said: Of what will be until the Day of Resurrection. So he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, the world is green and sweet, and Allah makes you successors in it and looks how you act. Beware the world and beware women. The sons of Adam were created in different ranks. Among them is one born a believer, living a believer, dying a believer. Among them is one born a disbeliever, living a disbeliever, dying a disbeliever. Among them is one born a believer, living a believer, dying a disbeliever. Among them is one born a disbeliever, living a disbeliever, dying a believer. Anger is a coal kindled in the belly of Adam. Do you not see the redness of his eyes and swelling of his jugular veins. If one of you finds something of that, the ground, the ground. The best men are slow to anger, quick to be pleased, and the worst men are quick to anger, slow to be pleased. If a man is slow to anger, slow to return, and quick to anger and quick to return, then it is with it. The best traders are good in paying, good in demanding, and the worst traders are bad in paying, bad in demanding. If a man is good in paying, bad in demanding, or bad in paying, good in demanding, then it is with it. Every traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection according to his treachery. The greatest treachery is the treachery of a general ruler. Let not fear of people prevent a man from speaking truth when he knows it. The best jihad is a word of truth before a tyrannical ruler. When it was at sunset, he said: What remains of the world compared to what passed is like what remains of this day of yours compared to what passed of it."
"11161","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of lizards, what do you command us. He said: It reached me that a nation from Bani Israil was transformed into beasts, and I do not know which beasts they are. So he neither commanded nor forbade."
"11162","Yazid narrated to us, Dawud informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: Abu Musa sought permission of Umar thrice, and Umar did not permit him, so he returned. Umar met him and said: What is your affair, you returned. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever seeks permission thrice and is not permitted, let him return. He said: You shall bring proof for this or I shall do and do. So he came to his people's gathering, and adjured them by Allah Almighty. I said: I am with you. So they testified for him of that, so he let them go."
"11163","Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my brother's belly is loose. He said: Give him honey to drink. He went, then came and said: I gave him to drink and it only increased looseness. He said: Give him honey to drink. He went, then came and said: I gave him to drink and it only increased looseness. He said: Give him honey to drink. He went, then came and said: I gave him to drink and it only increased looseness. He said to him on the fourth: Give him honey to drink. I think he said: So he gave him to drink and he recovered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the fourth: Allah spoke truth and your brother's belly lied."
"11164","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, and he narrated from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My nephew's belly is corrupted. He said: Give your nephew honey to drink. He gave him to drink and it only increased severity. He returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three times. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him on the third: Give your nephew honey to drink, for Allah Almighty spoke truth and your nephew's belly lied. He said: So he gave him to drink, and Allah Almighty healed him."
"11165","Yazid narrated to us, Zakariyya informed us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah gave every prophet a gift, and each hastened it, and I delayed my gift as intercession for my nation. A man from my nation will intercede for multitudes and they will enter Paradise, a man will intercede for a tribe, a man will intercede for a clan, a man will intercede for three, two, and one."
"11166","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Yahya, from Abu Ibrahim, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram with his companions in the year of Hudaybiyah except Uthman and Abu Qatadah, and he sought forgiveness for those who shaved thrice and for those who shortened once."
"11167","Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed me, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: Marwan addressed before prayer on Eid day. A man stood and said: Prayer was only before the sermon. He said: Do you see that, O Abu so-and-so. Abu Said al-Khudri stood and said: As for this, he discharged his duty. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever sees an evil, let him change it with his hand, if unable then with his tongue, if unable then with his heart, and that is the weakest faith."
"11168","Yazid narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The people of Hell whom Allah Almighty does not want to bring out neither die therein nor live, and the people of Hell whom Allah Almighty wants to bring out, He causes them to die a death until they become charcoal, then they are brought out in bundles and thrown upon the rivers of Paradise, or sprinkled from the rivers of Paradise, sprouting as a seed sprouts in flood debris."
"11169","Yazid narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever prays over a funeral and accompanies it will have two qirats, and whoever prays over it without accompanying it will have one qirat, and the qirat is like Uhud."
"11170","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Abu Naamah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed and removed his sandals, so people removed their sandals. When he finished, he said: Why did you remove your sandals. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you remove, so we removed. He said: Jibril came to me and informed me there was filth on them. When one of you comes to the mosque, let him turn his sandal and look in it, if he sees filth let him rub it on the ground, then pray in them."
"11171","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: I only narrate to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my ears heard it and my heart retained it. A servant killed ninety-nine souls, then repentance presented itself to him. He asked about the most knowledgeable of earth, and was directed to a man. He came to him and said: I killed ninety-nine souls, is there repentance for me. He said: After killing ninety-nine souls. He said: So he drew his sword and killed him with it, completing a hundred. Then repentance presented itself to him, so he asked about the most knowledgeable of earth, and was directed to a man. He came to him and said: I killed a hundred souls, is there repentance for me. He said: Who stands between you and repentance. Leave the evil village you are in for the righteous village, such-and-such village, and worship your Lord therein. He said: So he left for the righteous village, when his term met him on the way. The angels of mercy and angels of punishment disputed over him. Iblis said: I am most entitled to him, he never disobeyed me for a moment. The angels of mercy said: He left repentant. Hammam said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from Abu Rafi, he said: Allah Almighty sent to him an angel, so they disputed to him. Then he returned to the hadith of Qatadah. He said: So he said: Look, whichever village was nearer to him, join him to its people. Qatadah said: Al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: When he recognized death, he pushed himself forward, so Allah Almighty brought the righteous village near to him and distanced the evil village from him, so they joined him to the people of the righteous village."
"11172","Yazid narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq informed us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Duha until we said he does not leave it, and leave it until we said he does not pray it."
"11173","Yazid narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq informed us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri. I said to Fudayl: Did he raise it. He said: I think he raised it. He said: Whoever says when going out to prayer: O Allah, I ask You by the right of supplicants upon You and by the right of my walking, for I did not go out arrogantly, insolently, showily, nor for repute. I went out fearing Your wrath and seeking Your pleasure. I ask You to save me from the Fire and forgive my sins, for none forgives sins but You. Allah assigns seventy thousand angels seeking forgiveness for him, and Allah turns to him with His Face until he finishes his prayer."
"11174","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdillah al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us one day, ascended the pulpit, and we sat around him. He said: What I fear for you after me is what Allah opens for you of the blossom and adornment of the world. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, does good bring evil. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent, and we saw that Jibril was descending upon him. It was said to him: What is your affair, you speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he does not speak to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was relieved, wiping sweat from him. He said: Where is the questioner, as if praising him. He said: Good does not bring evil. What spring grows kills or nearly, with indigestion. Have you not seen the eater of greens, it ate until when its flanks extended and it faced the sun, then dropped dung, urinated, then grazed again. Wealth is sweet and green, and excellent companion of a Muslim man is it for whoever gives from it to the poor, orphan and traveler, or as he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. Whoever takes it without right is like one who eats and is not satiated, and it will be a witness against him on the Day of Resurrection."
"11175","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not write from me anything except the Quran, so whoever wrote from me anything other than the Quran, let him erase it."
"11176","Yazid narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you come upon a camel herdsman, call: O camel herdsman, thrice. If he answers you, otherwise milk and drink without spoiling. When you come upon a garden wall, call: O owner of the wall, thrice. If he answers you, otherwise eat. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days, what exceeds is charity."
"11177","Yazid narrated to us, Abu Masud al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, passing a river with rainwater, and the people were fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Drink. No one drank. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, and the people drank."
"11178","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu Asim, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When a man comes to his wife then wants to repeat, let him perform ablution."
"11179","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Dhakwan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man from the Ansar and sent to him. He came out dripping head. He said to him: Perhaps we hastened you. He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: When you are hastened or prevented, no ghusl upon you, upon you is ablution."
"11180","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: I heard Zayd Abu al-Hawari, he said: I heard Abu al-Siddiq narrating from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: We feared after our Prophet an event, so we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Mahdi will come out in my nation five or seven or nine, Zayd the doubter. He said: I said: What thing. He said: Years. Then he said: Heaven sends abundant rain upon them, earth withholds nothing of its plants, and wealth will be piled. A man comes to him and says: O Mahdi, give me, give me. He said: So he scoops for him in his garment what he can carry."
"11181","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Zayd Abu al-Hawari, he said: I heard Abu al-Siddiq narrating from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: We used to sell mothers of children in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11182","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Zayd Abu al-Hawari, he said: I heard Abu al-Siddiq narrating from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: We used to enjoy mutah in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a garment."
"11183","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid, from Ikrimah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ammar: The rebellious party will kill you."
"11184","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari al-Tai, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When this surah was revealed: When Allah's help and victory come, and you see people, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it until he finished it, and said: People are a side and I and my companions are a side. And he said: No hijrah after the conquest, but jihad and intention. Marwan said to him: You lied, and with him Rafi ibn Khadij and Zayd ibn Thabit, sitting with him on the couch. Abu Said said: If these two wished they would narrate to you, but this one fears you will remove him from leadership of his people, and this one fears you will remove him from charity. So they were silent. Marwan raised the stick to strike him. When they saw that, they said: He spoke truth."
"11185","Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The people of Qurayzah came down upon the judgment of Sad ibn Muadh. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to Sad, so he came on a donkey. When he neared the mosque, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand to your chief, or your best. Then he said: These came down upon your judgment. He said: Their fighters killed and their offspring enslaved. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You judged with Allah's judgment, and perhaps he said: You judged with the King's judgment."
"11186","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah, he said: I heard Abu Nadrah narrating from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The world is green and sweet, and Allah Almighty makes you successors in it to see how you act. Fear the world and fear women, for the first trial of Bani Israil was in women."
"11187","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Abu Umamah ibn Sahl narrating from Abu Said, then he mentioned the meaning of Ghundar's hadith from Shubah concerning the judgment of Sad ibn Muadh, except he said: I judge their fighters killed and their offspring enslaved. He said: You judged them with Allah's judgment. And once he said: You judged them with the judgment of the King or the Angel, Abd al-Rahman doubted."
"11188","And Affan narrated it to us, he said: The King."
"11189","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah informed us, then he mentioned like the hadith of Ibn Jafar: Their fighters killed and their offspring enslaved. And he said: You judged with the King's judgment. Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf said."
"11190","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Sirin, from Mabad, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about coitus interruptus, or he said concerning coitus interruptus: There is no harm upon you not to do that, for it is only destiny."
"11191","Husayn narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Anas ibn Sirin informed us, from his brother Mabad, then he mentioned similar."
"11192","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Fudayl narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved people to Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection and nearest to Him in sitting is a just imam, and the most hateful people to Allah on the Day of Resurrection and severest in punishment is a tyrannical imam."
"11193","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Arubah, Qatadah narrated to us, from one who met the delegation, mentioning Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, that the delegation of Abd al-Qays when they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: We are a tribe of Rabiah, and between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot come to you except in the sacred months. Command us with a matter if we take it we enter Paradise, and we command or call those behind us with it. He said: I command you four and forbid you four. Worship Allah and associate nothing with Him, this is not from the four, establish prayer, give zakat, fast Ramadan, and give a fifth of spoils. I forbid you four: dubba, naqir, hantam and muzaffat. They said: What is your knowledge of naqir. He said: A trunk hollowed, then they throw in qutay dates or dates and water, until when its boiling subsides you drink it, until one of you strikes his cousin with the sword. Among the people was a man wounded thus, so I hid it shy from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: What do you command us to drink in. He said: In waterskins tied over their mouths. They said: Our land has many rats, leather waterskins do not remain in it. He said: Even if rats eat them twice or thrice. And he said to Ashajj Abd al-Qays: In you are two traits Allah Almighty loves: forbearance and deliberation."
"11194","Yahya narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ishaq, he said: Zaynab narrated to me, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sacrificial meat beyond three days. Qatadah ibn al-Numan, brother of Abu Said by his mother, arrived, so they offered him dried sacrificial meat. He said: As if this is dried sacrificial meat. They said: Yes. He said: Did not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid it. Abu Said said to him: Did a matter occur in it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade keeping it beyond three days, then permitted us to eat and store."
"11195","Yahya narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ishaq, he said: Zaynab narrated to me, from Abu Said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sanctified what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah, its trees cut or beaten."
"11196","Yahya narrated to us, from Unays ibn Abi Yahya, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Said say: Two men disputed, a man from Bani Khudrah and a man from Bani Amr ibn Awf, about the mosque founded on piety. The Khudri said: It is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Umari said: It is the mosque of Quba. So they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that. He said: It is this mosque, for the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And he said concerning that: In it is much good, meaning the mosque of Quba."
"11197","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, Qatadah informed us, from Dawud al-Sarraj, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"11198","Yahya narrated to us, from al-Muthanna, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Isa al-Uswari, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Visit the sick and walk with funerals, they remind you of the Hereafter."
"11199","Yahya narrated to us, from Malik, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sasaah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Say, He is Allah, One, equals, or is equal to, a third of the Quran."
"11200","Yahya narrated to us, from Dawud, meaning Ibn Qays, from Iyad, from Abu Said: Zakat al-Fitr continued to be given in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a sa of dates, barley, aqit, or raisins."
"11201","Yahya narrated to us from Saad ibn Ishaq who said: Zaynab bint Kaab ibn Ujrah narrated to me from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: A man said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What do you think of these sicknesses that afflict us, what do we have through them? He said: Expiations. My father said: Even if little? He said: Even a thorn and what is above it. He said: Then my father supplicated upon himself that fever never leave him until he dies, without preventing him from hajj nor umrah nor jihad in the path of Allah nor prescribed prayer in congregation. So no person touched him except he felt his heat, until he died."
"11202","Yahya narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Saeed from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Throne shook for the death of Saad ibn Muadh."
"11203","Yahya narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan who said: Iyad ibn Abdillah narrated to me from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like palm stalks, to hold them in his hand. One day he entered the mosque with one of them in his hand, and he saw sputum in the qibla of the mosque, so he scraped them off with it until he cleaned them. Then he turned to the people angry and said: Does any of you like that a man face him and spit in his face? When one of you stands for prayer, he is only facing his Lord, Almighty and Majestic, and the angel is on his right, so let him not spit in front of him nor on his right, but let him spit under his left foot or on his left. If something hasty overtakes him, let him do like this, and he folded one part over another. And Yahya spat into his garment and rubbed it."
"11204","Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he said: We were discussing Laylat al-Qadr, and some people said it rotates through the year. So we walked to Abu Saeed al-Khudri. I said: O Abu Saeed, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention Laylat al-Qadr? He said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) observed iatikaf in the middle ten of Ramadan, and we observed iatikaf with him. When morning came on the morning of the twentieth, he returned and we returned with him, and he had been shown Laylat al-Qadr then was made to forget it. He said: I was shown Laylat al-Qadr then I was made to forget it, and I see myself prostrating in water and mud. Whoever observed iatikaf with me, let him return to his place of iatikaf. Seek it in the last ten, in the odd nights thereof. The sky rained upon us at the end of that evening, and half the mosque was a roof of palm branches, so it leaked. By the One Who honored him and sent down the Book upon him, I saw him lead us in Maghrib prayer on the night of the twenty-first, with his forehead and the tip of his nose covered in water and mud."
"11205","Yahya narrated to us from Humayd al-Kharrat who said: I heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman say: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Saeed al-Khudri passed by me, and I said to him: How did you hear your father speak about the mosque founded on piety? He said: My father said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the house of one of his wives, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the two mosques is the one founded on piety? He took a handful of pebbles and struck the ground with it. He said: It is this, the mosque of Madinah. He said: I said to him: Do you bear witness that you heard your father mention it like this?"
"11206","Yahya narrated to us from Usamah who said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to me from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whatever befalls the Muslim of sickness, fatigue, or grief, even the worry that worries him, Allah, Almighty and Majestic, only expiates thereby some of his sins."
"11207","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, he said: Saeed ibn Khalid narrated to me from Abu Salamah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a fly falls into the food of one of you, then immerse it."
"11208","Yahya narrated to us, Hisham and Shuabah narrated to us, they said: Qatadah narrated to us from Abu Nadrah from Abu Saeed from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When they are three, let one of them lead them, and the most entitled of them to lead is the most reciting among them."
"11209","Yahya narrated to us from Shuabah, Qatadah narrated to us from Abu Nadrah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Hunayn when seventeen or eighteen days of Ramadan had passed. Some fasted and others broke fast, and neither blamed the others nor did these blame those."
"11210","Yahya narrated to us from Shuabah, Qatadah narrated to us from Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There will be rulers over whom gather crowds of people. They oppress and lie. Whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lies and aids them in their oppression is not from me and I am not from him. Whoever does not enter upon them nor believe them in their lies nor aid them in their oppression is from me and I am from him."
"11211","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Ibn Said about the soil of Paradise. He said: Fine white flour, musk. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth."
"11212","May Allah have mercy on him. Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Saeed al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Ibn Said about the soil of Paradise. He said: Fine white flour, musk. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth."
"11213","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us from Hisham, Yahya narrated to us from Abu Salamah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you see the funeral, stand for it. Whoever follows it, let him not sit until it is placed down."
"11214","Yahya narrated to us from Awf, Abu Nadrah narrated to us from Abu Saeed who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah will split into two factions, and a renegade group will break away between them. The party closer to the truth will kill them."
"11215","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan, Iyad narrated to us from Abu Saeed who said: A man entered the mosque on Friday while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the minbar, so he called him and ordered him to pray two rakahs. Then he entered on the second Friday while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on the minbar, so he called him and ordered him. Then he entered on the third Friday, and he ordered him to pray two rakahs. Then he said: Give charity. So they did, and he gave him two garments from what they gave in charity. Then he said: Give charity. So he threw one of his two garments. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked him and disliked what he did. Then he said: Look at this. He entered the mosque in shabby dress, so I called him, hoping you would give to him and give charity to him and clothe him, but you did not. So I said: Give charity, and you gave charity, and I gave him two garments from what you gave in charity. Then I said: Give charity, and he threw one of his two garments. Take your garment. And he rebuked him."
"11216","Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, Saeed ibn Abi Saeed narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Saeed from his father who said: We were held back on the day of the Trench from prayers until well after Maghrib, and that was before what was revealed about fighting was revealed. When we were spared the fighting, and that is His saying: And Allah spared the believers from fighting, and Allah is Strong, Mighty, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Bilal, so he called the iqamah for Dhuhr and prayed it as he prays it in its time. Then he called the iqamah for Asr and prayed it as he prays it in its time. Then he called the iqamah for Maghrib and prayed it as he prays it in its time."
"11217","Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us from Ibn Abi Dhib, and he mentioned it with its isnad and meaning, and added in it, he said: And that was before the fear prayer was revealed: on foot or mounted."
"11218","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to me from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: People will be displayed over the bridge of Hell, and upon it are thorns, hooks, and grapples that snatch people. He said: People will pass like lightning, others like wind, others like a swift horse, others running, others walking, others crawling on hands and knees, others creeping. As for the people of the Fire, they neither die nor live. As for some people, they will be seized for their sins and burned, becoming coal. Then Allah will permit intercession, and they will be found in bundles, and thrown onto a river, and they will sprout as a seed sprouts in the flood debris. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you seen al-Sabgha? He said: And over the Fire are three trees. A man will come out of the Fire and be at its edge, and say: My Lord, turn my face away from it. He will say: By your covenant and your pledge, you will not ask Me for other than it. He will see a tree and say: My Lord, bring me near this tree, to shade in its shade and eat from its fruit. He will say: By your covenant and your pledge, you will not ask Me for other than it. He will see another tree better than it and say: My Lord, move me to this tree, to shade in its shade and eat from its fruit. He will say: By your covenant and your pledge, you will not ask Me for other than it. He will see the third and say: My Lord, move me to this tree, to shade in its shade and eat from its fruit. He will say: By your covenant and your pledge, you will not ask Me for other than it. Then he will see the darkness of people and hear their voices, and say: My Lord, admit me to Paradise. He said: Abu Saeed and another man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) differed. One of them said: He will enter Paradise and be given the world and its like with it. The other said: He will be admitted to Paradise and given the world and ten times its like."
"11219","Rawh narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: People pass over the bridge of Hell, and he mentioned it. He said: On its sides are angels saying: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you seen al-Sabgha, a tree growing in rubbish? And he said: As for the people of the Fire who are its people, and he mentioned its meaning."
"11220","Muhammad ibn Jaafar narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, and he dictated it to me, he said: I heard Abu Nadrah narrating from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned intercession and said: People will be displayed over the bridge of Hell, and upon it are thorns and hooks that snatch people, and on its sides are angels saying: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. And he mentioned the hadith."
"11221","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us from Malik, Ayyub ibn Habib narrated to me from Abu al-Muthanna who said: I was with Marwan, and Abu Saeed entered. He said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid blowing into drink? He said: Yes. A man said: I am not quenched in one breath. He said: Remove it from you, then breathe. He said: I see a speck in it. He said: Pour it out."
"11222","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us from Mujalid who said: Abu al-Waddak narrated to me from Abu Saeed from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about withdrawal: Do what seems to you, for if Allah decrees something, it will be."
"11223","Yahya narrated to us from Mujalid, Abu al-Waddak narrated to me from Abu Saeed who said: We said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when wine was prohibited: We have wine belonging to an orphan of ours. So he ordered us and we poured it out."
"11224","Yahya narrated to us from Mujalid who said: Abu al-Waddak narrated to me from Abu Saeed from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The people of the highest ranks will be seen by those below them as you see the brilliant star in the horizon of the sky. Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and blessed be they both."
"11225","Yahya narrated to us from Shuabah from al-Hakam from Abu Salih Dhakwan al-Samman from Abu Saeed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the house of a man from the Ansar, and he came out with his head dripping. He said: Perhaps we hurried you. He said: When you are hurried or interrupted, then no ghusl is upon you."
"11226","Yahya narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya who said: My father narrated to me that Abu Saeed al-Khudri narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the day of Hudaybiyah, said: Do not light a fire at night. He said: After that, he said: Light fires and prepare food, for no people after you will attain your saa nor your mudd."
"11227","Yahya narrated to us, al-Taymi narrated to me from Abu Nadrah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: Ibn Said met me and said: Count the people saying, or I think the people saying, and you, O companions of Muhammad, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is Jewish and I am Muslim, he is one-eyed and I am sound, he does not come to Makkah nor Madinah though I have performed hajj, and I am now with you in Madinah, and no child is born to him though a child was born to me. Then he said: Yet I know where he was born, when he will emerge, and where he is. He said: So he confused me."
"11228","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Sumayy from al-Numan ibn Abi Ayyash al-Zuraqi from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant fasts a day in the path of Allah except Allah distances the Fire from his face by that day seventy autumns."
"11229","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Abi Sulayman, narrated to us from Atiyyah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have left among you the two weighty things, one of them greater than the other: the Book of Allah, Almighty and Majestic, a rope extended from heaven to earth, and my progeny, my household. They will not separate until they come to me at the Hawd."
"11230","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Musa, meaning al-Juhani, narrated to us, he said: I heard Zayd al-Ammi say: Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Saeed al-Khudri say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Mahdi will be from my ummah. Whether his life is long or short, he will live seven years, eight years, or nine years. He will fill the earth with equity and justice, the earth will bring forth its vegetation, and the sky will rain its rain."
"11231","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Aamash narrated to us, Atiyyah ibn Saad narrated to us at the door of this mosque, he said: I heard Abu Saeed al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the highest ranks will be seen by those beneath them as you see the rising star in the horizon of the sky. Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and blessed be they both."
"11232","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah informed us from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mamar al-Ansari from Nahar from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One of you will be asked on the Day of Resurrection, until among what he is asked about it will be said: What prevented you from denouncing evil when you saw it? He said: Whoever Allah inspires with his proof says: My Lord, I hoped in You and feared people."
"11233","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah informed us from Sayfi from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: A man found a snake in his house, took his spear and pierced it with it. The snake did not die until the man died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed of it and said: With you are dwellers. If you see any of them, warn it three times. If you see it after that, then kill it."
"11234","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from al-Numan ibn Abi al-Ayyash from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in rank is a man whose face Allah turns away from the Fire toward Paradise, and a tree with shade is shown to him. He says: My Lord, bring me forward to this tree, to be in its shade. Allah says: Perhaps if I do, you will ask Me for other than it. He says: No, by Your might. So Allah brings him forward to it, and a tree with shade and fruit is shown to him. He says: My Lord, bring me forward to this tree, to be in its shade and eat from its fruit. Allah says to him: Perhaps if I give you that, you will ask Me for other than it. He says: No, by Your might. So Allah brings him forward to it. Another tree with shade, fruit, and water is shown to him. He says: My Lord, bring me forward to this tree, to be in its shade, eat from its fruit, and drink from its water. He says to him: Perhaps if I do, you will ask Me for other than it. He says: No, by Your might, I will not ask You for other than it. So Allah brings him forward to it. The gate of Paradise appears to him. He says: My Lord, bring me forward to the gate of Paradise, to be under the lintel of Paradise and look at its people. So Allah brings him forward to it. He sees the people of Paradise and what is in it. He says: My Lord, admit me to Paradise. He said: So Allah admits him to Paradise. He said: When he enters Paradise, he says: This is mine. Allah, Almighty and Majestic, says to him: Wish. So he wishes, and Allah reminds him: Ask for such and such, until his wishes run out. Allah, Almighty and Majestic, says: It is yours and ten times its like. He said: Then he enters Paradise, and his two wives from the houris enter upon him and say to him: Praise be to Allah Who gave you life for us and gave us life for you. He says: No one was given like what I was given. He said: And the least of the people of the Fire in punishment is shod with two sandals of fire, and his brain boils from the heat of his sandals."
"11235","Suwayd ibn Amr al-Kalbi narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us from Abdillah ibn Abi Utbah from Abu Saeed who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The House will surely be hajjed and umrahed after the emergence of Yajuj and Majuj."
"11236","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us from Amr ibn Yahya al-Ansari, and Abu Salamah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us from Amr ibn Yahya from Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Abdillah ibn Salam from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever comes to a funeral and walks with its family until prayer is offered over it, he has one qirat. Whoever waits until it is buried or finished with, he has two qirats, like Uhud."
"11237","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Imran informed us from Qatadah from Abdillah ibn Abi Utbah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: This House will surely be hajjed and umrahed after the emergence of Yajuj and Majuj."
"11238","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Dinar narrated to us from Abu Hazim from al-Numan ibn Abi Ayyash al-Zuraqi from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I will say: My companions, my companions. It will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you. He said: So I will say: Away, away, or he said: Crushing, crushing, for whoever changed after me."
"11239","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Shuabah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Abu Hisham from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ammar: The rebellious party will kill you."
"11240","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muslim, narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us from Mujahid from Abu Saeed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one who reminds of favors, nor disobedient to parents, nor alcoholic will enter Paradise."
"11241","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Matar and al-Mualla informed us from Abu al-Siddiq from Abu Saeed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The earth will be filled with injustice and tyranny. Then a man from my progeny will emerge, ruling seven or nine years, filling the earth with equity and justice."
"11242","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father and Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to me from Abdillah al-Bahi from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers over you in whom hearts find tranquility and for whom skins soften. Then there will be rulers over you from whom hearts recoil and from whom skins shudder. A man said: Shall we fight them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: No, as long as they establish prayer."
"11243","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Suhayb, narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to me from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Are you ill, O Muhammad? He said: Yes. He said: In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah upon you, from everything that harms you, from the evil of every soul and eye. May He heal you. In the name of Allah I perform ruqyah upon you."
"11244","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubaydullah informed us from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to break fast on the day of Fitr before going out, and he would not pray before the prayer. When he finished his prayer, he prayed two rakahs."
"11245","Muhadir ibn al-Muwarra narrated to us, Asim ibn Sulayman narrated to us from Abu al-Mutawakkil from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you comes to his wife then wants to return, let him perform wudu as his wudu for prayer."
"11246","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Qays ibn Wahb and Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Waddak from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about the captives of Awtas: He shall not have intercourse with a pregnant woman until she delivers, nor with a non-pregnant woman until she menstruates one menstruation."
"11247","Harun narrated to us, and I heard from Harun, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj from Ubaydah ibn Musafi from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was distributing something, a man came and pressed upon him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck him with a palm stalk he had with him, wounding his face. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Come and take retaliation. He said: I have pardoned, O Messenger of Allah."
"11248","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us from Abu al-Haytham from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If one of you were to work in a solid rock with no door and no opening, his deed would emerge to people, whatever it is."
"11249","From the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If a bucket of ghassaq were poured out into the world, the people of the world would stink."
"11250","And from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Dust eats everything of man except the tailbone. It was said: And what is it like, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Like a mustard seed. From it you will grow."
"11251","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father and Affan narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to me from Abdillah al-Bahi from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers for whom skins soften and in whom hearts find tranquility. And there will be rulers over you from whom hearts recoil and from whom skins shudder. They said: Shall we not kill them? He said: No, as long as they establish prayer."
"11252","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us from Abu al-Haytham from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The seat of the disbeliever in the Fire is a journey of three days. Every molar is like Uhud, his thigh is like Warqan, and his skin apart from his flesh and bones is forty cubits."
"11253","And from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If an iron mace were placed on the earth, and the two weighty beings gathered for it, they could not lift it from the earth."
"11254","And from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The enclosure of the Fire has four walls, the thickness of each wall like a journey of forty years."
"11255","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Boasting of intercourse is unlawful. Ibn Lahiah said: He means one who boasts of intercourse."
"11256","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise has one hundred degrees. If all the worlds gathered in one of them, it would contain them."
"11257","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan said: By Your might, my Lord, I will not cease misleading Your servants while their souls are in their bodies. The Lord said: By My might and majesty, I will not cease forgiving them while they seek My forgiveness."
"11258","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, even two goats will dispute about butting."
"11259","And from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: What is between two door leaves in Paradise is like a journey of forty years."
"11260","He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most truthful of dreams are at dawn."
"11261","And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If people knew what is in the call to prayer, they would fight over it with swords."
"11262","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us from Saeed ibn Abd al-Aziz from Atiyyah ibn Qays from Qazaah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached Marr al-Zahran in the year of the Conquest, he informed us of meeting the enemy, and ordered us to break fast, so we all broke fast."
"11263","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me from Ibn Shihab from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who narrated to him from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Water is from water."
"11264","Abu Salamah narrated to us, Layth informed us from Yazid ibn al-Had from Amr from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Iblis said to his Lord: By Your might and majesty, I will not cease misleading the children of Adam while souls are in them. Allah said: By My might and majesty, I will not cease forgiving them while they seek My forgiveness."
"11265","Abu Salamah narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal informed us from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Nahar al-Abdi that he heard him narrating from Abu Saeed that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will ask the servant on the Day of Resurrection, until He says: What prevented you, when you saw evil, from denouncing it? When Allah inspires a servant with his proof, he says: My Lord, I trusted in You and feared people."
"11266","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Abu al-Numan Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Numan al-Ansari narrated to us from Abu Saeed, freedman of al-Mahri, who said: My brother died, and I came to Abu Saeed al-Khudri and said: O Abu Saeed, my brother died leaving dependents, and I have dependents, and we have no wealth. I want to go out with my dependents and my brother's dependents until we settle in one of these cities, which would be easier for us in livelihood. He said: Woe to you, do not go out, for I heard him say, meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever endures its hardship and severity, I will be an intercessor or witness for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"11267","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to me from Bishr ibn Harb that Ibn Umar came to Abu Saeed al-Khudri and said: O Abu Saeed, was I not informed that you pledged to two leaders before people united upon one leader? He said: Yes. I pledged to Ibn al-Zubayr, then the people of Sham came and drove me to the army of Ibn Dalahah, and I pledged to him. Ibn Umar said: It is what I feared, it is what I feared, and Hammad raised his voice with it. Abu Saeed said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you not hear that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is able not to sleep a night, nor wake in a morning, nor enter an evening except with a leader over him. He said: Yes, but I dislike pledging two leaders before people unite upon one leader."
"11268","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us from Saeed ibn Iyas al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a new garment, he named it by its name, shirt or turban, then said: O Allah, praise is Yours. You clothed me with it. I ask You for its good and the good of what it was made for, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what it was made for."
"11269","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Lahiah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Saeed ibn Suwayd al-Saidi from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril led me in prayer. He prayed Dhuhr when the sun declined, prayed Asr when the shadow was a cubit, prayed Maghrib when the sun set, prayed Isha when the twilight disappeared, and prayed Fajr when dawn broke. Then he came to him the next day and prayed Dhuhr when the shadow of everything was its like, prayed Asr when the shadow was two cubits, prayed Maghrib when the sun set, prayed Isha until the first third of the night, and prayed Subh when the sun was about to rise. Then he said: Prayer is between these two times."
"11270","Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed us from Bukayr from Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Saeed al-Khudri from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghusl on Friday is upon every adult, and siwak, and he touches of perfume what he can, even from the perfume of his wife."
"11271","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Bishr ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Saeed al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, yet you do it. He said: I am not like any of you. I am fed and given drink."
"11272","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us from Rubayh ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Saeed al-Khudri from his father from his grandfather who said: We used to take turns with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), spending the night with him in case he had a need or a night matter came to him and he would send us. Those seeking reward and those on turn grew many, and we were talking. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us at night and said: What is this private talk? Did I not forbid you from private talk? He said: We said: We repent to Allah, O Prophet of Allah. We were only mentioning the Messiah, fearing him. He said: Shall I not inform you of what I fear for you more than the Messiah in my view? He said: We said: Yes. He said: Hidden shirk, that a man stands working for the sake of another man."
"11273","Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abdillah, meaning al-Umari, narrated to us from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from Abu Saeed who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sadaqah in less than five camels, no sadaqah in less than five ounces, and no sadaqah in less than five wasqs."
"11274","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari from his father that he heard Abu Saeed al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Soon the best wealth of the Muslim will be sheep, following mountain peaks and places of rain, fleeing with his religion from trials."
"11275","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-Aamash informed us from Amr ibn Murrah from Abu al-Bakhtari from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you belittle himself, to see a matter of Allah upon which there is a word, then not speak it. Allah will say: What prevented you from speaking about it? He will say: My Lord, I feared people. He will say: I am more deserving to be feared."
"11276","Yaala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower garment of the believer is to mid-shin. What is to the ankle, there is no harm. What is below the ankle is in the Fire."
"11277","Abu Usamah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Kathir narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Kaab from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah, and Abu Usamah once said: From Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi ibn Khadij, from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we perform wudu from the well of Budaah, a well into which menstruation cloths, filth, and dog meat are thrown? He said: Water is pure. Nothing makes it impure."
"11278","Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Fitr narrated to me from Ismail ibn Raja from his father from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Among you is one who will fight for the interpretation of the Quran as he fought for its revelation."
"11279","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, al-Aamash narrated to us from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wealthy have perished. They said: Except whom? He said: The wealthy have perished. They said: Except whom? He said: The wealthy have perished. They said: Except whom? Until we feared it had become binding. He said: Except one who says like this and like this and like this, and how few they are."
"11280","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us from Abu al-Waddak from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the fetus in the belly of a she-camel, cow, or sheep. He said: Eat it if you wish, for its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother."
"11281","Ammar ibn Muhammad ibn Ukht Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us from al-Aamash from Abu Salih from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until you fight a people with small eyes, broad faces, as if their eyes are locust pupils, as if their faces are hammered shields. They wear hair footwear and take shields, until they tie their horses to palm trees."
"11282","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from Ibn Abi Saeed al-Khudri from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can, for Satan enters his mouth."
"11283","Waki narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us from Iyad ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Sarh from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed standing on his feet."
"11284","Waki narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us from his father from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sleeps past witr or forgets it, let him pray witr when he remembers or wakes."
"11285","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Amr ibn Yahya from his father from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not give preference among the prophets."
"11286","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The day when some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith. He said: The rising of the sun from its west."
"11287","Waki narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Saeed ibn Masruq from Ibn Abi Num from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: Those whose hearts were reconciled in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were four: Alqamah ibn Ulathah al-Jafari, al-Aqra ibn Habis al-Hanzali, Zayd al-Khayl al-Tai, and Uyaynah ibn Badr al-Fazari. He said: Ali came with gold from Yemen with its soil, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it among them."
"11288","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from Atiyyah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sadaqah is not lawful for a rich man except for three: in the path of Allah, the wayfarer, and a man who had a neighbor to whom charity was given and he gifted to him."
"11289","Waki narrated to us, Shuabah narrated to us, Khulayd ibn Jaafar narrated to us from Abu Nadrah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: Musk was mentioned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: It is the best of perfume."
"11290","Waki narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu Isa al-Uswari from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit the sick and follow funerals. They remind you of the Hereafter."
"11291","Waki narrated to us, al-Aamash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Saeed al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The middle is the just: We made you a middle nation."
"11292","Waki narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: You are to me as Harun was to Musa, except there is no prophet after me."
"11293","Waki narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Ibn Abi Num from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a pilgrim in ihram killing a snake, and he said: There is no harm in it."
"11294","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Jabir from Muhammad ibn Qarazah from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: I bought a ram to sacrifice, and a wolf attacked and took its tail. He said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Sacrifice it."
"11295","Waki narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A renegade group will break away at a division among the Muslims. The party closer to the truth will kill them."
"11296","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Hashim al-Rummani narrated to us from Ismail ibn Riyah ibn Ubaydah from his father or from another than him, from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he finished his food, said: Praise be to Allah Who fed us, gave us drink, and made us Muslims."
"11297","Waki narrated to us, Misar narrated to us from Zayd al-Ammi from Abu al-Siddiq from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a man, Misar said: I think about drink, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck him with two sandals forty times."
"11298","Waki narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu Isa al-Uswari from Abu Saeed al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man drink standing."
"11299","Waki narrated to us from Malik ibn Anas from Ayyub ibn Habib, freedman of Banu Zuhrah, from Abu al-Muthanna al-Juhani who said: I was sitting with Marwan ibn al-Hakam, and Abu Saeed al-Khudri entered. Marwan said to him: Did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid blowing into drink? He said: Yes. He said: A man said to him: I am not quenched in one breath. He said: Remove it from your mouth, then breathe. He said: If I see a speck? He said: Pour it out."
"11300","Al-Muttalib ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Saeed al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not thank people has not thanked Allah."
"11301","Al-Muttalib narrated to us from Ibn Abi Layla from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"11302","Waki' narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Rafi' from Muhammad ibn Yahya from his uncle Wasi' ibn Habban from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man is most entitled to the front of his riding animal, and most entitled to his seat when he returns."
"11303","Waki' narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nuh, peace be upon him, will be called on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said to him: Did you convey? So he will say: Yes. Then his people will be called and it will be said to them: Did he convey to you? So they will say: No warner came to us, or: No one came to us. He said: Then it will be said to Nuh: Who will testify for you? So he will say: Muhammad and his nation. He said: So that is His saying: And thus We made you a middle nation. He said: Middle means just. He said: Then they will be called and they will testify for him that he conveyed. He said: Then I will testify over you."
"11304","Waki' narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Exalted and Majestic, will say on the Day of Resurrection: O Adam, rise and send forth the contingent of the Fire. So he will say: At Your service and with Your help, and all good is in Your hands, my Lord, and what is the contingent of the Fire? He will say: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine. He said: Then at that time the newborn will turn grey, and every pregnant female will lay down her burden, and you will see the people drunk though they are not drunk, but the punishment of Allah is severe. He said: So they will say: Then which of us is that one? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nine hundred and ninety-nine from Ya'juj and Ma'juj, and one from among you. He said: So the people said: Allah is Most Great. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will you not be pleased to be one quarter of the people of Paradise? By Allah, I hope you will be one quarter of the people of Paradise. By Allah, I hope you will be one third of the people of Paradise. By Allah, I hope you will be one half of the people of Paradise. He said: So the people magnified Allah. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You on that day among mankind are but like a white hair on a black bull, or like a black hair on a white bull."
"11305","Waki' narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us from Asim ibn Shumaykh from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore and strove in his oath, he said: No, by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim, people from my nation will surely come forth, you will deem your deeds insignificant beside their deeds; they will recite the Quran and it will not pass their collarbones; they will shoot out of Islam as the arrow shoots out of the target. They said: Then is there a mark by which they are known? He said: Among them is a man with a small arm, or a small breast, with shaven heads. Abu Sa'id said: Then twenty or some twenty of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me that Ali, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, undertook their killing. He said: Then I saw Abu Sa'id after he had grown old, with his hands trembling, saying: Fighting them is more lawful to me than fighting an equal number of the Turks."
"11306","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Amr ibn Yahya from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prefer some prophets over others. And I am the first over whom the earth will split on the Day of Resurrection, then I will recover and find Musa clinging to a leg of the legs of the Throne, and I will not know whether he was recompensed for the swoon of the Mount or recovered before me."
"11307","Waki' narrated to us from Isra'il from Abu Ishaq from al-Agharr Abu Muslim who said: I testify regarding Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayrah that they both testified regarding the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said, and I testify regarding them both: No people sit remembering Allah Almighty except that the angels surround them, and tranquility descends upon them, and mercy covers them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."
"11308","Waki' narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to me from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban from Abu Muti' ibn Rifa'ah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Jews said: Coitus interruptus is the minor live burial. My father said: And in our book it was Abu Rifa'ah ibn Muti', so Waki' changed it and said: from Abu Muti' ibn Rifa'ah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews have lied. If Allah wanted to create a thing, no one could turn it away."
"11309","Waki' narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us from Isma'il ibn Raja from his father from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among you is one who will fight for its interpretation as I fought for its revelation. He said: So Abu Bakr and Umar stood up, so he said: No, but the mender of the sandal, and Ali is mending his sandal."
"11310","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us from Ubaydullah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Mu'ayqib from Amr ibn Sulaym. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And other than Yazid ibn Harun said: from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Utwari, and he is Abu al-Haytham, and he was in the care of Abu Sa'id, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and from Abu al-Zinad from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah, they both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I take with You a covenant which You will not break for me, for I am only a human; so whichever of the believers I have harmed or insulted, or he said: cursed, or flogged, then make it for him a prayer and a purification and a nearness by which You bring him near to You on the Day of Resurrection."
"11311","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us from Abu Salamah, he said: A man came to Abu Sa'id and said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention anything about the Haruriyyah? He said: I heard him mention a people who go deep in religion; one of you will deem his prayer insignificant beside their prayer and his fasting beside their fasting; they will shoot out of religion as the arrow shoots out of the target; he took his arrow and looked at its head and saw nothing, then looked at its binding and saw nothing, then looked at its shaft and saw nothing, then looked at the feathers and doubted whether he saw anything or not."
"11312","Yazid narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab informed us from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw lagging among his companions, so he said: Move forward and follow me, and let those after you follow you. People will keep lagging until Allah, Exalted and Majestic, puts them behind on the Day of Resurrection."
"11313","Yazid narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab informed us from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at a man turning his mount about among the people, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has an extra mount, let him give it to one who has no mount, and whoever has extra provision, let him give it to one who has no provision, until we thought that none of us had any right to any surplus."
"11314","He said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Affan narrated to us, they both said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr from Qaza'ah, he said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) four things, and they pleased me and delighted me; Affan said: and pleased me. He forbade a woman to travel a journey of two days, Affan said: or two nights, except with her husband or a mahram, and he forbade prayer at two times: after dawn until the sun rises, and after Asr until it sets, and he forbade fasting two days: the day of sacrifice and the day of breaking fast, and he said: Mounts are not tied except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the Aqsa Mosque, and this mosque of mine. Affan said in his hadith: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr said: He informed me, he said: I heard Qaza'ah, the freedman of Ziyad."
"11315","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from al-Agharr who said: I testify regarding Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that they both testified regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Allah, Exalted and Majestic, grants respite until a third of the night has gone, then He descends and says: Is there any asker? Is there any repentant? Is there any seeker of forgiveness? Is there any sinner? He said: Then a man said to him: Until dawn breaks? He said: Yes."
"11316","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani from Dhakwan from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the women said: The men have dominated over you against us, O Messenger of Allah, so appoint for us a day, O Messenger of Allah, in which we may come to you. So he appointed for them an appointment, then he commanded them and admonished them and said: There is no woman among you whose three children die except that they will be for her a veil from the Fire. So a woman said: Or two? For two of mine have died. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or two."
"11317","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Ibn al-Waddak, and Hajjaj said: from Abu al-Waddak, saying: I will not drink nabidh after I heard Abu Sa'id say: A drunken man was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: I did not drink wine; I only drank raisins and dates in a gourd. He said: So he ordered him to be struck, and he was pushed with hands and struck with sandals. And he forbade gourds, and he forbade raisins and dates, meaning that they be mixed together."
"11318","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, and he was asked about three who gather and prayer comes upon them. He said: Sa'id narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three gather, let one of them lead them, and the most entitled of them to lead is the most reciting of them."
"11319","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is praying, let him not leave anyone to pass in front of him, and let him repel him as much as he can; then if he refuses, let him fight him, for he is only a devil."
"11320","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No man who believes in Allah and His Messenger hates the Ansar."
"11321","Abu Amir narrated to us, Ali, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us from Yahya, he said: Abu Sa'id, the freedman of al-Mahri, narrated to me from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition to Lihyan ibn Hudhayl. He said: Let one of every two men go forth, and the reward is between them both. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless for us our mudd and our sa', and make the blessing two blessings."
"11322","Abu Amir narrated to us, Ali narrated to us from Yahya, Abu Nadrah narrated to us that Abu Sa'id informed them that they asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about witr, so he said: Pray witr before dawn."
"11323","Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Khulayd ibn Ja'far narrated to us from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): For every traitor there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he will be known at his buttocks."
"11324","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us from Abu Sinan from Abu Salih al-Hanafi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has chosen four from speech: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great. So whoever says: Glory be to Allah, twenty good deeds will be written for him and twenty evil deeds will be dropped from him. And whoever says: Allah is Most Great, the like of that. And whoever says: There is no god but Allah, the like of that. And whoever says: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, of his own accord, thirty good deeds will be written for him, and thirty evil deeds will be dropped from him thereby."
"11325","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah al-Mazini from his father that he informed him that Abu Sa'id said to him: I see that you love sheep and the desert; so when you are among your sheep or in your desert and you call the adhan for prayer, then raise your voice with the call, for no jinn nor man nor anything hears the extent of the voice of the caller except that it will testify for him on the Day of Resurrection. I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11326","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that a man heard a man reciting: Say, He is Allah, One, repeating it before dawn. So when morning came, he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and the man deemed it little. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, it surely equals a third of the Quran."
"11327","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to me from Rabi'ah ibn Yazid, he said: Qaza'ah narrated to me, he said: I came to Abu Sa'id while he was crowded upon. So when the people dispersed from him, I said: I will not ask you about what these ask you about. I said: I ask you about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: You have no good in that. Then he repeated it to him, so he said: The noon prayer would be established, then one of us would go out to al-Baqi', relieve himself, then come to his family, perform ablution, then return to the mosque, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the first rak'ah. He said: And I asked him about zakat, so he said: I do not know whether he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or not. On two hundred dirhams there are five dirhams, and on forty sheep there is a sheep up to one hundred and twenty; then if one more is added, in it are two sheep up to two hundred; then if it increases, in it are three sheep up to three hundred; then if it increases, in every hundred there is a sheep. And on camels: on five there is a sheep, and on ten there are two sheep, and on fifteen there are three sheep, and on twenty there are four sheep, and on twenty-five there is a she-camel in her second year up to thirty-five; then if one more is added, in it is a she-camel in her third year up to forty-five; then if one more is added, in it is a she-camel in her fourth year up to sixty; then if one more is added, in it is a she-camel in her fifth year up to seventy-five; then if one more is added, in it are two she-camels in their third year up to ninety; then if one more is added, in it are two she-camels in their fourth year up to one hundred and twenty; then if it increases, in every fifty there is a she-camel in her fourth year, and in every forty there is a she-camel in her third year. And I asked him about fasting while traveling. He said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Makkah while we were fasting. He said: So we stopped at a halt, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have drawn near your enemy, and breaking fast is stronger for you. So it was a concession. So some of us fasted and some of us broke fast. Then we stopped at another halt, so he said: You will meet your enemy in the morning, and breaking fast is stronger for you, so break fast. So it was a binding order, so we broke fast. Then he said: I have seen us fast with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after that while traveling."
"11328","He said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us from Sharik from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Water is from water."
"11329","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of sitting in the roads. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we must have our sittings in which we talk. He said: Then if you refuse except the sitting, then give the road its right. They said: O Messenger of Allah, then what is the right of the road? He said: Lowering the gaze, withholding harm, returning the greeting, and enjoining the good and forbidding the evil."
"11330","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Hilal ibn Iyad, he said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Two men should not go out to relieve themselves, uncovering their private parts, talking to each other, for Allah detests that."
"11331","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyan narrated to us from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best perfume is musk."
"11332","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Fudayl narrated to us from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Duha until we would say: He does not leave it, and he would leave it until we would say: He does not pray it."
"11333","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Awf narrated to us from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until the earth is filled with injustice and aggression. He said: Then a man from my progeny, or from my household, will come forth and fill it with equity and justice as it was filled with injustice and aggression."
"11334","Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us from Qatadah from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three gather, let one of them lead them, and the most entitled of them to lead is the most reciting of them."
"11335","Abu Amir narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us from Iyad ibn Abdullah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out on the day of Eid at the breaking of fast and pray with the people those two rak'ahs, then he would step forward and face the people while they were sitting and say: Give charity, give charity, give charity, three times. He said: So the most of what the people gave in charity were women, with earrings and rings and things. Then if he had a need for an expedition, he would mention it, and if he had none, he would leave."
"11336","Abdullah ibn al-Harith narrated it to us, he said: Dawud narrated to me, then he mentioned it. He said: And if he wanted to send an expedition against the people, he would mention it, otherwise he would leave."
"11337","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj from Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Sa'd from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: A man was afflicted in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding fruits he had bought, and his debt became great. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity to him. He said: So the people gave charity to him, but that did not reach the payment of his debt. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take what you find, and you have nothing but that."
"11338","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from al-Zuhri, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed me that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us a long hadith about the Dajjal. So he said in what he narrated to us, he said: The Dajjal will come, while it is forbidden for him to enter the passes of Madinah. Then a man will go out to him on that day, and he is the best of people, or among the best of them. So he will say: I testify that you are the Dajjal of whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us his hadith. So the Dajjal will say: What do you think, if I kill this man then bring him to life, will you doubt the matter? So they will say: No. So he will kill him, then bring him to life. So he will say when he comes to life: By Allah, I have never been more clear-sighted about you than I am now. He said: So he will want to kill him a second time, but he will not be given power over him."
"11339","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me from Abu al-Khayr from Abu al-Khattab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of Tabuk addressed the people while leaning his back against a palm tree. So he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people and the worst of people? Among the best of people is a man who strives in the path of Allah on the back of his horse, or on the back of his camel, or on his feet, until death comes to him. And among the worst of people is a dissolute, audacious man who reads the Book of Allah but does not respond to anything of it."
"11340","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Hilal ibn Iyad informed me that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Satan confuses one of you while he is in his prayer and says: You have broken wind, then let him say to himself: You have lied, until he hears a sound with his ears or finds a smell with his nose. And when one of you prays and does not know whether he added or decreased, then let him prostrate two prostrations while he is sitting."
"11341","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Hisham from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Iyad that he asked Abu Sa'id, then he mentioned it."
"11342","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah or Ata ibn Yazid, Ma'mar doubted, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are best? He said: A believing struggler with himself and his wealth in the path of Allah. He said: Then who? He said: Then a man secluded in a mountain pass among the passes, worshipping his Lord, Exalted and Majestic, and leaving the people safe from his evil."
"11343","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from Ibn Abi Sa'id from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you yawns in prayer, let him place his hand over his mouth, for Satan enters with the yawn."
"11344","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray witr before you enter morning."
"11345","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us from al-Jurayri from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days, then whatever is beyond that is charity."
"11346","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us from al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad, al-Ala ibn Bashir narrated to us from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I give you glad tidings of the Mahdi. He will be sent among my nation amid disagreement of people and earthquakes. So he will fill the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with tyranny and injustice. The dweller of heaven and the dweller of earth will be pleased with him. He will distribute wealth in handfuls. So a man said to him: What are handfuls? He said: Equally among people. He said: And Allah will fill the hearts of the nation of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with richness, and his justice will encompass them, until he will order a caller who will call out and say: Who has a need for wealth? So none of the people will stand except a man. So he will say: Come to the treasurer, meaning the storekeeper, and say to him: The Mahdi orders you to give me wealth. So he will say to him: Scoop up. Then when he has placed it in his lap and brought it out, he will regret it and say: I was the greediest soul of the nation of Muhammad; did what encompassed them fail to encompass me? He said: So he will return it, but it will not be accepted from him. So it will be said to him: We do not take anything we have given. So it will be so for seven years, or eight years, or nine years. Then there is no good in life after him, or he said: Then there is no good in living after him."
"11347","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Isra'il informed us from Abu Sinan from Abu Salih al-Hanafi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah has chosen four from speech: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Most Great. So whoever says: Glory be to Allah, twenty good deeds will be written for him and twenty evil deeds will be dropped from him. And whoever says: Allah is Most Great, then the like of that. And whoever says: There is no god but Allah, then the like of that. And whoever says: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, of his own accord, thirty good deeds will be written for him thereby, or thirty evil deeds will be dropped from him."
"11348","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you follow a funeral, do not sit until it is placed down."
"11349","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from Usamah from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from his uncle from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them, for in them there is a lesson. And I forbade you from nabidh, so drink, but I do not permit an intoxicant. And I forbade you from sacrificial meats, so eat."
"11350","al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Isra'il informed us from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you shoots or strikes, let him avoid the face of his brother."
"11351","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Isra'il informed us from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, raising it, he said: A man may speak a word intending no harm by it except to make the people laugh by it, yet he will fall because of it farther than the sky."
"11352","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Hamzah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us from al-Agharr Abu Muslim from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Then it will be called out with that: You shall live and never die, and you shall be healthy and never fall sick, and you shall be young and never grow old, and you shall enjoy bliss and never suffer. He said: They will be called with these four."
"11353","Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, Haywah and Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, they both said: Salim ibn Ghaylan al-Tujibi informed us that he heard Abu Darraj Abu al-Samh say that he heard Abu al-Haytham say that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I seek refuge with Allah from disbelief and debt. So a man said: O Messenger of Allah, is debt equated with disbelief? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes."
"11354","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Samh say: I heard Abu al-Haytham say: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ninety-nine dragons will be given power over the disbeliever in his grave, biting him until the Hour comes. If one of them breathed upon the earth, it would not grow any green."
"11355","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us from Abu Sulayman al-Laythi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The parable of the believer is like the parable of a horse on its tether; it roams then returns to its tether. And the believer errs then returns to faith."
"11356","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to me from Yazid ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: No worry nor grief nor fatigue nor illness nor harm befalls the believer except that it is expiated from him thereby."
"11357","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Salim ibn Ghaylan informed us that al-Walid ibn Qays al-Tujibi informed him that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, or from Abu al-Haytham from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Accompany only a believer, and none but a pious one should eat your food."
"11358","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, Salim ibn Ghaylan informed me that he heard Darraj Abu al-Samh narrating from Abu al-Haytham from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah is pleased with a servant, He praises him with seven kinds of good which he did not do. And when He is angry with a servant, He praises him with seven kinds of evil which he did not do."
"11359","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Dawud narrated to us from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id and Jabir, they both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: At the end of time there will be a caliph who will distribute wealth and not count it."
"11360","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah informed me, Bashir ibn Abi Amr al-Khawlani informed me that al-Walid ibn Qays narrated to him that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be successors after sixty years who will neglect prayer and follow desires, then they will meet error. Then there will be successors who will recite the Quran and it will not pass their throats. And the Quran will be read by three: a believer, a hypocrite, and a wicked one. Bashir said: So I said to al-Walid: Who are these three? So he said: The hypocrite disbelieves in it, the wicked eats by it, and the believer believes in it."
"11361","Hajjaj narrated to us, Abu Isra'il narrated to us from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found a slain man between two villages. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the distance between them to be measured. He said: And it is as if I am looking at the span of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he assigned him to the nearer of the two."
"11362","Wahb narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Yunus from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No prophet was sent nor any caliph appointed except that he had two entourages: an entourage ordering him to good and urging him to it, and an entourage ordering him to evil and urging him to it. And the protected is the one whom Allah protects."
"11363","Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us from Mujalid from Abu al-Waddak Jabr ibn Nawf from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."
"11364","Abu Ubaydah narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Sa'id that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not write from me anything except the Quran. So whoever wrote from me anything, let him erase it. And he said: Narrate from me, and whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"11365","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: You claim that my kinship will not benefit my people. By Allah, my womb is joined in this world and the Hereafter. When the Day of Resurrection comes, people will be raised for me and ordered to the left. So a man will say: O Muhammad, I am so-and-so son of so-and-so. And another will say: I am so-and-so son of so-and-so. So I will say: As for lineage, I knew it, but you innovated after me and turned back on your heels, retreating backward."
"11366","Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection."
"11367","Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When a man purifies himself and perfects purification, then comes to Friday without idle talk and without ignorant behavior until the imam leaves, it will be an expiation for what is between it and the next Friday. And in Friday there is an hour which no believing man meets asking Allah for anything except that He gives it to him. And the prescribed prayers are expiations for what is between them."
"11368","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us from Jabir from Amir from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer after dawn until the sun rises, nor after Asr until the sun sets, and no fasting on the day of breaking fast nor on the day of sacrifice."
"11369","Hashim narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Sulayman al-Yashkuri from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he said about doubt in prayer that the correct is aimed at. A man said to him: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: As far as I know."
"11370","Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, then he has a house in the Fire."
"11371","Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A banner will be raised for the traitor for his treachery on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: This is the banner of the treachery of so-and-so."
"11372","Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah that Abu Sa'id narrated to him from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: And Ibn Umar narrated this to me also."
"11373","Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: While a man was walking between two cloaks, strutting, Allah sank him into the earth, and he keeps rattling in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"11374","Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: A neck will come out of the Fire, speaking. It will say: Today I have been entrusted with three: with every tyrant, and with whoever made another god with Allah, and with whoever killed a soul without a soul. So it will fold over them and cast them into the depths of Hell."
"11375","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr informed us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would break fast on the day of breaking fast before going out, and he would not pray before the prayer; then when he finished his prayer, he prayed two rak'ahs."
"11376","al-Nadr ibn Isma'il Abu al-Mughirah al-Qass narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man among those before you went out in two green cloaks, swaggering in them, Allah ordered the earth and it seized him, and he keeps rattling in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"11377","Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever shows off, Allah will expose him, and whoever seeks repute, Allah will spread report of him."
"11378","Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Charity is not lawful for a rich one except that he has a poor neighbor who invites him and he eats with him, or he is a wayfarer, or in the path of Allah."
"11379","Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The changed breath of the fasting mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. He said: This one fasted for My sake and left his desire for food and drink for My sake, so fasting is Mine and I reward for it."
"11380","Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will be said to the companion of the Quran on the Day of Resurrection, when he enters Paradise: Recite and ascend. So he will recite and ascend a degree with every verse, until he recites the last thing with him."
"11381","Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever draws near to Allah a span, Allah draws near to him a cubit. And whoever draws near to Him a cubit, He draws near to him a fathom. And whoever comes to Him walking, Allah comes to him hastening."
"11382","Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us from Firas from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."
"11383","Abu Asim narrated to us from Haywah ibn Shurayh, Salim ibn Ghaylan narrated to us that he heard Abu al-Samh Darraj say: I heard Abu al-Haytham say: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah is pleased with a servant, He praises him with seven kinds of good which he did not do. And when He is angry with him, He praises him with seven kinds of evil which he did not do."
"11384","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyan narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us from Abu Sa'id that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the Children of Isra'il there was a short woman. So she made two legs of wood and would walk between two short women. And she took a ring of gold and stuffed under its stone the best perfume, musk. So when she passed by a gathering, she moved it and it blew its scent."
"11385","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini narrating from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: A Jew came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having been struck in his face. So he said to him: A man of your companions struck me. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Why did you do it? He said: O Messenger of Allah, he preferred Musa over you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not prefer some prophets over others. For people will swoon on the Day of Resurrection, and I will be the first to raise his head from the dust. Then I will find Musa, peace be upon him, at the Throne; I will not know whether he was among those who swooned or not."
"11386","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Aban narrated to us from Yahya from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see the funeral, stand. So whoever follows it, let him not sit until it is placed down."
"11387","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Amr from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Iblis said to his Lord, Exalted and Majestic: By Your might and majesty, I will keep luring the children of Adam while souls are in them. So his Lord, Exalted and Majestic, said to him: By My might and majesty, I will keep forgiving them while they seek My forgiveness."
"11388","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us from Yazid, meaning Ibn al-Had, from Yuhannas, the freedman of Mus'ab ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Arj, a poet appeared reciting. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seize the devil, or: Hold the devil. For a man's belly to be filled with pus is better for him than to be filled with poetry."
"11389","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us from Ibn Ajlan from Sayfi from Abu Sa'id, the freedman of the Ansar, from Abu al-Sa'ib that he said: I came to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri. So while I was sitting with him, I heard under his bed the movement of something. So I looked, and there was a snake. So I stood up. So Abu Sa'id said: What is with you? I said: A snake here. So he said: Then what do you want? So I said: I want to kill it. So he pointed for me to a house in his dwelling facing his house. So he said: A cousin of mine was in this house. So when it was the day of the Confederates, he sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to go to his family, and he was newly married. So he permitted him and ordered him to go with his weapon with him. So he came to his house and found his wife standing at the door of the house. So he pointed at her with the spear. So she said: Do not hasten until you see what brought me out. So he entered the house, and there was a disowned snake. So he stabbed it with the spear, then went out with it on the spear, writhing. He said: I do not know which of them died faster, the man or the snake. So his people came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Supplicate Allah to return our companion. He said: Seek forgiveness for your companion, twice. Then he said: A group of the jinn have embraced Islam. So if you see one of them, then warn it three times. Then if it appears to you after that to kill it, then kill it after the third."
"11390","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Zayd al-Laythi narrated to me, he said: Rubayh ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to me from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it."
"11391","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us from Rubayh ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri from his father from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it."
"11392","He said: Yunus and Hajjaj narrated to us, they both said: Layth narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me from his father that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the funeral is placed and the men carry it on their necks, then if it was righteous, it says: Advance me. And if it was not righteous, it says: O woe to it, where are you going with it? Everything hears its voice except man. And if man heard it, he would swoon. Hajjaj said: He would swoon."
"11393","Isma'il ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Bishr ibn Harb narrated to us from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a lizard. So he turned it with a stick in his hand, back for belly. So he said: A tribe of the Children of Isra'il was lost; then if it is, then it is this."
"11394","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Khayr from Abu al-Khattab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of Tabuk addressed the people while leaning his back against a palm tree. So he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people and the worst of people? Among the best of people is a man who strives in the path of Allah on the back of his horse, or on the back of his camel, or on his feet, until death comes to him. And among the worst of people is a dissolute, audacious man who reads the Book of Allah and is not restrained to anything of it."
"11395","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Nadr that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri used to complain of his leg. So his brother entered upon him, while he had placed one of his legs over the other, lying down. So he struck him with his hand on his painful leg and pained him. So he said: You pained me; did you not know that my leg is painful? He said: Yes. He said: Then what made you do that? He said: Did you not hear that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this?"
"11396","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Harb narrated to us from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a lizard. So he said: Turn it on its back. So it was turned on its back. Then he said: Turn it on its belly. So it was turned on its belly. So he said: A tribe of those with whom Allah is angry among the Children of Isra'il was lost; then if it is, then it is this; then if it is, then it is this; then if it is, then it is this."
"11397","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Jahdam, meaning al-Yamami, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Zayd from Shahr ibn Hawshab from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade buying what is in the bellies of cattle until they give birth, what is in their udders except by measure, buying a slave while he is runaway, buying spoils until they are divided, buying charities until they are received, and the diver's strike."
"11398","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Abu al-Aswad narrated to us from Urwah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to walk in one sandal or in one slipper."
"11399","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr informed me from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri from his father that he complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of his need. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be patient, Abu Sa'id, for poverty to one who loves me among you is faster than a flood on the top of the valley, and from the top of the mountain to its bottom."
"11400","Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us from al-Hajjaj from Atiyyah ibn Sa'd from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The camel people boasted before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tranquility and dignity are among the sheep people, and pride and arrogance are among the camel people."
"11401","Ismail ibn Umar Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra narrated to us, Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Abi Sarh narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he went out on the day of Eid, on the day of Fitr, would pray with the people those two rakahs, then give the salutation and stand and face the people while they were sitting, and he would say: Give charity, three times. The ones who gave charity most were the women, with earrings and with rings and with things. If the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a need to dispatch an expedition against the people, he would mention it to them, otherwise he would leave."
"11402","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spat in his garment and then rubbed it."
"11403","Arim narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said, Ali ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Said, and he raised it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: When a man is uncertain in his prayer and does not know whether he added or decreased, let him prostrate two prostrations while he is sitting."
"11404","Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Suhayl, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mukmil, from Ayyub ibn Bashir al-Ansari, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No one has three daughters, or three sisters, or two daughters, or two sisters, and he fears Allah concerning them and treats them well, except that he will enter Paradise."
"11405","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, he said, Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said, my uncle, meaning Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, narrated to me, from a freedman of Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: While I was with Abu Said al-Khudri with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, we entered the mosque, and there was a man sitting in the middle of the mosque, sitting with his knees drawn up, interlacing his fingers with one another. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gestured to him, but the man did not notice the gesture of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to Abu Said and said: When one of you is in the mosque, let him not interlace his fingers, for interlacing is from Satan, and one of you remains in prayer as long as he is in the mosque until he leaves it."
"11406","Surayj narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, he said: I bear witness concerning Abu Said and Abu Hurayrah that they both bore witness concerning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Allah grants respite until, when it is the last third of the night, He descends and says: Is there any asker, that he be given? Is there any seeker of forgiveness for a sin? Is there any supplicant, that he be answered?"
"11407","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ismah al-Hanafi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: A man prayed behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he would bow before he bowed and raise his head before he raised his head. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished the prayer, he said: Who did this? He said: I did, O Messenger of Allah, I wanted to know whether you would notice that or not. So he said: Beware of the defective prayer. When the imam bows, then bow, and when he rises, then rise."
"11408","Surayj and Affan narrated to us, they said, Hammad narrated to us, and Affan said, al-Hajjaj informed us, from Atiyyah ibn Sad, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he said: I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, or a man asked him and said: O Messenger of Allah, a wolf cut off the tail of a sheep of mine, so may I sacrifice it? He said: Yes. And Affan said: concerning the tail of a sheep of his, and the wolf cut it off, so he said: May I sacrifice it? He said: Yes."
"11409","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked Ibn Said about the soil of Paradise. He said: Fine white flour, pure musk. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He spoke the truth."
"11410","Surayj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We performed Hajj and camped under a tree, and Ibn Said came and camped in its vicinity. I said: To Allah we belong, what has been cast upon me? He said: So he said: O Abu Said, what I meet from the people and what they say to me! They say that I am the Dajjal. Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Dajjal will have no child born to him, and he will not enter Madinah nor Makkah? He said: I said: Yes indeed. And he said: A child has been born to me, and I have left Madinah, and I am heading for Makkah. Abu Said said: It is as if I felt pity for him. Then he said: By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of the people about his place. He said: I said: Fie upon you for the rest of the day."
"11411","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said, Malik informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is close that the best wealth of a Muslim man will be sheep with which he follows the mountain peaks and the places of rainfall, fleeing with his religion from tribulations."
"11412","Ishaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sasah al-Ansari, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a neighbor who stands in prayer at night and recites nothing but Say, He is Allah, the One, as if he considers it little. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, it indeed equals a third of the Quran."
"11413","Ishaq and al-Khuzai narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, and al-Khuzai said: Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sasah, from his father, that he informed him that Abu Said al-Khudri said to him: I see that you love sheep and the desert. When you are among your sheep or in your desert and you call the adhan for prayer, raise your voice with the call, for no one hears the voice of the muadhdhin, and al-Khuzai said: none hears the extent of the voice of the muadhdhin, neither jinn nor man nor anything, except that it will bear witness for him on the Day of Resurrection. Abu Said said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah."
"11414","Ishaq narrated to us, he said, Malik informed me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you is praying, let him not leave anyone to pass in front of him, and let him repel him as much as he can. If he refuses, then let him fight him, for he is only a devil."
"11415","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever forgets the witr or sleeps through it, let him pray it when he remembers it or when he wakes in the morning."
"11416","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The pre-dawn meal is a blessed meal, so do not leave it, even if one of you takes only a sip of water, for Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who take the pre-dawn meal."
"11417","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said, I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from his father, he said: I asked Abu Said al-Khudri about the lower garment. He said: You have come upon one well informed. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The lower garment of the Muslim is to the middle of the shin, and there is no harm, or no blame, in what is between it and the ankles. What is lower than that is in the Fire. Whoever drags his lower garment out of arrogance, Allah will not look at him."
"11418","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said another time, I think it is from Abu Said, that he said: There will not enter Paradise one who reminds others of his favors, nor one disobedient to his parents, nor one addicted to drink."
"11419","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that some people from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon a tribe from the Arab tribes, but they did not host them. While they were like that, the chief of those people was stung. They said: Is there among you a remedy or one who recites incantations? They said: You did not host us, and we will not do anything until you set a wage for us. So they set for them a flock of sheep. He said: So he began reciting the Mother of the Quran, gathering his saliva and spitting, and the man recovered. Then they brought them the sheep. They said: We will not take them until we ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about them. So they asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that. He laughed and said: What made you know that it is an incantation? Take them, and strike a share in them for me."
"11420","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste, and whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will enrich him. Whoever asks us for something and we find it, we will give it to him."
"11421","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said, Shubah narrated to us, he said, I heard Abu Hamzah narrating from Hilal ibn Hisn, he said: I stayed with Abu Said al-Khudri, and the sitting place brought me and him together. He said: So he narrated that one morning he woke having bound a stone over his belly from hunger. His wife or his mother said to him: Go to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ask him, for so-and-so came to him and asked him and he gave him, and so-and-so came to him and asked him and he gave him. He said: I said: Until I look for something. He said: So I looked, and I came to him. Hajjaj said: So I did not find anything, and I came to him while he was preaching, and I caught from his speech, as he was saying: Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste, and whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will enrich him. Whoever asks us, either we will give him or we will console him, Abu Hamzah being the one in doubt. Whoever seeks chastity from us or seeks self-sufficiency is dearer to us than whoever asks us. He said: So I returned and did not ask him for anything. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, continued to provide for us until I know of no household among the Ansar with more wealth than us."
"11422","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said, Abu Hamzah informed me, he said, I heard Hilal ibn Hisn, the brother of Banu Qays ibn Thalabah, he said: I came to Madinah and stayed in the house of Abu Said, and he mentioned the hadith."
"11423","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Let not fear of people prevent any man among you from speaking the truth when he sees it or knows it."
"11424","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah, that he heard Abu Nadrah narrating from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"11425","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abu Said, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There is no charity on less than five camels, nor on five awsuq, nor on five awaqi is there charity."
"11426","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Safwan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance his face from Hell by a journey of seventy years."
"11427","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, they said, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Dhakwan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: No man who believes in Allah and the Last Day hates the Ansar."
"11428","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that a man entered the mosque after the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had prayed with his companions. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who will give charity to this one and pray with him? So a man from the people stood and prayed with him."
"11429","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab, from Said, from Qatadah, from Qazaah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Journeys are undertaken only to three mosques: the mosque of Ibrahim, and the mosque of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Bayt al-Maqdis. He said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade prayer at two times: after the morning, and Abd al-Wahhab said: after Fajr, until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets. And he forbade fasting on two days: Fitr and Nahr. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a woman to travel more than three days, or three nights, except with a mahram. Abd al-Aziz said in his hadith: Qazaah, the freedman of Ziyad."
"11430","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abdullah informed us, from Qatadah, from Qazaah, except that he said: concerning prayer after the Fajr prayer until the sun shines, and he did not doubt three nights."
"11431","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh narrated to us, they said, Said narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahhab, from Said, from Qatadah, from Abu Isa, Abd al-Wahhab said in his hadith: from Abu Isa al-Harithi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to drink standing."
"11432","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought fresh Rayyan dates, while the dates of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were dry unirrigated dates with dryness in them. He said: Where did you get these dates from? They said: These are dates we bought, a sa for two sas of our dates. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That is not proper, but sell your dates, then buy what you need."
"11433","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with twelve nights remaining of Ramadan, on his departure to Hunayn. Some groups of people fasted and others broke their fast, and neither did the fasting blame the one breaking fast, nor the one breaking fast blame the fasting."
"11434","Muhammad ibn Jafar Ghundar narrated to us, he said, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said concerning the fetus: Its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother."
"11435","Bahz and Affan narrated to us, they said, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, Affan said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to recite the Opening of the Book and what is easy."
"11436","Bahz narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: My community will be two factions, and there will emerge between them renegades; the nearer of them to the truth will undertake killing them."
"11437","Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Qazaah, from Abu Said, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, and my mosque, and the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis. A woman shall not travel more than three nights except with a husband or a mahram. There is no prayer after the Asr prayer until the sun sets, and no prayer after the Fajr prayer until the sun rises. And he forbade fasting on the day of Fitr and the day of Nahr."
"11438","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Abu al-Waddak, he said: I will not drink nabidh after I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: A man was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: They said: He is intoxicated. He said: I only drank raisins and dates in a gourd. He said: So he was struck with sandals and pushed with hands, and he forbade the gourd, and forbade raisins and dates to be mixed together."
"11439","Hajjaj and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, they said, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Usm, Abu Ulwan, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is not lawful for anyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day to untie the hobble of a she-camel without the permission of its owners, for it is their seal upon it. If you are in a desert and you see the milk skin, or the water skin, or the vessel of milk, then call the owners of the camels three times. If they give you drink, then drink, otherwise not. If you are destitute, Abu al-Nadr said: and you have no food with you, then let two men among you hold it, then drink."
"11440","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shubah informed us, and Muhammad ibn Jafar, Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Sulayman al-Yashkuri, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he said concerning doubt in prayer: one aims for what is most correct. A man said to him: From the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: So far as I know."
"11441","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said, Ibn Shihab informed me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wrapping in a single garment that covers the whole body, and that a man sit with his knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing of it over his private part."
"11442","Yunus and Hashim narrated to us, they said, Layth narrated to us, Hashim said, he said, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade wrapping in a single garment that covers the whole body, and that a man sit with his knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing of it over his private part."
"11443","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came upon a river from the sky while the people were fasting on a hot summer day on foot, and the Prophet of Allah was on a mule of his. He said: Drink, O people. He said: But they refused. He said: I am not like you, I am the most eased of you, I am riding. But they refused. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bent his thigh and dismounted and drank, and the people drank, though he had not wanted to drink."
"11444","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Zayd narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Narrate from me and do not lie upon me. Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And narrate from the Children of Israil, and there is no harm."
"11445","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Two tribes of the Children of Israil went astray, and I fear that they are the lizards."
"11446","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyan al-Iyadi narrated to us, Abu Nadrah al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned the worldly life and said: The worldly life is green and sweet, so beware of it and beware of women. Then he mentioned three women from the Children of Israil: two tall women who were known, and a short woman who was not known. She took two legs of wood and fashioned a ring and stuffed it with the best of perfume, musk, and made for it a lid. When she passed by a gathering or a sitting place, she motioned with it and opened it, and its scent spread. Al-Mustamirr said: With his left little finger, and he raised it apart from his three fingers somewhat, and he closed the three."
"11447","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Mustamirr narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: For every treacherous one there is a banner on the Day of Resurrection, raised for him according to his treachery. Indeed, there is no treacherous one greater than the treachery of a leader of the people."
"11448","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Mustamirr narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let not fear of people, or of men, prevent any one of you from speaking the truth when he sees it or knows it, or sees it or hears it."
"11449","Abd al-Samad and Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Silver for silver and gold for gold, like for like."
"11450","Surayj narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Gold for gold and silver for silver, and do not prefer some of them over others."
"11451","Said ibn Mansur narrated to us the like of it with its chain."
"11452","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, he said, Abu Said, the freedman of al-Mahri, narrated to me, he said, Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless for us in our mudd. O Allah, bless for us in our sa, and place with the blessing two blessings."
"11453","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, this greeting upon you we have known, so how should we send prayers upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad, Your servant and Your Messenger, as You sent prayers upon Ibrahim, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim."
"11454","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to Quba on Monday, and we passed through Banu Salim. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stopped at the door of Ibn Itban and shouted, while Ibn Itban was upon the belly of his wife. He came out dragging his lower garment. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw him, he said: We hastened the man. Ibn Itban said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man who comes to his wife and does not ejaculate, what is upon him? So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Water is only from water."
"11455","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Zayd, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: My family sent me to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to ask him for food. I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was preaching, and I heard him say: Whoever is patient, Allah will make him patient, and whoever seeks self-sufficiency, Allah will enrich him, and whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste. No provision has been given to a servant wider for him than patience."
"11456","Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Zayd, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Beware of sitting in the roads. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we must have our sittings in which we talk. He said: Then give the road its right. They said: And what is the right of the road, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Lowering the gaze, withholding harm, enjoining the good, and forbidding the evil."
"11457","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Safar, from al-Shabi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: A funeral passed by Marwan and he did not stand. He said: So Abu Said said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had a funeral pass by him and he stood. He said: So Marwan stood."
"11458","Waki narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Amr, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said, he said: We took captives on the day of Hunayn, and we were seeking their ransom. We asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about withdrawal. He said: Do what seems fit to you, for what Allah has decreed will be. Not from all the fluid is there a child."
"11459","Waki narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khulayd ibn Jafar, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, he said: Musk was mentioned before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: It is the best of perfume."
"11460","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Sufyan informed us, from Zubayd, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let none of you belittle himself when he sees a matter of Allah about which there is something to be said, that he fails to speak about it. Then it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: What prevented you from speaking about it? He will say: My Lord, I feared the people. He said: So I was more deserving to be feared. And Abu Nuaym said, meaning in the hadith: I was more deserving that you fear Me."
"11461","Waki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to me, Abu al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, from Abu Said, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: People will come out of the Fire after they have burned and become charcoal, and they will enter Paradise and sprout therein as rubbish sprouts in the flood debris."
"11462","Waki narrated to us, from Ali ibn Salih, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayh al-Anazi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: They will sprout as the sadanah plant sprouts."
"11463","Waki narrated to us, from Sharik, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Said, he said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, followed a funeral, he would not sit until it was placed down."
"11464","Waki narrated to us, from Ikrimah ibn Ammar, from Asim ibn Shumaykh, from Abu Said, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, emphasized an oath, he would say: No, by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Abu al-Qasim."
"11465","Waki and Bahz narrated to us, they said, Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, and Waki, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Isa, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Visit the sick and follow funerals; they remind you of the Hereafter."
"11466","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Isa al-Uswari, and he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: the sick one."
"11467","Waki narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ali al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Jawza, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas giving a ruling about exchange. He said: So I gave rulings by it for a time. He said: Then I met him and he retracted it. He said: So I said to him: Why? He said: It was only an opinion I held. Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it."
"11468","Waki narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl, Abu Nadrah al-Abdi narrated to us, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Renegades will pass at a division among the Muslims; the nearer of the two parties to the truth will kill them."
"11469","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Sharik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father and his uncle Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Eat the meat of the sacrifices and store it."
"11470","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No weariness, nor toil, nor worry, nor grief, nor harm, nor distress befalls the believer, even the thorn he is pricked with, except that Allah expiates thereby some of his sins."
"11471","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you see the funeral, stand. Whoever follows it, let him not sit until it is placed down."
"11472","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Yazid, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We were given mixed dates in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"11473","Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, Jafar ibn Iyas narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Jabir ibn Abdullah and Abu Said al-Khudri, they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Truffles are from the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye. Ajwah dates are from Paradise, and they are a cure from poison."
"11474","Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Said ibn Yazid, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When they are three, let one of them lead them, and the most entitled of them to lead is the most reciting among them."
"11475","Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Said ibn Yazid, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When they are three, let one of them lead them, and the most entitled of them to lead is the most reciting among them."
"11476","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Said ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: There will be after me a caliph who will scoop wealth scooping and will not count it counting."
"11477","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Yazid, Hisham informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said, he said: We were given mixed dates, Yazid said: dates from the mixed dates, in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we would sell two sas for a sa. That reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: No two sas of dates for a sa, nor two sas of wheat for a sa, nor two dirhams for a dirham. Yazid said: No two sas of dates for a sa, nor two sas of wheat for a sa."
"11478","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said, Anas ibn Sirin narrated to me, from his brother Mabad ibn Sirin, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Shubah said: I said to him: Did you hear it from Abu Said? He said: Yes, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about withdrawal. He said: There is no harm upon you if you do not do that, for it is only the decree."
"11479","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you stands praying, let him not leave anyone to pass in front of him. If he refuses, then let him fight him, for he is only a devil."
"11480","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: The first to present the sermon before the prayer was Marwan. A man stood and said: O Marwan, you have opposed the Sunnah. He said: What was there has been left, O Abu so-and-so. Abu Said said: As for this one, he has fulfilled what was upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever among you sees an evil, let him change it with his hand. If he cannot, then with his tongue. If he cannot, then with his heart, and that is the weakest of faith."
"11481","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Abu Said, the freedman of al-Mahdi, narrated to him, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent an expedition to Banu Lihyan of Hudhayl and said: Let one of every two men go forth, and the reward is between them."
"11482","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We took captives on the day of Hunayn and we practiced withdrawal from them while we wanted ransom. Some of us said to others: You do that while among you is the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? So I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Not from all the fluid is there a child. When Allah wants to create something, nothing prevents Him."
"11483","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Shubah and Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, he said: I bear witness concerning Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said that they both bore witness concerning the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: No people sit remembering Allah except that the angels surround them, and mercy covers them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."
"11484","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade mixing unripe dates and ripe dates, and raisins and dates."
"11485","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, and Hajjaj, they said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, he said: We were detained on the day of the Trench from prayer until after Maghrib, well into the night, until we were sufficed. That is the saying of Allah, Exalted: And Allah sufficed the believers in fighting, and Allah is Strong, Mighty. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called Bilal, and he made the iqamah for the Zuhr prayer and he prayed it, and he prayed it well as he used to pray it in its time. Then he ordered him and he made the iqamah for Asr and he prayed it, and he prayed it well as he used to pray it in its time. Then he ordered him and he made the iqamah for Maghrib and he prayed it likewise. He said: And that was before Allah revealed concerning the fear prayer: on foot or mounted."
"11486","Rawh narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji narrated to us, Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to us, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. A man from the people said to him: Is there between you and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, anyone other than Abu Said? He said: No, by Allah, there is none between me and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, other than Abu Said. He said: Gold for gold, and silver for silver, and wheat for wheat, and barley for barley, and dates for dates, and salt for salt, equal for equal. Whoever adds or seeks addition has dealt in usury; the taker and the giver therein are alike."
"11487","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people of Illiyyin are seen by those below them as a star is seen in the horizon of the sky. Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and blessed."
"11488","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, Iyad ibn Hilal al-Ansari narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you prays and forgets how many he prayed, or he said: and does not know whether he added or decreased, let him prostrate two prostrations while he is sitting. When Satan comes to one of you and says: You have broken your ablution, let him say: You lie, except what he hears with his ear or finds its smell with his nose."
"11489","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, Said al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, put on a new garment, he would name it by its name, a turban or a shirt or a cloak, then he would say: O Allah, to You is praise, You have clothed me with it. I ask You its good and the good of what it was made for, and I seek refuge in You from its evil and from the evil of what it was made for."
"11490","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Ibn al-Had, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had his uncle Abu Talib mentioned before him. He said: Perhaps my intercession will benefit him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will be placed in a shallow part of the Fire reaching his ankles, and his brain will boil from it."
"11491","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Said ibn Iyas informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, he said: We used to travel with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Ramadan. Some of us were fasting and some of us were breaking fast, and neither did the fasting blame the one breaking fast, nor the one breaking fast blame the fasting."
"11492","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Numan Abu al-Numan al-Ansari narrated to us in Kufah, from Sulayman ibn Qannah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent an expedition, and I was among them. We came upon a village and sought food from its people, but they refused to feed us anything. A man from the people of the village came to us and said: O Arabs, is there among you a man who recites incantations? Abu Said said: I said: And what is that? He said: The king of the village is dying. He said: So we went with him, and I recited over him the Opening of the Book, repeating it over him many times, and he was healed. He sent to us food and sheep driven to us. My companions said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not instruct us about this; we will not take anything from it until we come to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So we drove the sheep until we came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we told him. He said: Eat, and feed us with you. And what made you know that it is an incantation? He said: I said: It was cast into my heart."
"11493","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Atish narrated to us, Jafar, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, from Ali ibn Ali al-Yashkuri, from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood at night and opened his prayer and said the takbir, he would say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. Blessed is Your name, exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god besides You. Then he would say: There is no god but Allah, three times. Then he would say: I seek refuge in Allah, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, from the accursed Satan, from his madness and his arrogance. Then he would say: Allah is Greatest, three times. Then he would say: I seek refuge in Allah, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, from the accursed Satan, from his madness, his arrogance, and his poetry."
"11494","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, from al-Mualla al-Qardusi, from al-Hasan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let not fear of people prevent any one of you from speaking the truth when he sees it or witnesses it, for it neither brings near a term nor distances a provision, to speak the truth or to remind of a grievous matter."
"11495","Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, and Yazid ibn Harun, Hisham informed us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We were given mixed dates, and Yazid said: dates from the mixed dates, in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we would sell two sas for a sa. That reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: No two sas of dates for a sa, nor two sas of wheat for a sa, nor two dirhams for a dirham."
"11496","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you see the funeral, stand. Whoever follows it, let him not sit until it is placed down."
"11497","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said, Abu Rifah narrated to me, that Abu Said al-Khudri said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a slave girl, and I practice withdrawal from her, and I want what a man wants, and I hate that she conceive. The Jews claim that the lesser burying alive is withdrawal. He said: The Jews lied. If Allah wants to create it, no one can avert it."
"11498","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Yahya, Iyad narrated to us, that he asked Abu Said al-Khudri and said: One of us prays and does not know how many he prayed. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you prays and does not know how many he prayed, let him prostrate two prostrations while he is sitting. If Satan comes to one of you and says: You have broken your ablution in your prayer, let him say: You lied, except what he finds as wind with his nose or hears a sound with his ear."
"11499","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ali al-Rabi informed us, Abu al-Jawza narrated to us more than once, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about exchange, hand to hand. He said: There is no harm in that, two for one, more than that and less. He said: Then I performed Hajj another time, while the Shaykh was alive, and I came to him and asked him about exchange. He said: Weight for weight. He said: So I said: You gave me a ruling of two for one, and I have continued to give rulings by it since you gave me that ruling. He said: That was from my opinion. This Abu Said al-Khudri narrates from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I left my opinion for the hadith of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"11500","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Awn informed us, from Nafi, he said: A man used to narrate to Ibn Umar a hadith from Abu Said al-Khudri about exchange. He said: Abu Said came and stayed in this house. Ibn Umar took my hand and the hand of the man until we came to Abu Said. He stood over him and said: What is this that this one narrates from you? Abu Said said: Yes, my eye saw and my ear heard, and he pointed with his finger to his eyes and his ears. I did not forget his saying with his fingers, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he forbade gold for gold and silver for silver except equal for equal, like for like. Behold, do not sell what is absent for what is present, and do not make one of them exceed the other."
"11501","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Sa'id informed us from Qatadah, my father said, and Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When three gather, let one of them lead them, and the most entitled of them to lead is the best reciter among them."
"11502","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us from al-Aswad ibn Qays from Rubayh from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that they went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and they alighted in groups, a group with so-and-so and a group with so-and-so. He said: So I alighted in the group of Abu Bakr, and with us was a Bedouin from the people of the desert. We alighted with a Bedouin household among whom was a pregnant woman, and the Bedouin said to her: Would it please you to bear a boy, if you give me a sheep you will bear a boy. So she gave him a sheep and he chanted rhymed chants for her. He said: Then he slaughtered the sheep, and when the people sat eating, a man said: Do you know what this sheep is. Then he informed them. He said: Then I saw Abu Bakr holding himself apart, stretching forth his neck, vomiting."
"11503","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us: Qaza'ah narrated to me that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So I was impressed, and I drew near to him, and it was in my mind until I came to him, and I said: Did you hear from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Then he became intensely angry. He said: So should I narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what I did not hear. Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques, this mosque of mine, and the Sacred Mosque, and al-Aqsa Mosque. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A woman does not travel except with her husband or a mahram of hers. And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no fasting on two days, the day of Adha and the day of Fitr from Ramadan. And I heard him say: There is no prayer after two prayers, the Fajr prayer until the sun rises, and the Asr prayer until the sun sets."
"11504","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to me: al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad al-Ma'wali narrated to us from al-Ala ibn Bashir al-Muzani from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I give you glad tidings of the Mahdi. He will be sent in my ummah amid disagreement among people and earthquakes, and he will fill the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with wrong and injustice. The dweller of heaven and the dweller of earth will be pleased with him, and Allah will fill the hearts of the ummah of Muhammad with richness, so no one will need anyone. Then a caller will call: Who has a need for wealth. He said: Then a man will stand and say: I do. Then it will be said to him: Go to the keeper, meaning the treasurer, and say to him: The Mahdi says to you: Give me. He said: Then he will come to the keeper and say it to him. Then it will be said to him: Scoop up. So he will scoop up, and when he has secured it he will say: I was the greediest soul of the ummah of Muhammad, or was what sufficed them beyond me. He said: Then he will remain seven years, or eight years, or nine years, then there is no good in life, or in living, after him."
"11505","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to me: al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad narrated to us from al-Ala ibn Bashir al-Muzani, and he was one who wept at remembrance and brave at encounter, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri the like of it, and he added in it: Then he will regret, and he will bring it to the keeper, and he will say to him: We do not accept anything we have given."
"11506","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Marzuq, freedman of Banu Anz, narrated to me from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one will enter Paradise except by the mercy of Allah. We said: O Messenger of Allah, not even you. He said: Not even I, unless Allah envelops me with His mercy. And he said with his hand over his head."
"11507","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower garment of the Muslim is to mid-shin, and what is to the ankle there is no harm, and what is below the ankle is in the Fire."
"11508","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Najih narrated to us from Yazid al-Faqir who said: I said to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: Among us are men who are the best of us in reciting the Quran and the most of us in prayer and the most joining of kinship and the most of us in fasting, they have gone out against us with their swords. Then Abu Sa'id said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will emerge a people who recite the Quran, it will not pass their throats, they will pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game."
"11509","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir from Abu Sa'id who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying on a mat and prostrating upon it."
"11510","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay the Zuhr in the heat, for the intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell. Thus al-A'mash said: from the blast of Hell."
"11511","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The accumulators of wealth have perished. They said: Except who. He said: The accumulators of wealth have perished. They said: Except who. He said: The accumulators of wealth have perished. He said: Until we feared it had become binding. He said: Except one who says thus and thus and thus, and few are they."
"11512","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us from Ismail ibn Raja from his father who said: The first to bring out the minbar on the day of Eid was Marwan, and the first to begin with the sermon before the prayer. Then a man stood and said: O Marwan, you have opposed the Sunnah, you brought out the minbar though it was not brought out, and you began with the sermon before the prayer. Abu Sa'id said: Who is this. They said: So-and-so son of so-and-so. He said: As for this, he has fulfilled what was upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever sees an evil, if he is able to change it with his hand, then if he is not able then with his tongue, then if he is not able then with his heart, and that is the weakest of faith."
"11513","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir from Abu Sa'id who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying wrapped in a single garment."
"11514","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Ubayd Allah: Nafi' informed me, he said: It reached Ibn Umar that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri related a hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about exchange. So he took my hand, and I and he and the man went. Then he said: What hadith has reached me from you that you relate from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about exchange. Then he said: My ears heard it and my heart retained it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Do not sell gold for gold except like for like, nor silver for silver except like for like, and do not prefer some of it over some, and do not sell of it what is absent for what is present."
"11515","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Mujalid: Abu al-Waddak narrated to us from Abu Sa'id who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the fetus of the she-camel and the cow. Then he said: If you wish, eat it, for its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother."
"11516","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from al-A'mash from Dhakwan from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the heat is intense, delay the prayer, for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"11517","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell, so delay the prayer."
"11518","Yahya narrated to us from al-Taymi: Abu Nadrah narrated to us from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Let not fear of people prevent one of you from speaking the truth when he sees it or witnesses it or hears it. Then Abu Sa'id said: I wish I had not heard it. And Abu Nadrah said: I wish I had not heard it."
"11519","Yahya narrated to us from Hisham from Yahya from Iyad that he asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: One of us prays, not knowing how much he prayed. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays and does not know how much he prayed, let him prostrate two prostrations, and if Satan comes to him and says: You have broken your ablution, let him say: You have lied, unless he finds a smell with his nose or a sound with his ear."
"11520","Suwayd ibn Amr narrated to us: Aban narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us from Hilal ibn Iyad from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays, then he mentioned its meaning."
"11521","He said: Yunus narrated to us, he said: Aban narrated to us from Yahya from Hilal ibn Iyad, and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us from Yahya, he said: Iyad ibn Hilal informed me that he heard Abu Sa'id, then he mentioned its meaning."
"11522","Yahya narrated to us: Hisham narrated to us: Yahya narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, he said: Abu Rifa'ah narrated to me that Abu Sa'id said: A man said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have a slave girl and I practice coitus interruptus with her, and I dislike that she conceive, and the Jews claim it is the minor burying alive. He said: The Jews have lied. When Allah wills to create it, you cannot repel it."
"11523","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about coitus interruptus: Do you create him, do you provide for him. Leave it in its place, for that is only the decree."
"11524","Yahya narrated to us from Malik, and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Malik narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Ata ibn Yazid from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you hear the call, say the like of what the caller to prayer says."
"11525","Yahya narrated to us from Mujalid: Abu al-Waddak narrated to me from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not fast two days, and do not pray two prayers, and do not fast the day of Fitr nor the day of Adha, and do not pray after Fajr until the sun rises, nor after Asr until the sun sets, and a woman does not travel three days except with a mahram with her, and saddles are not tightened except to three mosques, the Sacred Mosque, and my mosque, and the mosque of Bayt al-Maqdis."
"11526","Yahya and Waki' narrated to us from Zakariyya: Amir narrated to me, he said: Abu Sa'id and Marwan were sitting, and a funeral passed by them, so Abu Sa'id stood. Then Marwan said: Sit. Then Abu Sa'id said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand, so Marwan stood. And Waki' said: A funeral passed by him, so he stood."
"11527","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Dawud ibn Qays informed us that he heard Iyad ibn Abd Allah narrating that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out on the day of Fitr praying those two rak'ahs."
"11528","Yahya narrated to us from Dawud ibn Qays, he said: Iyad narrated to me: Abu Sa'id narrated to me, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out on the day of Eid, Yahya said: I do not know it except he said Fitr and Adha, and he would pray with the people two rak'ahs. Then he would stand up, face the people with his face, and say: Give charity. Then the most who gave charity were the women. Abd al-Razzaq said: With the ring and the earring and the thing, then he mentioned its meaning. If he had a need or wanted to dispatch an expedition, he spoke, otherwise he left."
"11529","Waki' and Affan and Abd al-Samad narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us from Abu Isa al-Uswari from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rebuked drinking while standing."
"11530","Waki' narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to me from Atiyyah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: A man asked him about washing from major impurity. Then he said: Three times. Then he said: I have much hair. Abu Sa'id said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had more hair than you and was more perfumed."
"11531","Waki' narrated to us: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us: Abu Nadrah al-Abdi narrated to us from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw lagging among his companions. Then he said: Advance and follow me, and let those after you follow you. And people will continue to lag until Allah delays them."
"11532","Waki' narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab narrated to us from his uncle from a freedman of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he was with Abu Sa'id while he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and saw a man sitting in the middle of the mosque interlacing his fingers, talking to himself. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him, but he did not notice. He said: Then he turned to Abu Sa'id and said: When one of you prays, let him not interlace his fingers, for interlacing is from Satan. One of you remains in prayer as long as he is in the mosque until he leaves it."
"11533","Waki' narrated to us: Ali ibn Mubarak narrated to us from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Iyad ibn Hilal from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Satan comes to one of you in his prayer and says: You have broken your ablution, let him say: You have lied, unless he finds a smell with his nose or hears a sound with his ear."
"11534","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Qays ibn Muslim from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: The first to begin with the sermon on the day of Eid before the prayer was Marwan ibn al-Hakam. Then a man stood to him and said: The prayer is before the sermon. Then Marwan said: What was there has been left, O Abu so-and-so. Then Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: As for this, he has fulfilled what was upon him. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever among you sees an evil, let him change it with his hand, and if he is not able then with his tongue, and if he is not able then with his heart, and that is the weakest of faith."
"11535","Waki' and Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, they said: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id, and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from al-A'mash from Dhakwan from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman does not travel a journey of three days or more except with her father, or her brother, or her son, or her husband, or with a mahram."
"11536","Waki' narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile my companions, for by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if one of you spent the like of Uhud in gold, he would not reach the mudd of one of them nor half of it."
"11537","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sulayman from Dhakwan from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"11538","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us the like of it."
"11539","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abd Allah informed us: Ibn Lahi'ah informed us from Habban ibn Wasi' from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays in a single garment, let him place its two ends upon his shoulders."
"11540","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Haywah: Ibn al-Had narrated to me that Abd Allah ibn Khabbab narrated to them from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his uncle Abu Talib was mentioned in his presence. Then he said: Perhaps my intercession will benefit him on the Day of Resurrection, so he will be placed in a shallow pool of the Fire reaching his ankles, his brain boiling from it."
"11541","Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Haywah: Ibn al-Had narrated to me from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of the solitary by twenty-five degrees."
"11542","And with this isnad that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me, he has seen the truth, for Satan does not take my likeness."
"11543","And with this isnad from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that major impurity befalls him and he wants to sleep. So he ordered him to perform ablution, then sleep."
"11544","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us from Abd Allah ibn Qurayt that Ata ibn Yasar narrated to him that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever fasts Ramadan and knows its limits and guards what he ought to guard in it, it expiates what came before it."
"11545","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abd Allah informed us: al-Fudayl ibn Marzuq informed us from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved of people to Allah on the Day of Resurrection and the nearest of them to Him in seating is a just imam, and the most hateful of people to Allah on the Day of Resurrection and the most severe of them in punishment is a tyrannical imam."
"11546","Ya'mar ibn Bishr narrated to us: Abd Allah informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed us: Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us from Abu Sulayman al-Laythi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The example of the believer and the example of faith is like the example of the horse in its tether, it roams then returns to its tether. The believer errs then returns to faith. So feed your food to the God-fearing, and bestow your kindness upon the believers."
"11547","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated it to us, and this is more complete."
"11548","Attab narrated to us: Abd Allah narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah informed us: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me from Yazid ibn Abi Sa'id, freedman of al-Mahra, from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition to Banu Lihyan. He said: Meaning let one of every two men go forth. And he said to the one staying: Whichever of you stays behind caring for the family and wealth of the one going forth with good will have the like of half the reward of the one going forth."
"11549","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us: al-Mubarak narrated to us from al-Hasan from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he narrated to him from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that dates were brought to him and their quality pleased him. Then they said: O Messenger of Allah, we took a sa' for two sa's to feed him it. Then he disliked that and forbade it."
"11550","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim informed us: Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Had narrated to us from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of the solitary by twenty-five degrees."
"11551","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty has one hundred mercies. He divided of them one part among creation, and by it people and beasts and birds show mercy to one another."
"11552","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Asim ibn Bahdalah from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has one hundred mercies, with Him ninety-nine, and He has placed with you one by which you show mercy among the jinn and mankind and among creation. Then when the Day of Resurrection comes, He will join it to it."
"11553","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The worst of people in theft is he who steals his prayer. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and how does he steal it. He said: He does not complete its bowing nor its prostration."
"11554","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of the Fire enter the Fire, he said: Allah Blessed and Exalted says: Whoever had in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith, take him out. He said: Then they will be taken out, burnt and turned to coal. Then they will be cast into a river called the River of Life. Then they will sprout in it as the seed sprouts in the debris of the flood, or he said in the debris-borne soil of the flood. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you not seen that it sprouts yellow, curling."
"11555","Affan narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us: Abu Nadrah narrated to us from Abu Sa'id that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Have you complained, O Muhammad. Then he said: Yes. Then he said: In the name of Allah I charm you from everything that harms you, from the evil of every eye and soul, He heals you. In the name of Allah I charm you."
"11556","Affan narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us from Ata, and Affan once said Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Sa'id who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the believers is best. He said: A believer who strives in the path of Allah with himself and his wealth. They said: Then who. He said: A believer who has secluded himself in a mountain pass of the mountain passes, or the ravine, sparing people his evil."
"11557","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Zayd ibn Aslam informed us from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not write from me anything other than the Quran. Whoever wrote from me anything other than the Quran, let him erase it. And he said: Narrate from the Children of Israel and there is no harm. Narrate from me and do not lie. He said: And whoever lies upon me, Hammam said: I think he said deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"11558","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was dividing a distribution, Ibn Dhi al-Khuwaysirah al-Tamimi came to him and said: Be just, O Messenger of Allah. Then he said: Woe to you, and who will be just if I am not just. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab said: O Messenger of Allah, will you permit me regarding him that I strike his neck. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him, for he has companions, one of you deems his prayer insignificant beside their prayer and his fasting beside their fasting. They pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game. Then it is looked at its fletchings, and nothing is found in it. Then it is looked at its shaft, and nothing is found in it. Then it is looked at its joint, and nothing is found in it. Then it is looked at its head, and nothing is found in it. It has outrun the dung and the blood. Among them is a black man, in one of his hands, or he said in one of his breasts, the like of the breast of a woman, or the like of a piece of flesh, shaking. They emerge at a time of break among people. Then there was revealed about them: And among them is he who criticizes you concerning charities, the verse. Abu Sa'id said: I bear witness that I heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I bear witness that Ali, when he killed him while I was with him, the man was brought upon the description the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) described."
"11559","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity is not lawful for a rich man except for five: a worker upon it, or a man who buys it with his wealth, or a debtor, or a warrior in the path of Allah, or a poor man given charity from it who then gifts from it to a rich man."
"11560","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me from Iyad ibn Abd Allah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to begin on the day of Fitr and the day of Adha with the prayer before the sermon, then preach, and in his sermon would be the command for dispatch and expedition."
"11561","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us from Zayd ibn Aslam from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one wants to pass between you and your sutra, repel him. If he refuses, push him. If he refuses, fight him, for he is only a devil."
"11562","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Malik narrated to us from Ayyub ibn Habib that he heard Abu al-Muthanna say: I heard Marwan asking Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid blowing into the drink. Then he said: Yes. He said: Then a man said: I am not quenched, O Messenger of Allah, with one breath. He said: Move the cup from your mouth, then breathe. He said: I see a mote in it. He said: Pour it out."
"11563","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Malik narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Soon the best wealth of a man will be sheep with which he follows the mountain peaks and the places of rain, fleeing with his religion from tribulations."
"11564","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us from Ayyub from Abu Qilabah and from Ibn Sirin from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, each of them narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden the meats of sacrifices beyond three days, so eat and take provision and store what you wish. And the other said: Eat and feed and store what you wish."
"11565","Abd al-Razzaq and Rawh narrated to us, they said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us: Abu Qaza'ah informed me that Abu Nadrah informed him, and Hasan informed them both, that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri informed him that the delegation of Abd al-Qays, when they came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make us ransom for you, what is proper for us in drinks. Then he said: Do not drink in the naqir. Then they said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make us ransom for you, do you know what the naqir is. He said: Yes, the trunk hollowed in its middle. Nor in the dubba, nor in the hantamah. And upon you is the muwka. Rawh said: With the muwka, twice."
"11566","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about coitus interruptus. Then he said: Do you indeed do it. They said: Yes. He said: There is no harm upon you if you do not do it, for Allah Exalted has not decreed a soul that He creates it except it will be."
"11567","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us from Abu Amr al-Nadabi who said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not practice continuous fasting. They said: But you practice continuous fasting, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I am not like you. I spend the night fed and given drink."
"11568","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us: Rabah narrated to us from Ma'mar from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: Some people of the Ansar gathered and said: He has favored others over us. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gathered them, then addressed them. Then he said: O company of Ansar, were you not abased, then Allah honored you. They said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken truly. He said: Were you not misguided, then Allah guided you. They said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken truly. He said: Were you not poor, then Allah enriched you. They said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken truly. Then he said: Will you not answer me. Will you not say: You came to us fugitive, so we sheltered you, and you came to us fearful, so we gave you security. Are you not pleased that people go with sheep and cattle, meaning cows, and you go with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), bringing him into your houses. If people took a valley or a path, and you took a valley or a path, I would take your valley or your path. Were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Ansar. You will meet after me preference to others, so be patient until you meet me at the Hawd."
"11569","Ibrahim narrated to us: Rabah narrated to us from Ma'mar from Qatadah about His saying: And We removed what was in their breasts of rancor. He said: Abu al-Mutawakkil narrated to us from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers will be saved from the Fire, then detained upon a bridge between Paradise and the Fire, and retaliation will be taken for some of them from others."
"11570","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me from Abu al-Khayr from Abu al-Khattab from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in the year of Tabuk, addressed the people while leaning his back against a palm tree. Then he said: Shall I not inform you of the best of people and the worst of people. Among the best of people is a man who works in the path of Allah on the back of his horse, or on the back of his camel, or on his feet, until death comes to him. And among the worst of people is a dissolute, daring man who reads the Book of Allah, heeding nothing of it."
"11571","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us: Uqayl narrated to me from Ibn Shihab from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman that Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw sputum in the wall of the mosque. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a pebble and scraped it. Then he said: When one of you expectorates, let him not spit before his face nor to his right. Let him spit to his left or under his left foot."
"11572","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us: Bukayr ibn Abd Allah narrated to me from Iyad ibn Abd Allah ibn Sa'd from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he said: A man suffered loss in the year of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in fruits he had bought, and his debt increased. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give charity to him. He said: Then the people gave charity to him, but that did not reach the payment of his debt. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take what you find, and you have only that."
"11573","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me from his father that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the bier is placed and the men carry it upon their necks, if it was righteous it says: Advance me. And if it was not righteous it says: O woe to it, where are you taking it. Everything hears its voice except man, and if man heard it he would fall unconscious."
"11574","al-Khuza'i, meaning Abu Salamah, narrated to us, except that he said: he would fall unconscious."
"11575","Hajjaj narrated to us: Layth narrated to us, and al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Layth informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id narrated to me from Abu Sa'id, freedman of al-Mahra, that he came to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri in the nights of the Harrah, and consulted him about leaving Medina, and complained to him of its prices and his many dependents, and informed him that he had no patience for the hardship of Medina. Then he said: Woe to you, I do not command you with that. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one endures the hardship of Medina and its distress then dies except I will be for him an intercessor or a witness on the Day of Resurrection, if he was a Muslim."
"11576","Mu'tamir narrated to us from his father, he said: Abu Nadrah informed me from Abu Sa'id that the owner of the dates brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dates, and he disapproved of it. Then he said: Whence is this for you. He said: We bought a sa' for two sa's of our dates. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have dealt in usury."
"11577","Mu'tamir narrated to us from Asim from Shurahbil that Ibn Umar and Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold like for like, and silver for silver like for like, exact for exact. Whoever adds or seeks addition has dealt in usury. Shurahbil said: If I did not hear it, may Allah admit me into the Fire."
"11578","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi narrated to us: Dawud narrated to us from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained, and Jibril came to him and charmed him. Then he said: In the name of Allah I charm you from everything that harms you, from every eye and envier, He heals you, or he said: Allah heals you."
"11579","Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prophet will come on the Day of Resurrection, and with him is a man, and a prophet with him are two men, and more than that. Then his people will be called, and it will be said to them: Did this convey to you. Then they will say: No. Then it will be said to him: Did you convey to your people. Then he will say: Yes. Then it will be said to him: Who witnesses for you. Then he will say: Muhammad and his ummah. Then Muhammad and his ummah will be called, and it will be said to them: Did this convey to his people. Then they will say: Yes. Then it will be said: And what is your knowledge. Then they will say: Our prophet came to us and informed us that the messengers had conveyed. That is His saying: And thus We made you a middle nation. He said: He says: Just, that you be witnesses over people and the Messenger be a witness over you."
"11580","Ibn Numayr narrated to us from al-A'mash from Habib from Abu Artah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing unripe dates and ripe dates, and raisins and dates."
"11581","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Sa'id ibn Masruq informed us from Sumayy from al-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance the Fire from his face by that day seventy autumns."
"11582","Ibn Numayr narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us from Atiyyah al-Awfi from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have left among you what if you hold to it you will not stray after me, the two weighty things, one of them greater than the other, the Book of Allah, a rope extended from heaven to earth, and my progeny, my household. And they will not separate until they come to me at the Hawd."
"11583","Ya'la narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to me, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying in a single garment wrapped."
"11584","Ya'la narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us from Abu Sufyan from Jabir who said: Abu Sa'id narrated to me, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying on a mat."
"11585","Ya'la narrated to us: Idris al-Awdi narrated to us from Amr ibn Murrah from Abu al-Bakhtari from Abu Sa'id, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no zakat in less than five awsaq, and the wasq is sixty sealed measures."
"11586","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Hammad from Ibrahim from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hiring a worker until his wage is made clear to him, and forbade false bidding, and the touch sale, and the throwing of the stone."
"11587","Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Waddak from Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about coitus interruptus. Then he said: Not from all the fluid is the child, and when Allah wills to create from it something, nothing prevents Him."
"11588","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir who said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you finishes his prayer in the mosque, let him make for his house a share of his prayer. Allah will place in his house from his prayer good."
"11589","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Za'idah narrated to us from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you finishes his prayer in the mosque, let him make for his house a share of his prayer, for Allah will place in his house from his prayer good."
"11590","Musa narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir that Abu Sa'id said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you finishes his prayer, then he mentioned its meaning."
"11591","Waki' narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Bishr ibn Harb from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting in fasting, and this sister of mine practices continuous fasting and I forbid her."
"11592","Ishaq ibn Yusuf and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, they said: Sufyan informed us from Ismail ibn Umayyah from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from Yahya ibn Umarah from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity in less than five awsaq of grain or dates, and there is no charity in less than five awaq, and there is no charity in less than five dhawd."
"11593","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us the like of it with its isnad, and he said: fruit, and Abd al-Razzaq said: dates, and he said: Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Thawri from Ismail ibn Umayyah, then he mentioned it."
"11594","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan from al-A'mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa'id from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the heat is intense, delay the prayer, for the intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell."
"11595","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Za'idah from Abd al-Malik from Qaza'ah, freedman of Ziyad, from Abu Sa'id who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no prayer after two prayers, after dawn until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets."
"11596","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Malik from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah, from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no charity in less than five awsuq, nor in five awaq charity, nor in five dhawd charity."
"11597","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us from Sufyan and Shu'bah and Malik from Amr ibn Yahya from his father from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"11598","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Malik narrated to us from Dawud ibn al-Husayn from Abu Sufyan from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muzabanah and muhaqalah. And muzabanah is buying the fruit on the palm tops for dates by measure, and muhaqalah is concerning the renting of land."
"11599","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, my father said, and Abu Salamah, meaning al-Khuza'i, narrated it to us: Malik informed us from Safwan ibn Sulaym from Ata ibn Yasar from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The washing of Friday is obligatory upon every one who has reached puberty."
"11600","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will emerge among you a people, you will deem your prayer insignificant beside their prayer, and your fasting beside their fasting, and your deeds beside their deeds. They recite the Quran, it does not pass their throats. They pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game. He looks at the head and sees nothing, then he looks at the shaft and sees nothing, and he looks at the feathers and sees nothing, and he disputes about the fore-part. Abd al-Rahman said: Malik narrated it to us, meaning this hadith."
"11601","Ismail narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, he said: We were discussing Laylat al-Qadr among a group of Quraysh, so I came to Abu Said al-Khudri, and he was a friend of mine, and I said: Come out with us to the palm groves. So he came out wearing a khamisah of his. I said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mention Laylat al-Qadr. He said: Yes, we observed itikaf with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, during the middle ten of Ramadan, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us on the morning of the twentieth and said: I was shown Laylat al-Qadr then I was made to forget it, or he said: then I forgot it, so seek it in the last ten, in the odd nights, for I saw that I prostrate in water and mud. Whoever observed itikaf with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, let him return. So we returned, and we did not see any trace of cloud in the sky. Then a cloud came and we were rained upon until the roof of the mosque flowed, and it was made of palm branches, and the prayer was established, and I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prostrating in water and mud until I saw the trace of mud on his forehead."
"11602","Ismail narrated to us, Said ibn Yazid informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among your caliphs will be a caliph who scoops up wealth scooping, without counting it."
"11603","Ismail narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about sarf and he said: Hand to hand. I said: Yes. He said: No harm. Then I met Abu Said al-Khudri and told him that I had asked Ibn Abbas about sarf and he said: No harm. He said: Did he really say that. We shall write to him and he will not give you that fatwa. He said: By Allah, some of the young men of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, once brought some dates and he disapproved of them and said: It is as if this is not from the dates of our land. He said: There was some deficiency in our dates this year, so I took this and added some extra. He said: You have doubled, you have dealt in riba. Do not come near this. If anything in your dates causes you doubt, sell it, then buy whatever dates you want."
"11604","Ismail narrated to us, Said informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, he said: No sooner was Khaybar conquered than we, the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fell upon that green plant, garlic, and we ate from it heavily, and people were hungry. Then we went to the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, found the smell and said: Whoever eats anything of this foul plant, let him not come near us in the mosque. So people said: It has been forbidden, it has been forbidden. That reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O people, I have no right to forbid what Allah has made lawful, but it is a plant whose smell I dislike."
"11605","Ismail narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No fatigue afflicts the believer, nor weariness, nor illness, nor grief, nor harm, even worry that weighs upon him, except that Allah expiates thereby some of his sins."
"11606","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar came in to Abu Said, and I was with him, and he said: This man narrated to me a hadith claiming that you narrate it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Did you hear it. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Do not sell gold for gold, nor silver for silver, except like for like, and do not give excess of one over the other, and do not sell anything absent thereof for what is present."
"11607","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from a man, from Abu Said, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Beware of sitting on the road, and perhaps Mamar said: on the elevated paths. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we cannot do without our sittings. He said: Then render its due. They said: And what is its due. He said: Return the greeting, lower the gaze, guide the questioner, enjoin the good and forbid the evil."
"11608","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, once led us in the Asr prayer in the daytime, then stood addressing us until the sun set. He left nothing of what will be until the Day of Resurrection except that he narrated it to us. Whoever remembered it remembered it, and whoever forgot it forgot it. Among what he said was: O people, this world is green and sweet, and Allah has made you stewards in it, so He looks at how you act. So beware of this world and beware of women. Verily every traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection according to his treachery, raised at his buttocks, requited thereby, and there is no traitor greater than a leader of the generality. Then he mentioned character and said: A man may be quick to anger and quick to return, so one offsets the other. And one may be slow to anger and slow to return, so one offsets the other. The best of them are slow to anger and quick to return, and the worst of them are quick to anger and slow to return. He said: Anger is a live coal in the heart of the son of Adam, blazing. Have you not seen the redness of his eyes and the swelling of his jugular veins. If one of you feels that, let him sit down, or he said: let him cling to the ground. He said: Then he mentioned demanding and repaying and said: A man may be good in demanding and bad in repaying, so one offsets the other. And one may be good in repaying and bad in demanding, so one offsets the other. The best of them are good in demanding and good in repaying, and the worst of them are bad in demanding and bad in repaying. Then he said: People are created in ranks. A man is born a believer and lives a believer and dies a believer. And a man is born a disbeliever and lives a disbeliever and dies a disbeliever. And a man is born a believer and lives a believer and dies a disbeliever. And a man is born a disbeliever and lives a disbeliever and dies a believer. Then he said in his hadith: Nothing is better than a word of justice spoken before a tyrannical ruler. Let no fear of people prevent any of you from speaking the truth when he sees it or witnesses it. Then Abu Said wept and said: By Allah, that has indeed prevented us. He said: You complete seventy nations, you are the best of them and the most honored of them to Allah. Then the sun drew near to setting and he said: What remains of this world compared to what has passed of it is like what remains of this day of yours compared to what has passed of it."
"11609","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, he said: I heard Mujalid say: I bear witness concerning Abu al-Waddak that he bore witness concerning Abu Said al-Khudri that he heard him say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people of Paradise will see the people of Illiyyin as you see the brilliant star on the horizon of the sky. Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and how excellent. Ismail ibn Abi Khalid said, while he was sitting with Mujalid on the cushion: And I bear witness concerning Atiyyah al-Awfi that he bore witness concerning Abu Said al-Khudri that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say that."
"11610","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to stone Maiz ibn Malik, we took him out to al-Baqi. By Allah, we neither dug for him nor bound him, but he stood for us and we pelted him with bones and potsherds. Then he complained and ran swiftly until he stood upright for us in the عرض of al-Harrah, and we pelted him with heavy stones of basalt until he fell silent."
"11611","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Mustamirr ibn al-Rayyan al-Zahrani narrated to me, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of perfume is musk."
"11612","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Amr, informed us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Hamzah ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say upon the minbar: What is the matter with people who say that the kinship of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, will not benefit on the Day of Resurrection. By Allah, my kinship remains joined in this world and the Hereafter. And I, O people, am your forerunner at the Hawd."
"11613","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from Qazaah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman shall not travel three except with a dhu rahim."
"11614","Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, my father said: Thus Yahya ibn Adam said, from Qazaah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A woman shall not travel more than two days except with her husband or a mahram of hers. I found this hadith in my father's book in his handwriting, and I think I heard it from him in other places."
"11615","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim al-Naji informed me, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, repeated a verse until morning."
"11616","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Num, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise."
"11617","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Abi Sallam al-Habashi narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Abi Kathir say: I heard Uqbah ibn Abd al-Ghafir say: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: Bilal came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with some dates, and he said: Where did you get this from. He said: I had some inferior dates and I sold them for these. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Oh, the very essence of riba, the very essence of riba. Do not come near it. But sell your dates for whatever you wish, then buy with it whatever seems good to you."
"11618","Yahya ibn Ishaq and Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, they said: Sharik informed us, from Abu Ishaq and Qays ibn Wahb, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said concerning the captives of Awtas: A pregnant woman shall not be approached, Aswad said: until she gives birth, nor one who is not pregnant until she menstruates one menstruation. Yahya said: or seeks clearance by one menstruation."
"11619","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Qazaah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No wisal, meaning in fasting."
"11620","Abu Said and Muawiyah narrated to us, they said: Zaidah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade dates and raisins, and unripe dates and ripe dates. I said to Sulayman: That they be steeped together. He said: Yes."
"11621","Abu Said narrated to us, Abu Aqil narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Said, he said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Most of the food of my family, meaning dabbs. He did not answer him, and he had gone only a short distance when he repeated to him, and he did not answer him. He repeated to him three times, then he said: Allah Almighty cursed, or became angry with, a tribe of the Children of Israel, and they were transformed into beasts. I do not know, perhaps it is some of them. So I neither eat it nor forbid it."
"11622","Hammad al-Khayyat narrated to us, Abd al-Malik al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Said ibn Amr ibn Sulaym, from a man of his people called Fulan ibn Muawiyah, or Muawiyah ibn Fulan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The dead person knows who washes him and carries him and lowers him. He said: So I rose from Abu Said to Ibn Umar and told him. Then Abu Said passed by, and Ibn Umar said to him: From whom did you hear this hadith. He said: From the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"11623","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, al-Dahhak, meaning Ibn Uthman, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man shall not look at the nakedness of a man, nor shall a woman look at the nakedness of a woman, nor shall a man lie with a man in one garment, nor shall a woman lie with a woman in one garment."
"11624","Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, al-Dahhak narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Ibn Muhayriz al-Shami, that he heard Abu Sirmah al-Mazini and Abu Said al-Khudri say: We took captives in the raid of Banu al-Mustaliq, and it is the raid in which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gained Juwayriyah. Some of us wanted to take wives, and some of us wanted to enjoy and sell. So we reconsidered about azl and mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: It does not matter if you do not practice azl, for Allah has decreed whatever He will create until the Day of Resurrection."
"11625","Rawh narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The believers will be saved from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection and detained upon a bridge between Paradise and Hell. Then retaliation will be exacted for some of them from others for wrongs that were between them in this world, until when they are refined and purified, they are permitted to enter Paradise. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, one of them will be better guided to his dwelling in Paradise than he was to his dwelling in this world."
"11626","Sayyar narrated to us, Jafar narrated to us, al-Mualla ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Bashir al-Muzani narrated to us, and he was, by Allah, as far as I knew, brave in battle and weeping at remembrance, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: I was in a circle of the Ansar, so much so that some of us screened others from nakedness, and a reciter of ours was reciting to us, and we were listening to the Book of Allah, when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stopped by us and sat among us in order to count himself with them. The reciter fell silent. He said: What were you saying. We said: O Messenger of Allah, a reciter of ours was reciting to us the Book of Allah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, motioned with his hand, circling with it, gesturing to them to form a circle. So the circle rounded. I did not see the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recognize anyone among them except me. He said: Then he said: Rejoice, O company of the poor. You will enter Paradise before the rich by half a day, and that is five hundred years."
"11627","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal informed us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man of my nation will intercede for a multitude of people, and they will enter Paradise by his intercession. And a man will intercede for a tribe of people, and they will enter Paradise by his intercession. And a man will intercede for a man and his household, and they will enter Paradise by his intercession."
"11628","Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, Fulayh informed us, and Surayj said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Thabit, from his father, he said: Ibn Umar passed by me and I said: From where have you come early, Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: To Abu Said al-Khudri. So I set out with him. Abu Said said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I forbade you the meat of sacrifices and storing it after three days, so eat and store, for Allah has brought relief. And I forbade you certain drinks and nabidhs, so drink, and every intoxicant is unlawful. And I forbade you visiting graves, but if you visit them, do not speak foul."
"11629","Hashim ibn al-Qasim and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abu Salih, Bahz said: al-Samman, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: When one of you prays, Bahz said: toward something screening him from people, and someone wants to pass in front of him, let him repel him in his chest. If he refuses, let him fight him, for he is but a devil."
"11630","Hashim narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Said, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Do not revile my companions. If one of you spent the like of Uhud in gold, it would not reach the mudd of one of them, nor half of it."
"11631","Hashim narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, Shahr narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri, and prayer at al-Tur was mentioned in his presence, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A riding beast should not have its saddles bound for a mosque in which prayer is sought other than the Sacred Mosque, and al-Masjid al-Aqsa, and this mosque of mine. And a woman who has entered Islam should not leave her house traveling except with a husband or with a mahram of hers. And prayer should not be in two hours of the day: after the Fajr prayer until the sun has moved on, and not after the Asr prayer until the sun sets. And fasting should not be on two days of the year: the day of Fitr from Ramadan, and the day of Nahr."
"11632","He said: Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sharfa, freedman of Abdullah ibn Umar, narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is between my grave and my minbar is a garden of the gardens of Paradise."
"11633","My father said: Ishaq ibn Sharfa, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated from him, Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, and Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad said: Ishaq ibn Sharfa."
"11634","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will be two factions in my nation. Renegades will emerge between them, and the one of them closer to the truth will undertake killing them."
"11635","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then he mentioned the like of it."
"11636","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Sulayman al-Aswad narrated to us, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said, that a man came after the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had prayed, and he said: Will no man give charity to this one and pray with him."
"11637","Affan narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Mabad ibn Sirin, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: People will emerge from the east reciting the Quran, it will not pass their collarbones. They will shoot out of the religion as the arrow shoots out of the target, then they will not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch. It was said: What is their mark. He said: Their mark is shaving and close cropping."
"11638","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah and Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hospitality is three days. Whatever is after that is charity."
"11639","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Khulayd ibn Jafar, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Every traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection at his buttocks."
"11640","Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Utbah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The House will surely be hajjed and umrahed after the emergence of Yajuj and Majuj."
"11641","Affan narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Num, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise, and Fatimah is the mistress of their women, except what belonged to Maryam daughter of Imran."
"11642","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that a Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have camels and I wish to emigrate, so what do you command me. He said: Do you grant use of them. He said: Yes. He said: And do you pay their zakah. He said: Yes. He said: And do you milk them on the day of their watering. He said: Yes. He said: Go and work beyond the seas, for Allah will not diminish anything of your work. The matter of emigration is weighty."
"11643","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, Umarah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Thunderbolts will increase as the Hour approaches, until a man comes to a people and says: Who was struck this morning. They say: So-and-so and so-and-so were struck."
"11644","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and al-Dahhak al-Mashriqi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was one day distributing wealth, Dhu al-Khuwaysirah came to him, a man of Banu Tamim, and said: O Muhammad, be just, for by Allah you have not been just since today. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Allah, you will not find after me one more just to you than me, three times. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, will you permit me to strike his neck. He said: No, for he has companions. One of you would belittle his prayer beside their prayer and his fasting beside their fasting. They shoot out of the religion as the arrow shoots out of the target. Its owner looks at its notch and sees nothing. Their sign is a man, one of whose hands is like a lump of flesh, or like the breast of a woman. They emerge against two parties of people. The party of the two closer to Allah will kill them. Abu Said said: I bear witness that I heard this from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and that I witnessed Ali when he killed them. They searched among the slain and found him with the description the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had described."
"11645","Muhammad ibn Rabiah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Atiyyah al-Awfi, narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the wailing woman and the one who listens."
"11646","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, Bishr ibn Harb narrated to us, I heard Abu Said al-Khudri narrate, he said: We raided with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Fadak and Khaybar. He said: Allah granted His Messenger victory over Fadak and Khaybar, and people fell upon a green plant of theirs, this garlic and onion. He said: They went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he found its smell and was offended by it. Then the people returned, and he said: Verily do not eat it. Whoever eats any of it, let him not come near our gathering. He said: And on the day of Khaybar people fell upon the meat of domestic donkeys and set up the pots, and I set up my pot among those who set up. That reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: I forbid you it, I forbid you it, twice. So the pots were overturned, and I overturned my pot among those who overturned."
"11647","Yunus and Surayj narrated to us, they said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Harith, from Abu Salamah, he said: Abu Hurayrah used to narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: In Friday there is an hour which no Muslim coincides with while he is in prayer asking Allah for good except that He gives it to him. He said: And Abu Hurayrah made it seem brief with his hand. He said: When Abu Hurayrah died, I said: By Allah, if I went to Abu Said and asked him about this hour, perhaps he would have some knowledge of it. So I came to him and found him straightening palm stalks. I said: O Abu Said, what are these stalks that I see you straightening. He said: These are stalks in which Allah has placed blessing for us. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to love them and lean upon them. So we would straighten them and bring them to him. Then he saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque, and in his hand was a stalk of those stalks, so he scraped it and said: When one of you is in his prayer, let him not spit before him, for his Lord is before him. Let him spit to his left or under his foot. If he does not, Surayj said: find a spittoon, then in his garment or his sandal. He said: Then the sky clouded over that night. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out for the last Isha prayer, lightning flashed, and he saw Qatadah ibn al-Numan and said: What is the night journey, O Qatadah. He said: I knew, O Messenger of Allah, that those attending the prayer are few, so I wished to attend it. He said: When you have prayed, remain until I pass by you. When he finished, he gave him the stalk and said: Take this, it will light ten before you and ten behind you. When you enter the house and discern a black shape in the corner of the house, strike it before it speaks, for it is a devil. He said: So he did. So we love these stalks for that. He said: I said: O Abu Said, Abu Hurayrah narrated to us about the hour that is on Friday. Do you have any knowledge of it. He said: I asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about it, and he said: I had been informed of it, then I was made to forget it as Laylat al-Qadr was made forgotten. He said: Then I left him and went in to Abdullah ibn Salam."
"11648","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Upon every adult is ghusl on Friday, and let him wear of his good clothes, and if he has perfume let him touch of it."
"11649","Yunus narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Amrah, she is the daughter of Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad ibn Zurarah al-Ansariyyah, that Aishah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was told that Abu Said al-Khudri gives fatwa that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is not right for a woman to travel except with a mahram of hers."
"11650","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Thabit, he said: My father narrated to me that Abdullah ibn Umar passed by him and said to him: Where are you heading, Abu Abd al-Rahman. He said: I intended Abu Said al-Khudri. So I set out with him. He said: Ibn Umar said: O Abu Said, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid the meat of sacrifices, and certain drinks, and visiting graves, and it has reached me that you narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning that. Abu Said said: My two ears heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he says: I forbade you eating the meat of sacrifices after three, so eat and store, for Allah has brought relief. And I forbade you certain drinks, or nabidhs, so drink, and every intoxicant is unlawful. And I forbade you visiting graves, but if you visit them, do not speak foul."
"11651","Yunus narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, we would inform him of whoever of our dead was present, and he would come to him before he died, attend him, seek forgiveness for him, and await his death. He said: That would sometimes detain him a long detention, and it burdened him. He said: So we said: It is gentler to the Messenger of Allah not to inform him of the dead until he dies. He said: So when one of our dead died, we would inform him of him, and he would come among his family, seek forgiveness for him and pray over him. Then if it seemed good to him to witness his burial, he would await witnessing it, and if it seemed good to him to leave, he would leave. He said: We remained upon that for another period. He said: So we said: It is gentler to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to carry our dead to his house, and not displace him nor burden him. He said: So we did that, and such was the matter."
"11652","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Ali, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ibn Said: What do you see. He said: I see a throne upon the sea with snakes around it. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He sees the throne of Iblis."
"11653","And Muammal narrated it to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir."
"11654","Yunus and Surayj narrated to us, they said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Damrah ibn Said, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade two prayers, and fasting two days, and two kinds of wearing: prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and after Fajr until the sun rises. And he forbade fasting the day of the two Eids. And wrapping in one garment, and that a man sit with knees drawn up in a single garment. Yunus said in his hadith: with nothing over his private parts. And Surayj said in his hadith: from fasting the day of Adha and the day of Fitr."
"11655","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade two kinds of wearing and two kinds of sale: limas and nibadh."
"11656","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Abu al-Alaniyah Muslim, he said: I asked Abu Said al-Khudri about nabidh of the jar, and he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade nabidh of the jar. I said: And the hollowed trunk. He said: That is more evil and more evil."
"11657","Yazid narrated to us, Dawud informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of dabbs, so what do you command us. He said: It has reached me that a nation of the Children of Israel was transformed into beasts, and I do not know which beasts they are. He said: So he neither commanded nor forbade."
"11658","Yazid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt, equal for equal, like for like. Whoever increases or seeks increase has dealt in riba. Taker and giver are alike."
"11659","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Abu Said al-Khudri, and from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Ansar. If people took a valley or a pass, and the Ansar took a valley or a pass, I would take the valley of the Ansar and their pass."
"11660","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad informed us, and Muhammad ibn Ubayd said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Utbah, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid fasting two days, and two prayers, and two marriages. I heard him forbid prayer after Subh until the sun rises, and after Asr until the sun sets, and fasting the day of Fitr and Adha, and joining a woman and her maternal aunt, and a woman and her paternal aunt."
"11661","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade muhaqalah and muzabanah."
"11662","Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Umar ibn al-Hakam ibn Thawban, that Abu Said al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent Alqamah ibn Mujazziz on an expedition, I among them, until we reached the head of our raid, or we were on part of the road. He permitted a party of the army and put over them Abdullah ibn Hudhafah ibn Qays al-Sahmi, and he was of the men of Badr, and there was in him playfulness, meaning jest. I was among those who returned with him. We halted on part of the road. He said: The people kindled a fire to prepare upon it something of theirs, or to warm themselves. He said: He said to them: Do I not have over you hearing and obedience. They said: Yes. He said: Whatever I command you, if you do it. They said: Yes. He said: I adjure you by my right and your obedience to leap into this fire. Some people stood and girded themselves, until when he thought they would leap, he said: Restrain yourselves, I was only joking with you. They mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, after they came, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever of them commands you to disobedience, do not obey him."
"11663","Yazid narrated to us, Said informed us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, that Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to them that a servant of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, once brought him fresh dates, while the dates of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, were unirrigated, containing dryness. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whence this dates for you. He said: This is a sa which we bought with two sas of our dates. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not do it, for this is not proper. But sell your dates and buy of whatever dates you wish."
"11664","Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Flogging was inflicted in the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for wine with two sandals, forty. When it was the time of Umar, a lash was flogged in place of each sandal."
"11665","Yazid and Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, Yazid said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade bending the mouths of waterskins. Abu al-Nadr said: That drink be taken from their mouths."
"11666","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said ibn Khalid, he said: I came in to Abu Salamah, and he brought us butter and a lump, and a fly fell into the food. Abu Salamah began to dip it with his finger into it. I said: O uncle, what are you doing. He said: Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: In one of the two wings of the fly is poison, and in the other is cure. When it falls into food, dip it, for it puts forward the poison and delays the cure."
"11667","Yazid and Hajjaj narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, from al-Maqburi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, he said: We were detained on the day of al-Khandaq until a long part of the night had gone, until we were sufficed, and that is the saying of Allah: And Allah sufficed the believers in fighting, and Allah is Strong, Mighty. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called Bilal and commanded him, and he gave the iqamah, and he prayed Zuhr, doing it well as he would pray it in its time. Then he gave the iqamah for Asr and prayed it likewise. Then he gave the iqamah for Maghrib and prayed it likewise. Then he gave the iqamah for Isha and prayed it likewise. That was before there came down concerning the fear prayer. Hajjaj said: Concerning the fear prayer: But if you fear, on foot or mounted."
"11668","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from his brother Mabad ibn Sirin, he said: I said to Abu Said al-Khudri: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning azl. He said: Yes, we asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about azl, and he said: And what is it. We said: A man has a nursing wife, he has intercourse with her and dislikes that she conceive, so he practices azl from her. And he has a slave girl, he has no wealth besides her, he has intercourse with her and dislikes that she conceive, so he practices azl from her. He said: It does not matter if you do not do it, for it is but decree."
"11669","Yazid narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Khulayd ibn Jafar and al-Mustamirr, they said: We heard Abu Nadrah narrate from Abu Said al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned a woman of the Children of Israel who stuffed her ring with musk, and musk is the best of perfume."
"11670","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, my father said: And Ishaq narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Ibn Muhayriz, that he said: I entered the mosque and saw Abu Said al-Khudri, so I sat with him and asked him about azl. Abu Said said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the raid of Banu al-Mustaliq, and we took captives of the Arabs. We desired women, and celibacy bore hard upon us, and we loved azl and wished to practice azl, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was among us, before we asked him. So we asked him about that, and he said: It does not matter if you do not do it. There is no soul to be until the Day of Resurrection except that it will be."
"11671","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from his father, from Ibn Abi Num, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Ali, while in Yemen, sent to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a nugget of gold in its dust. He divided it between al-Aqra ibn Habis al-Hanzali, then one of Banu Mujashi, and between Uyaynah ibn Badr al-Fazari, and between Alqamah ibn Ulathah al-Amiri, then one of Banu Kilab, and between Zayd al-Khayr al-Tai, then one of Banu Nabhan. He said: Quraysh and the Ansar became angry and said: He gives the chiefs of Najd and leaves us. He said: I only conciliate them. He said: A man came forward, deep-eyed, prominent-browed, thick-bearded, high-cheeked, shaven. He said: He said: O Muhammad, fear Allah. He said: Who obeys Allah if I disobey Him. Does He trust me with the people of the earth and you do not trust me. He said: A man of the people asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to kill him, I think Khalid ibn al-Walid, and he prevented him. When he turned away, he said: From the offspring of this are a people who recite the Quran, it does not pass their throats. They shoot out of Islam as the arrow shoots out of the target. They kill the people of Islam and leave the people of idols. If I reach them, I shall surely kill them as Ad were killed."
"11672","Surayj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade hiring a worker until his wage is made clear, and najsh, and lams, and casting the stone."
"11673","Surayj narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that Darraj Abu al-Samh narrated to him, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The truest of dreams are at dawn."
"11674","And with this isnad that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When you see a man frequenting the mosque, testify for him with faith. Allah Almighty said: Only those maintain the mosques of Allah who believe in Allah and the Last Day."
"11675","And with this isnad that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Lord Almighty will say on the Day of Resurrection: The people of the gathering shall know who are the people of generosity. It was said: And who are the people of generosity, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Gatherings of remembrance in the mosques."
"11676","And with this isnad that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Remember Allah much until they say: Mad."
"11677","Yunus and Surayj narrated to us, they said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Habib, from Abu al-Muthanna al-Juhani, he said: I heard Marwan asking Abu Said al-Khudri: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid breathing while drinking in his vessel. Abu Said said: Yes. A man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I am not quenched with one breath. He said: When you breathe, remove the water from your face. He said: I see a speck and I blow it away. He said: When you see it, pour it out and do not blow it."
"11678","Ismail ibn Muhammad, meaning Abu Ibrahim al-Muaqqib, narrated to us, Marwan, meaning Ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari, narrated to us, Umar ibn Hamzah al-Umari narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad, freedman of the family of Abu Said, narrated to us, I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the greatest of trusts with Allah on the Day of Resurrection is a man who is intimate with his wife and she is intimate with him, then he spreads her secret."
"11679","Surayj narrated to us, Abu Layla narrated to us, my father said: Surayj named him Abdullah ibn Maysarah al-Khurasani, from Attab al-Bakri, he said: We would sit with Abu Said al-Khudri in Medina, and I asked him about the seal of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that was between his shoulders. He said with his forefinger: Thus, a protruding piece of flesh between his shoulders, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"11680","Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ali ibn Ali, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he opened the prayer, would say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, and blessed is Your name, and exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god but You."
"11681","Abu al-Ala al-Hasan ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Khalid, meaning Ibn Yazid, from Said, from Abu Bakr ibn al-Munkadir, that Amr ibn Sulaym informed him, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Said, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Ghusl on Friday is upon every adult, and the siwak, and that he touch of perfume what he can."
"11682","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Shurahbil, from Abu Said, freedman of al-Mahri, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever endures in Medina its hardship and severity, I shall be for him an intercessor on the Day of Resurrection."
"11683","Abu Ibrahim al-Muaqqib, Ismail ibn Muhammad, and he was one of the righteous, narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir informed me, he said: I came in to Jabir ibn Abdullah while he was dying, and I said to him: Convey to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, greeting from me."
"11684","Harun, he is Ibn Maruf, narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no forbearing one except one with a slip, and no wise one except one with experience."
"11685","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah informed us, and Attab said: Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah narrated to me that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbid bending the mouths of waterskins."
"11686","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Mawal, freedman of the family of Ali, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah narrated to us, he said: There was a funeral in al-Hijr, and Abu Said came, and they made room for him, but he refused to advance, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of sittings are the widest of them."
"11687","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Uqbah ibn Abd al-Ghafir, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man of those before you, Allah had granted him wealth and children. When death came to him, he summoned his sons and said: What sort of father was I to you. They said: An excellent father. He said: By Allah, he never stored any good with Allah at all. When I die, burn me, until when I am charcoal, crush me, then scatter me on a day, meaning a violently windy day. He said: And the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He took their pledges upon that, by my Lord. So they did, by my Lord. When he died, they burned him, until when he was charcoal, they crushed him, then scattered him on a windy day. His Lord said: Be, and behold he was a man standing. His Lord said to him: What carried you to what you did. He said: My Lord, fear of Your punishment. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, nothing met him but that Allah forgave him. al-Hasan once said: Nothing met him but that Allah forgave him. Qatadah said: A man feared the punishment of Allah, and Allah saved him by his fear."
"11688","al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Harun al-Abdi and Matar al-Warraq, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The earth will be filled with tyranny and injustice. Then a man of my progeny will emerge, ruling seven or nine. He will fill the earth with equity and justice."
"11689","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Verily every traitor will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection according to his treachery. Verily there is no treachery greater than that of a leader of the generality."
"11690","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Said al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah, they said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The last to emerge from the Fire are two men. Allah says to one of them: O son of Adam, what did you prepare for this day. Did you do good or hope in Me. He says: No, my Lord. So he is ordered to the Fire, and he is the most regretful of the people of the Fire. And He says to the other: O son of Adam, what did you prepare for this day. Did you do good or hope in Me. He says: Yes, my Lord, I used to hope, when You brought me out, that You would never return me to it. Then a tree is raised for him, and he says: My Lord, settle me under this tree, that I may shade in its shade and eat of its fruit and drink of its water. He says: O son of Adam. So He takes his pledge that he will not ask Him for other than it. So He brings him near it. Then a tree is raised for him, better than the first and more abundant in water, and he says: My Lord, this, I shall not ask You for other than it. Settle me under it, that I may shade in its shade and eat of its fruit and drink of its water. He says: O son of Adam, did you not pledge to me that you would not ask Me for other than it. He says: My Lord, this, I shall not ask You for other than it. So He settles him under it and takes his pledge that he will not ask Him for other than it. Then a tree is raised for him at the gate of Paradise, better than the first two and more abundant in water, and he says: My Lord, I shall not ask You for other than it. So settle me under it, that I may shade in its shade and eat of its fruit and drink of its water. He says: Son of Adam, did you not pledge to me that you would not ask Me for other than it. He says: My Lord, this, I shall not ask You for other than it. So He settles him under it and takes his pledge that he will not ask Him for other than it. Then he hears the voices of the people of Paradise and cannot restrain himself, and says: My Lord, admit me to Paradise. He, Blessed and Exalted, says: Ask and wish. And Allah prompts him with what he has no knowledge of. So he asks and wishes to the extent of three days of the days of this world. He says: Son of Adam, yours is what you asked. Abu Said al-Khudri said: And the like of it with it. Abu Hurayrah said: And ten the like of it with it. Then one of them said to his companion: Narrate what you heard, and I shall narrate what I heard."
"11691","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Aflah al-Ansari, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Love of the Ansar is faith, and hatred of them is hypocrisy."
"11692","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on Friday, and a Bedouin entered while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was upon the minbar. The Bedouin sat at the back of the people. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Did you pray two rakahs. He said: No. He said: So he commanded him, and he went to the courtyard that is by the minbar and prayed two rakahs."
"11693","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, from Hanash ibn Abdullah, that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, once led us in prayer and found the smell of garlic from a man. When he finished, he said to him: Let one of you go and eat of this foul thing, then come and harm us."
"11694","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Hubayrah, from Hanash, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in prayer, then he mentioned it."
"11695","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said, Like molten metal. He said: Like the dregs of oil. When it is brought near him, the skin of his face falls into it."
"11696","Hasan narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Luhayah, he said: Darraj Abu al-Samh narrated to us that Abu al-Haytham narrated to him, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that a man said to him: O Messenger of Allah, blessed is he who saw you and believed in you. He said: Blessed is he who saw me and believed in me, then blessed, then blessed, then blessed is he who believed in me and did not see me. A man said to him: And what is Tuba. He said: A tree in Paradise, a journey of a hundred years. The garments of the people of Paradise come out of its sheaths."
"11697","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, Darraj narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Remember Allah much until they say: Mad."
"11698","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: Abu Nadrah narrated to me that Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about Witr and said: Perform Witr before Fajr."
"11699","Hasan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade hiring a worker until his wage is made clear to him, and casting the stone, and lams, and najsh."
"11700","Affan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, he said: We left Medina shouting with Hajj, shouting. When we came to Mecca, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Make it Umrah, except whoever has the sacrificial animal with him. When it was the evening of al-Tarwiyah, we entered ihram for Hajj."
"11701","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Hasan, that Abu Said al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not fear of people prevent a man from upholding the truth when he knows it. He said: Then Abu Said wept and said: By Allah, we have witnessed it and we did not uphold it."
"11702","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten nights of Ramadan, on the ninth remaining, and the seventh remaining, and the fifth remaining, and the third remaining."
"11703","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: I heard Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf narrating from Abu Said, that when the people of Qurayzah came down to the judgment of Sad ibn Muadh, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for him, and he came on a donkey, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand for your chief, or for your best one. And he said: These people have come down to your judgment. He said: I judge that their fighters be killed and their offspring be taken captive. He said: You have judged with the judgment of the King."
"11704","Affan narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr informed me, he said: I asked Qazah, the freedman of Ziyad, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: Four things I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they pleased me and delighted me. He said: No woman shall travel a journey of two days or two nights except with her husband or a mahram; and two days shall not be fasted, the day of al-Fitr and the day of al-Nahr; and no prayer after two prayers, after al-Subh until the sun rises, and after al-Asr until the sun sets; and saddles shall not be tied except to three mosques: al-Masjid al-Haram, and Masjid al-Aqsa, and this mosque of mine."
"11705","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade steeping unripe dates and ripe dates together, and raisins and dates together."
"11706","Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Qatadah informed us, from Abdillah ibn Abi Utbah, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a virgin in her chamber, and when he disliked something we recognized it in his face."
"11707","Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the nineteenth or seventeenth of Ramadan, and some fasted and some broke the fast, and neither did these criticize these nor these criticize these."
"11708","Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Anas ibn Sirin narrated to me, from his brother Mabad ibn Sirin, from Abu Said al-Khudri. Shubah said: I said to him: Did you hear it from Abu Said? He said: Yes, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning withdrawal: There is no harm upon you if you do not do it, for it is only the decree."
"11709","Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, he said: I heard Dhakwan narrating from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The women said: O Messenger of Allah, the men have dominated you, so promise us an appointment. So he promised them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman among you who sends forth three of her children, they will be for her a veil from the Fire. A woman said: O Messenger of Allah, I have sent forth two. He said: And two."
"11710","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man killed ninety-nine souls, then asked about the most learned of the people of the earth, and was directed to a man, and came to him and said: He killed ninety-nine souls, is there repentance for him? He said: He has killed ninety-nine souls, so there is no repentance for him. He said: So he drew his sword and killed him, completing one hundred. Then he remained as long as Allah willed, then asked about the most learned of the people of the earth, and was directed to a man, and said: He has killed one hundred souls, is there repentance for him? He said: And who stands between him and repentance? Leave the evil village you are in for such-and-such village, and worship your Lord therein. He said: So he left, and his appointed term met him, and the angels of punishment and the angels of mercy disputed concerning him. Iblis said: He did not disobey me for a single hour ever. The angels of mercy said: He left repentant. Humayd claimed that Bakr narrated to him from Abu Rafi, he said: So Allah sent an angel, and they referred their dispute to him. The narration returns to the narration of Qatadah. He said: Look to which of the two villages he was nearer, and join him to it. Qatadah said: So Allah brought the righteous village near to him and distanced the evil village from him, and they joined him to its people."
"11711","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban narrated to me, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Abu Said al-Khudri, concerning the raid of Bani al-Mustaliq, that they took captives and wanted to enjoy them without them becoming pregnant, so they asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: There is no harm upon you if you do not do it, for Allah has written whomever He will create until the Day of Resurrection."
"11712","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Fulayh narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of you doubts in his prayer and does not know how much he prayed, let him build upon certainty, until when he is certain he has completed, let him prostrate two prostrations before he greets. For if his prayer was odd it becomes even, and if it was even that is humiliation for Satan."
"11713","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of the highest ranks, those beneath them will see them as you see the star in the horizon of the sky. And Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and how excellent."
"11714","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Uthman al-Batti, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We took women from the captives of Awtas, and they had husbands, and we disliked to fall upon them while they had husbands, so we asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this verse was revealed: And married women except those your right hands possess. He said: So we deemed their private parts lawful thereby."
"11715","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no man who believes in Allah and His Messenger hate the Ansar."
"11716","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Sufyan informed us, from his father, from Ibn Abi Num, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Ali sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was in Yemen, a nugget of gold in its soil, and he divided it among al-Aqra ibn Habis al-Hanzali, then of Bani Mujashi, and Uyaynah ibn Badr al-Fazari, and Alqamah ibn Ulathah al-Amiri, then of Bani Kilab, and Zayd al-Khayr al-Tai, then of Bani Nabhan. Then he mentioned the hadith."
"11717","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Fudayl, meaning Ibn Marzuq, narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that a man asked him about washing the head, and he said: Three handfuls or three scoops suffice you. Then he joined his hands. Then he said: O Abu Said, I am a man of much hair. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had more hair than you and better."
"11718","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Sufyan informed us, from his father, from Ibn Abi Num, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Ali sent to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was in Yemen, a nugget of gold in its soil, and he divided it among al-Aqra ibn Habis al-Hanzali, then of Bani Mujashi, and Uyaynah ibn Badr al-Fazari, and Alqamah ibn Ulathah al-Amiri, then of Bani Kilab, and Zayd al-Khayr al-Tai, then of Bani Nabhan. He said: So Quraysh and the Ansar became angry and said: He gives the chiefs of Najd and leaves us. He said: I only conciliate them. He said: Then a man came forward, sunken-eyed, prominent-foreheaded, thick-bearded, high-cheeked, shaven-headed. He said: O Muhammad, fear Allah. He said: Who obeys Allah if I disobey Him? He trusts me with the people of the earth and you do not trust me. He said: Then a man of the people asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to kill him, I think it was Khalid ibn al-Walid, and he prevented him. When he turned away he said: From the offspring of this one are a people who recite the Quran and it does not pass their throats. They pass through Islam as the arrow passes through the prey. They kill the people of Islam and leave the people of idols. If I were to reach them I would kill them as Ad were killed."
"11719","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: How can I enjoy when the holder of the Trumpet has seized the Trumpet and bent his forehead and inclined his hearing, waiting when he will be commanded."
"11720","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Sufyan informed us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Yahya ibn Umarah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sadaqah in grain nor dates until it reaches five awsaq, and no sadaqah in less than five dhawd, and no sadaqah in less than five awaqi."
"11721","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Sufyan informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam: Iyad ibn Abdillah ibn Sad ibn Abi Sarh narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We used to give Sadaqat al-Fitr at the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a sa of barley, a sa of dates, a sa of raisins, a sa of dried yogurt. When Muawiyah came, Samra wheat came, and he deemed a mudd equal to two mudds."
"11722","Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Sufyan informed us, from Zubayd, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you belittle himself to see a matter of Allah requiring a statement and not speak concerning it. Then it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: What prevented you from saying concerning such-and-such? And he will say: Fear of people. And He will say: I was more deserving to be feared."
"11723","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to me, from Nafi, the freedman of Ibn Umar: Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sell gold for gold except like for like, none of it exceeding the other, and do not sell silver for silver except like for like, none of it exceeding the other, and do not sell absent for present."
"11724","Waki narrated to us: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Ata or Atiyyah, from Abu Said, and from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on his mount in voluntary prayer wherever it turned with him, gesturing, and making the prostration lower than the bowing. Abdillah said: And the correct is Atiyyah."
"11725","Waki narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prayer after al-Fajr until the sun rises, and none after al-Asr until it sets."
"11726","Muhammad ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not thank people does not thank Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"11727","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf narrated to me, he said: I went to Abu Said al-Khudri. He said: I said: Will you not go out with us to the palm grove to talk? He said: So he went out. He said: I said: Narrate to me what you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say concerning Laylat al-Qadr. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) observed itikaf in the first ten of Ramadan, and we observed itikaf with him. Then Jibril came to him and said: What you seek is ahead of you. When it was the morning of the twentieth of Ramadan, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood as a preacher and said: Whoever observed itikaf with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), let him return, for I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, and it is in the last ten of Ramadan, on an odd night. And I was made to forget it. And I saw as if I prostrated in clay and water. He said: And we saw nothing in the sky. Hammam said: I think he said: a patch, he named the cloud by a name. Then a cloud came, and the roof of the mosque was palm fronds, and we were rained upon. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us, and I saw the trace of clay and water on the forehead of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his nose, confirming his vision."
"11728","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the sixteenth of Ramadan, and among us were those who fasted and among us were those who broke the fast. The fasting did not criticize the breaking, nor did the breaking criticize the fasting."
"11729","Affan narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us concerning this verse: And We removed what was in their breasts of malice. He said: Qatadah narrated to us that Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji narrated to them that Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to them, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believers are cleared from the Fire and detained on a bridge between Paradise and the Fire. Then retaliation is taken for some of them from others for wrongs that were between them in the world, until when they are refined and purified they are permitted to enter Paradise. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, one of them is better guided to his dwelling in Paradise than to his dwelling he had in the world. Qatadah said: And some of them said: They are resembled only to the people of Friday when they dispersed from their Friday."
"11730","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sadaqah in less than five dhawd, nor in less than five awaqi, nor in less than five awsaq."
"11731","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Said al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last two men to come out of the Fire, Allah says to one of them: O son of Adam, what have you prepared for this Day? Did you do any good ever? Did you hope in Me? And he says: No, my Lord. Then he is ordered to the Fire, and he is the most regretful of the people of the Fire. And He says to the other: O son of Adam, what have you prepared for this Day? Did you do any good ever, or hope in Me? And he says: No, my Lord, except that I used to hope in You. He said: Then a tree is raised for him, and he says: My Lord, settle me under this tree, that I may shade in its shade and eat from its fruit and drink from its water. And he covenants to Him that he will not ask Him for other than it. So He settles him under it. Then a tree better than the first and more abundant in water is raised for him, and he says: My Lord, settle me under it, I will not ask You for other than it, that I may shade in its shade and eat from its fruit and drink from its water. And He says: O son of Adam, did you not covenant to Me that you would not ask Me for other than it? And he says: My Lord, this one, I will not ask You for other than it. And he covenants to Him that he will not ask Him for other than it. So He settles him under it. Then a tree at the gate of Paradise, better than the first two and more abundant in water, is raised for him, and he says: My Lord, this one, settle me under it. So He brings him near to it, and he covenants to Him that he will not ask Him for other than it. Then he hears the voices of the people of Paradise and cannot restrain himself, and says: My Lord, Paradise, my Lord, admit me to Paradise. And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Ask and wish. So he asks Him and wishes for the measure of three days of the days of the world, and Allah prompts him with what he has no knowledge of. So he asks and wishes, and when he finishes He says: For you is what you asked. Abu Said said: And the like of it with it. And Abu Hurayrah said: And ten times its like with it. One of them said to his companion: Narrate what you heard, and I will narrate what I heard."
"11732","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Dawud narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, or from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shouting loudly for Hajj. When we circumambulated the House he said: Make it Umrah. When the day of al-Tarwiyah came we entered ihram for Hajj."
"11733","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Dawud narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, or from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained, and Jibril came to him and said: In the name of Allah I incant you, from everything that harms you, from every envier and eye; Allah heals you."
"11734","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Darraj narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Every word in the Quran in which qunut is mentioned, it is obedience."
"11735","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Darraj narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Wayl is a valley in Jahannam into which the disbeliever falls forty autumns before reaching its bottom. And al-Saud is a mountain of fire up which he climbs seventy autumns, falling thereby likewise therein forever."
"11736","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Darraj narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Increase in the lasting righteous deeds. It was said: And what are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Millah. It was said: And what is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Millah. It was said: And what is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Millah. It was said: And what is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Takbir and tahlil and tasbih and tahmid, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah."
"11737","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Darraj narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The disbeliever will be established on the Day of Resurrection for the measure of fifty thousand years as if he had not worked in the world. And the disbeliever will see Jahannam and think it will befall him from a journey of forty years."
"11738","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Darraj narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man will recline in Paradise seventy years before he moves. Then his wife comes to him and strikes his shoulder, and he looks at his face in her cheek, clearer than the mirror. And the least pearl upon her lights what is between the east and the west. And she greets him. He said: So he returns the greeting and asks her: Who are you? And she says: I am of the increase. And upon her will be seventy garments, the least of them like al-Numan from Tuba, and his sight penetrates them until he sees the marrow of her leg from behind that. And upon her are crowns, the least pearl upon which lights what is between the east and the west."
"11739","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Darraj narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Winter is the spring of the believer."
"11740","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Darraj narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A day whose measure is fifty thousand years, how long is this day? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, it is lightened for the believer until it is lighter for him than a prescribed prayer he prays in the world."
"11741","And from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Gatherings are three: safe, gaining, and perishing."
"11742","And from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: And raised couches. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, its height is as between the heaven and the earth, and what is between the heaven and the earth is a journey of five hundred years."
"11743","And with this isnad, that he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which servants are best in rank with Allah on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Those who remember Allah much. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, and the warrior in the path of Allah? He said: If he struck with his sword among the disbelievers and idolaters until it broke and was dyed with blood, those who remember Allah would be better than him in rank."
"11744","And with this isnad, he said: A man migrated to the Messenger of Allah from Yemen, and the Messenger of Allah said to him: You have abandoned shirk, but it is jihad. Are your parents in Yemen? He said: Yes. He said: Did they permit you? He said: No. And the Messenger of Allah said to him: Return to your parents and seek their permission. If they do, otherwise honor them."
"11745","And with this isnad, from the Messenger of Allah, that he said: The Lord, Mighty and Majestic, says: The people of the gathering will know today who are the people of generosity. And it was said: And who are the people of generosity, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The people of remembrance in the mosques."
"11746","And with this isnad, that the Messenger of Allah said: The lowest of the people of Paradise in station is he who has eighty thousand servants and seventy-two wives, and a dome of pearl, ruby, and peridot is erected for him as between al-Jabiyah and Sanaa."
"11747","And with this isnad, that the Messenger of Allah said: Whoever humbles himself for Allah a degree, Allah raises him a degree until He places him in Illiyyin. And whoever is arrogant toward Allah a degree, Allah lowers him a degree until He places him in the lowest of the low."
"11748","And with this isnad, from the Messenger of Allah, that he said: If you see a man frequenting the mosque, testify for him with faith, for Allah said: Only populates the mosques of Allah whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day."
"11749","And with this isnad, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. He said it three times. He said: And what is the honoring of the guest, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Three days. What he sits beyond that is charity upon him."
"11750","And with this isnad, that the Messenger of Allah said: Whoever swears an oath and sees better than it, its expiation is abandoning it."
"11751","And with this isnad, he said: The Messenger of Allah said: If Allah loves a servant, He praises him with sevenfold good he did not do. And if Allah hates a servant, He praises him with sevenfold evil he did not do."
"11752","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Iblis said: My Lord, I will ceaselessly mislead the children of Adam while their souls are in their bodies. He said: Then the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, said: I will ceaselessly forgive them while they seek My forgiveness."
"11753","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah narrated to me, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave what he gave of those gifts among Quraysh and the tribes of the Arabs, and there was nothing of it among the Ansar, this clan of the Ansar found it in themselves, until much talk spread among them, until one of them said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has met his people. Then Sad ibn Ubadah entered upon him and said: O Messenger of Allah, this clan has found against you in themselves for what you did with this fay that you obtained. You divided among your people and gave great gifts among the tribes of the Arabs, and there was nothing in this clan of the Ansar. He said: Where are you in that, O Sad? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I am only a man of my people, and I am not. He said: Gather your people for me in this enclosure. He said: So Sad went out and gathered the people in that enclosure. He said: Some men of the Muhajirun came, and he left them and they entered, and others came and he turned them back. When they gathered, Sad came to him and said: This clan of the Ansar has gathered for you. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them, and praised Allah and extolled Him with what He deserves, then said: O company of the Ansar, what talk has reached me from you, and resentment you found in yourselves? Did I not come to you astray and Allah guided you, and poor and Allah enriched you, and enemies and Allah joined your hearts? They said: Rather, Allah and His Messenger are more bounteous and better. He said: Will you not answer me, O company of the Ansar? They said: With what shall we answer you, O Messenger of Allah, while to Allah and to His Messenger belong bounty and excellence? He said: By Allah, if you wished you would say, and you would speak truthfully and be believed: You came to us disbelieved and we believed you, and forsaken and we aided you, and expelled and we sheltered you, and poor and we enriched you. Do you find in yourselves, O company of the Ansar, concerning a trifle of the world with which I conciliate a people that they may accept Islam, while I entrust you to your Islam? Are you not pleased, O company of the Ansar, that the people go with sheep and camels and you return with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in your dwellings? By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, were it not for the Hijrah I would be a man of the Ansar. If the people took a path and the Ansar took a path, I would take the path of the Ansar. O Allah, have mercy on the Ansar, and the sons of the Ansar, and the sons of the sons of the Ansar. He said: So the people wept until they wet their beards, and said: We are pleased with the Messenger of Allah as share and portion. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed, and we dispersed."
"11754","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah al-Ansari, then al-Zafari, narrated to me, from Mahmud ibn Labid al-Zafari, one of Bani Abd al-Ashhal, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Yajuj and Majuj will be opened and emerge upon the people as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: From every elevation they hasten. And they will cover the earth, and the Muslims will withdraw from them to their cities and fortresses, and gather their livestock to them, and they will drink the waters of the earth, until some of them pass by the river and drink what is in it until they leave it dry, until those after them pass by that river and say: There was once water here. Until when none of the people remain except one in a fortress or city, one of them says: These people of the earth, we have finished them; there remain the people of heaven. He said: Then one of them shakes his spear and throws it to the sky, and it returns stained with blood, for trial and tribulation. While they are upon that, Allah sends worms in their necks like the naghaf of locusts that emerges in their necks, and they become dead in the morning with no sound heard from them. Then the Muslims say: Is there not a man who sells himself to see what this enemy has done? He said: Then a man of them strips himself for that, reckoning himself, thinking it likely he will be killed. He descends and finds them dead, some upon others. So he calls: O company of Muslims, rejoice, for Allah has sufficed you your enemy. Then they come out of their cities and fortresses and release their livestock, and it has no pasture except their flesh, and it becomes fat thereby as well as it ever becomes fat from any vegetation it ever grazed."
"11755","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Abu Said al-Khudri informed him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A people will come out of the Fire, burned, like char, and the people of Paradise will sprinkle water upon them, and they will sprout as scum sprouts in flood debris."
"11756","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah: Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Sahm, from Qazah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No fasting on the day of Eid, and no woman shall travel three days except with a mahram, and saddles shall not be tied except to three mosques: al-Masjid al-Haram, and the mosque of Madinah, and al-Masjid al-Aqsa. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bade farewell to a man and said to him: Where do you intend? He said: I intend Bayt al-Maqdis. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: A prayer in this mosque is better than a thousand prayers in other than it, except al-Masjid al-Haram."
"11757","Affan narrated to us: Wuhayb narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, from Nahar al-Abdi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah will question the servant on the Day of Resurrection, until He asks him, saying: O My servant, you saw wrong and did not denounce it. Then if Allah prompts His servant with his proof, he says: My Lord, I trusted in You and feared people."
"11758","Affan narrated to us: Mutamir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father: Qatadah narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Abd al-Ghafir, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he mentioned a man among those before, or he said: among those who were before you, then he mentioned a word meaning: Allah gave him wealth and children. He said: When death came to him he said to his sons: What kind of father was I to you? They said: A good father. He said: He had never stored any good with Allah ever. Qatadah explained it: He had not saved any good with Allah. And if Allah decrees against him He will punish him. When I die, burn me, until when I become charcoal, crush me, or he said: grind me, then when there is a stormy wind, scatter me in it. The Prophet of Allah said: So he took their covenants upon that. He said: So they did that, by my Lord. When he died they burned him, then crushed him or ground him, then scattered him on a stormy day. He said: Then Allah said to him: Be. And he was a standing man. Allah said: O My servant, what carried you to do what you did? And he said: My Lord, fear of You, or awe of You. He said: Nothing overtook him but that He had mercy on him. And he said another time: Nothing overtook him other than it but that He had mercy on him. He said: So I narrated it to Abu Uthman, and he said: I heard this from Salman more than once, except that he added: Then scatter me in the sea, or as he narrated."
"11759","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: Four men narrated to me, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the nabidh of the jar."
"11760","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Aban ibn Salih narrated to us, from Qusaym, the freedman of Umarah, from Qazah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Saddles shall not be tied except to three mosques: al-Masjid al-Haram, and al-Masjid al-Aqsa, and my mosque."
"11761","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment is a man wearing two sandals of fire, his brain boils from them, along with the ongoing punishment. And among them is one in the Fire to his ankles, along with the ongoing punishment. And among them is one in the Fire to his knees, along with the ongoing punishment. And among them is one in the Fire to his nose, along with the ongoing punishment. And among them is one in the Fire to his chest, along with the ongoing punishment, submerged."
"11762","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Ata ibn al-Saib informed us, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise and the Fire boasted. The Fire said: My Lord, the tyrants and kings and great and nobles enter me. And Paradise said: My Lord, the poor and weak and destitute enter me. Then the Blessed and Exalted said to the Fire: You are My punishment, I afflict with you whom I will. And He said to Paradise: You are My mercy, it embraces everything, and for each one of you is its fill. As for the Fire, its people are cast into it, and it says: Is there more, until the Blessed and Exalted comes to it and places His foot upon it, and it is drawn together and says: Enough, enough. As for Paradise, it remains as long as Allah wills it to remain, then Allah creates for it a creation as He wills. And Hasan al-Ashyab said: As for Paradise, it remains as long as Allah wills it to remain."
"11763","Affan narrated to us: Yazid, meaning Ibn Zuray, narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, he said: Bakr narrated to me that he informed him that Abu Said al-Khudri saw a dream that he was writing Sad. When he reached its prostration, he said: He saw the inkwell and the pen and everything in his presence turn prostrating. He said: So he told it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he kept prostrating with it afterwards."
"11764","Muhammad ibn Jafar Ghundar narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: If you hear the call, say like what he says."
"11765","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Jabir, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Qarazah, from Abu Said al-Khudri. I said: Did Muhammad hear it from Abu Said? He said: No. He said: I bought a sacrifice, and the wolf came and ate part of its tail, or ate its tail. So I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Sacrifice it."
"11766","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: He was asked about withdrawal. He said: Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about that, and he said: Do you create it? Do you provide for it? Settle it in its place, for it is only the decree."
"11767","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar, that he heard a man of Thaqif narrating from a man of Kinanah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said concerning this verse: Then We caused to inherit the Book those We chose of Our servants; among them wronging himself, and among them moderate, and among them foremost in good deeds. He said: All these are of one station, and all of them are in Paradise."
"11768","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah, he said: I heard Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The people of the Fire who are its people neither die therein nor live. But it afflicts a people for their sins or their faults, until when they become charcoal, permission is given for intercession. Then they are brought out in bundles and cast upon the rivers of Paradise. And it is said: O people of Paradise, pour water upon them. He said: So they sprout as the grain sprouts in flood debris."
"11769","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no sadaqah in less than five of dhawd, nor in five awsaq or five awaqi any sadaqah."
"11770","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, that he heard a freedman of Anas ibn Malik narrating from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a virgin in her chamber, and when he disliked something it was known in his face."
"11771","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Awf narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We came in an army from Madinah toward this east. He said: In the army was Abdillah ibn Sayyad, and no one would travel with him, nor accompany him, nor eat with him, nor drink with him, and they called him al-Dajjal. While I was one day staying in a dwelling of mine, Abdillah ibn Sayyad saw me sitting, and came until he sat with me, and said: O Abu Said, do you not see what the people do? No one travels with me, nor accompanies me, nor drinks with me, nor eats with me, and they call me al-Dajjal. And you know, O Abu Said, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Dajjal does not enter Madinah, and I was born in Madinah. And you heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Al-Dajjal will have no child born to him, and a child has been born to me. By Allah, I was about to, from what these people do to me, take a rope and be alone and place it in my neck and strangle myself, to rest from these people. By Allah, I am not al-Dajjal. But by Allah, if you wished I could tell you his name and his father's name and his mother's name and the name of the village from which he emerges."
"11772","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Awf narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: My community will split into two factions, and renegades will pass between them; the nearer of the two factions to the truth will kill them."
"11773","Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Zakariya narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies not associating anything with Allah enters Paradise. Abdillah said: I found this hadith in my father's book in his handwriting."
"11774","Abd al-Mutaal ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us: Mujalid narrated to us, from Abu al-Waddak, he said: Abu Said said to me: Do the Khawarij affirm al-Dajjal? And I said: No. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the seal of a thousand prophets or more. No prophet followed but he warned his community of al-Dajjal. And there has been clarified to me of his matter what was not clarified to anyone. He is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed. His right eye is blind, protruding, not hidden, as if it is sputum on a plastered wall. And his left eye is as if it is a brilliant star. With him are of every tongue, and with him is the image of Paradise, green, with water running in it, and the image of the Fire, black, smoking."
"11775","Abd al-Mutaal narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us: Mujalid narrated to us, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said, he said: Ibn Sayyad was mentioned before the Prophet, and Umar said: He claims that he passes nothing but it speaks to him."
"11776","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdillah said: And I heard it myself from Uthman: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise and the Fire argued. The Fire said: In me are the tyrants and the arrogant. And Paradise said: In me are the weak and poor of the people. He said: So He judged between them: You, Paradise, are My mercy, I have mercy with you upon whom I will. And you, Fire, are My punishment, I punish with you whom I will. And for both of you upon Me is their fill."
"11777","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Uthman: Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Num, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger said: The muhrim kills the snake, the scorpion, the kite, the vicious dog, and the fuwaysiqah. I said: What is the fuwaysiqah? He said: The mouse. I said: And what is the matter of the mouse? He said: The Prophet woke and it had taken the wick and climbed with it to the ceiling to burn it upon him."
"11778","Uthman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Uthman: Jarir narrated to us, from Yazid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Num, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fatimah is the mistress of the women of Paradise except what was of Maryam bint Imran."
"11779","Uthman narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Uthman: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will emerge at a break of time and appearance of trials a man called al-Saffah. His giving of wealth will be by handfuls."
"11780","Uthman narrated to us, Abdillah said: And I heard it myself from Uthman: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the sons of the family of so-and-so reach thirty men, they take the wealth of Allah as an estate, and the religion of Allah as deceit, and the servants of Allah as vassals."
"11781","Uthman narrated to us, Abdillah said: And I heard it myself from Uthman: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The wife of Safwan ibn al-Muattal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while we were with him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, my husband Safwan ibn al-Muattal beats me when I pray, and breaks my fast when I fast, and does not pray Fajr until the sun rises. He said: And Safwan was with him. He said: So he asked him about what she said. And he said: O Messenger of Allah, as for her saying he beats me when I pray, she reads two surahs and I forbade her them. He said: And he said: If it were one surah it would suffice people. As for her saying he breaks my fast, she fasts while I am a young man and cannot endure. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that day: No woman shall fast except with her husband's permission. He said: As for her saying that I do not pray until the sun rises, we are a household known for that; we hardly wake until the sun rises. He said: When you wake, then pray."
"11782","Harun narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the broken edge of the cup and blowing in the drink. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from Harun."
"11783","Ali ibn Abdillah narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, Mujalid informed us, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three to whom Allah laughs: the man who rises at night, and the people when they line for fighting."
"11784","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the Farewell Hajj: The most sacred of days is this day of yours, and the most sacred of months is this month of yours, and the most sacred of lands is this land of yours. Your wealth and your blood are unlawful to you as the sanctity of this day of yours, in this land of yours, in this month of yours. Have I conveyed? They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, bear witness."
"11785","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on the day of al-Nahr and mentioned its meaning."
"11786","Ali ibn Abdillah narrated to us: Muadh narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Amir al-Ahwal, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the believer desires a child in Paradise, its carrying and bearing and age are in an hour as he desires."
"11787","Ali ibn Abdillah narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Muhammad narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ishaq, from his paternal aunt, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is married for one of three traits: a woman is married for her wealth, and a woman is married for her beauty, and a woman is married for her religion. So take the one of religion and character, may your right hand be dusty."
"11788","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: I heard my father, from Yazid ibn al-Had, that Abdillah ibn Khabbab narrated to him that Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to him that Usayd ibn Hudayr, while one night reciting in his enclosure, his horse stirred. Then he recited, then it stirred again. Then he recited, then it stirred also. And Usayd said: I feared it would tread on Yahya, meaning his son. So I stood to it, and there was like a canopy over my head with things like lamps. It rose in the air until I no longer saw it. He said: In the morning I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, while last night in the depth of the night I recited in my enclosure, my horse stirred. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite, Ibn Hudayr. He said: So I recited, then it stirred also. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite, Ibn Hudayr. Then I recited, then it stirred. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite, Ibn Hudayr. He said: So I left, and Yahya was near it, and I feared it would tread on him. And I saw like a canopy with things like lamps. It rose in the air until I no longer saw it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those are the angels, they were listening to you. Had you recited, morning would find people seeing it, not hidden from them."
"11789","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Musa said: My Lord, Your believing servant is restricted upon in the world. He said: Then a gate of Paradise is opened for him and he looks at it. He said: O Musa, this is what I prepared for him. And Musa said: My Lord, by Your might and majesty, had he been cut off in hands and feet, dragged on his face since the day You created him until the Day of Resurrection, and this were his end, he would never have seen misery ever. He said: Then Musa said: My Lord, Your disbelieving servant, You expand for him in the world. He said: Then a gate of the Fire is opened for him, and it is said: O Musa, this is what I prepared for him. And Musa said: My Lord, by Your might and majesty, had he the world since the day You created him until the Day of Resurrection, and this were his end, it is as if he never saw good ever."
"11790","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf and Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Abu Said al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bathes on Friday and uses the siwak and touches perfume if he has it, and wears of his best clothes, then goes out until he comes to the mosque, and does not step over the necks of people, then prays what he wills to pray, then listens quietly when the imam emerges and does not speak until he finishes his prayer, it is expiation for what is between it and the Friday before it. He said: And Abu Hurayrah used to say: And three days extra; Allah made the good deed tenfold."
"11791","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When it is Friday, the angels sit at the doors of the mosque and write the people, who came of the people, by their stations. A man offers a camel, and a man offers a cow, and a man offers a sheep, and a man offers a chicken, and a man offers a sparrow, and a man offers an egg. He said: When the caller calls and the imam sits on the minbar, the scrolls are folded and they enter the mosque listening to the remembrance."
"11792","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to me that Ata ibn Yasar narrated to him that Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No ailment afflicts the believer, nor fatigue, nor sickness, nor grief, nor harm, even the worry that worries him, except Allah expiates thereby some of his sins."
"11793","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Yazid ibn Abdillah ibn Qusayt narrated to me that Abu Salamah and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban informed him that they heard Abu Said al-Khudri narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided among them varied food, some better than some. He said: So we went to outbid among ourselves, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to buy it except measure for measure, with no increase in it."
"11794","Yaqub narrated to us: Ibn Akhi Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle Muhammad ibn Muslim, he said: Salim ibn Abdillah narrated to me that Abu Said al-Khudri narrated to him like that, a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Abdillah ibn Umar met him and said: O Abu Said, what is this you narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And Abu Said said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Gold for gold like for like, and silver for silver like for like."
"11795","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Fitr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Raja al-Zubaydi, from his father, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: We were sitting waiting for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he emerged upon us from one of his wives' houses. He said: So we stood with him, and his sandal broke, and Ali stayed behind upon it mending it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proceeded, and we proceeded with him. Then he stood waiting for him, and we stood with him. And he said: Among you is one who fights for the interpretation of this Quran as I fought for its revelation. So we looked, and among us were Abu Bakr and Umar. And he said: No, but the mender of the sandal. He said: So we came to give him glad tidings. He said: And it was as if he had heard it."
"11796","Husayn narrated to us: Ibn Ayyash, meaning Ismail, narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Marwan al-Kalai and Aqil ibn Mudrik al-Sulami, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that a man came to him and said: Advise me. And he said: You asked about what I asked the Messenger of Allah about before you. I advise you with taqwa of Allah, for it is the head of everything, and upon you is jihad, for it is the monasticism of Islam, and upon you is remembrance of Allah and recitation of the Quran, for it is your spirit in heaven and your remembrance on earth."
"11797","Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Fitr narrated to us: Ismail ibn Raja narrated to me, he said: I heard my father say: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: We were sitting waiting for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: So I came to him to give him glad tidings. He said: And he did not raise his head with it, as if he had heard it."
"11798","Abu Nuaym narrated to us: al-Walid, meaning Ibn Abdillah ibn Jumay, narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah informed me, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Ibn Sayyad while he played with the boys. He said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have hidden for you something hidden. He said: Dukh. He said: Be gone, you will not exceed your measure."
"11799","Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ibn Abi Num, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youths of Paradise."
"11800","Abu Nuaym narrated to us: Yunus narrated to us: Abu al-Waddak Jabr ibn Nawf narrated to me, he said: Abu Said narrated to me, he said: We took captives on the day of Hunayn, and we practiced withdrawal with them, seeking to ransom them from their families. And some of us said to others: You do this while among you is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Come to him and ask him. So we came to him, or we mentioned that to him. He said: Not from all water is the child. If Allah decrees a matter it is. And we passed by the pots boiling, and he said to us: What is this meat? And we said: Donkey meat. And he said to us: Domestic or wild? And we said to him: Rather domestic. He said: So he said to us: Overturn it. He said: So we overturned it, though hungry desiring it. He said: And we were commanded to tie the mouths of the waterskins."
"11801","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from al-Dahhak al-Mashriqi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in a hadith he mentioned: a people will go out against a differing faction among the people; the closest of the two parties to the truth will kill them."
"11802","Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Masarrah ibn Ma'bad narrated to us, Abu Ubayd, the companion of Sulayman, narrated to me, he said: I saw Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi standing praying, wearing a black turban with its end hanging down behind him, his beard dyed yellow, so I went to pass in front of him and he turned me back, then he said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed the dawn prayer while he was behind him, and he recited and the recitation became confused for him, and when he finished his prayer he said: If you had seen me and Iblis, I reached out with my hand and I kept strangling him until I felt the cold of his saliva between these two fingers of mine, the thumb and the one next to it, and were it not for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, he would have remained tied to one of the pillars of the mosque, with the boys of Madinah playing with him, so whoever among you is able that no one come between him and the qiblah, let him do so."
"11803","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Mindal ibn Ali narrated to me, al-A'mash narrated to me, from Sa'd al-Ta'i, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The companion of five will not enter Paradise: the habitual drinker of wine, nor the believer in magic, nor the severer of kinship, nor the soothsayer, nor the reminder of favours."
"11804","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you doubts in his prayer and does not know how much he prayed, three or four, let him cast aside the doubt and build upon what he is certain of, then prostrate two prostrations before he gives the salutation. If he had prayed five, they were an intercession for his prayer. Musa once said: If he had prayed five, they intercede for his prayer, and if he had prayed a complete four, they were a humiliation for Satan."
"11805","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Ibn Lahi'ah, from Musa ibn Wardan, he said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-Wasilah is a rank with Allah, there is no rank above it, so ask Allah to grant me al-Wasilah."
"11806","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah, from his father, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the earth is a mosque and purification, except the graveyard and the bathhouse."
"11807","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The wasq is sixty sa's."
"11808","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a mountain were struck with a rod of iron it would crumble, then return as it was, and if a bucket of ghassaq were poured out in this world, the people of this world would stink."
"11809","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from his brother Ma'bad ibn Sirin, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: We alighted at a stopping place, and a woman came to us and said: The chief of the tribe has been stung; is there any reciter among you? He said: So a man stood up with her, whom we did not think knew ruqyah, and went with her and recited over him and he recovered, and they gave him thirty sheep. He said: And I think he said: And they gave us milk to drink. When he returned to us we said to him: Did you know ruqyah? He said: No, I only recited over him with the Opening of the Book. He said: So I said to them: Do not introduce anything concerning it until we come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When we arrived we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I mentioned that to him, and he said: How did he know that it is a ruqyah? Divide, and strike a share for me with you."
"11810","Yazid narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri and Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Amr ibn Yahya, from his father - Hammad in his hadith said: from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and Sufyan did not mention Abu Sa'id - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the earth is a mosque, except the graveyard and the bathhouse."
"11811","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, and he said: from Abu Sa'id, as he thought, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"11812","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Nu'man ibn Abi Ayyash, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance him from the Fire by a journey of seventy autumns."
"11813","Yazid narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Marzuq informed us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than a man who lost his mount in a desert land, and sought it and could not find it, then prepared himself for death, and while he was thus he heard the sound of the mount when it knelt down, and he uncovered his face, and behold, it was his mount."
"11814","Yazid narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Huddani informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: A wolf attacked a sheep and took it, and the shepherd pursued it and seized it from him, so the wolf sat back on its tail and said: Do you not fear Allah, taking from me provision that Allah drove to me? He said: How strange, a wolf sitting back on its tail speaking to me with the speech of humans. The wolf said: Shall I not inform you of something more strange than that? Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Yathrib informing the people of reports of what has passed. He said: So the shepherd came driving his sheep until he entered Madinah, and he gathered them to a corner of its corners, then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered and it was announced: the prayer is congregational. Then he came out and said to the shepherd: Inform them. So he informed them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the Hour will not come until beasts speak to humans, and a man is spoken to by the tip of his whip and the strap of his sandal, and his thigh informs him of what his family did after him."
"11815","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from a man, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not fear of people prevent one of you from speaking the truth when he witnesses it or knows it. Shu'bah said: So I narrated this hadith to Qatadah, and he said: What is this, Amr ibn Murrah from Abu al-Bakhtari from a man from Abu Sa'id? Abu Nadrah narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not fear of people prevent one of you from speaking the truth when he witnesses it or knows it. Abu Sa'id said: So that carried me to ride to Mu'awiyah and fill his ears, then I returned. Shu'bah said: Four men narrated this hadith to me from Abu Nadrah: Qatadah, Abu Maslamah, al-Jurayri, and another man."
"11816","Yazid and Abu al-Nadr both said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you doubts in the prayer and does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him stand and pray a rak'ah. Yazid said: Until the doubt is about the addition, then let him prostrate the two prostrations of forgetfulness. If he had prayed five, they intercede for his prayer, and if he had prayed four, they humiliate Satan."
"11817","Yazid narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us - my father and Abu Badr said: from Sa'id - from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When three gather, let one of them lead them, and the most entitled of them to lead is the most reciting among them."
"11818","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from al-Hasan, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Verily this world is green and sweet. Verily, beware of this world and beware of women. Verily every treacherous one will have a banner, and the greatest of that treachery is the leader of the generality. I did not forget his raising his voice with it."
"11819","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Salih Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Alqamah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took captives on the day of Awtas who had husbands among the people of polytheism, and some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held back and scrupled at approaching them. He said: So this verse came down concerning that: And married women, except what your right hands possess."
"11820","Bahz and Affan both said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abu Alqamah al-Hashimi, from Abu Sa'id, and he mentioned its meaning, except that he said: women."
"11821","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Bakr al-Muzani, he said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: I saw a dream while I was writing Surah Sad. When I reached the prostration, I saw the inkwell and the pen and everything in my presence turn over prostrating. He said: So I related it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he kept prostrating by it."
"11822","Rawh narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will surely follow the ways of those before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, until if they entered the hole of a lizard you would follow them. We said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews and the Christians? He said: Then who?"
"11823","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The wife of Safwan ibn Mu'attal came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Safwan makes me break my fast when I fast, and beats me when I pray, and does not pray the morning prayer until the sun rises. He said: So he sent for him and said: What does she say? He said: As for her saying that he makes me break my fast, I am a young man and I forbade her to fast. He said: On that day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a woman to fast except with her husband's permission. He said: As for her saying that I beat her over prayer, she recites two surahs and delays me. He said: If people recited them it would not harm you. As for her saying that I do not pray until the sun rises, I am heavy-headed, and I am of a household known for that, for heaviness of heads. He said: When you wake up, then pray."
"11824","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Zadhdhan, from al-Walid Abu Bishr, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand in Zuhr in the first two rak'ahs, in each rak'ah the measure of reciting thirty verses, and in the last two, in each rak'ah the measure of reciting fifteen verses, and he used to stand in Asr in the first two rak'ahs, in each rak'ah the measure of reciting fifteen verses, and in the last two the measure of half of that."
"11825","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, he said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate at Arafah thus, meaning with the outer side of his palm."
"11826","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Bishr, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting the day of Fitr and the day of Adha."
"11827","Yunus and Surayj both said: Hammad narrated to us, from Bishr, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade leeks, onions, and garlic. We said: Is it unlawful? He said: No, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"11828","Yunus narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, he said: I heard Abu Sa'id saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at Arafah and began supplicating thus, and he made the backs of his hands toward his face, and raised them above his nipples and below his shoulders."
"11829","Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, al-Hakam, meaning Ibn Aban, narrated to me, he said: I heard Ikrimah saying: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to me, he said: We used to take provisions from the dried meat of Hajj until a year almost passed over it."
"11830","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Sulayman al-Naji informed us, Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji informed us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr with his companions. He said: A man of his companions entered, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What kept you, O so-and-so, from the prayer? He said: He mentioned something, offering an excuse by it. He said: So he stood praying, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Will no man give charity to this one and pray with him? He said: So a man of the people stood and prayed with him."
"11831","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: Prices rose in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said to him: If only you would set our prices for us. He said: Allah is the Setter of value, or the Pricer. I hope to leave you with none of you seeking me for an injustice in wealth or soul."
"11832","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Suhayl ibn Abi Salih informed me, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows a funeral, let him not sit until it is placed down."
"11833","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of sacrifices beyond three days. He said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, we have dependents. He said: Eat, store, and do good."
"11834","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Iyas al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I think it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you come upon a wall, call its owner three times. If he answers you, otherwise eat without spoiling. If you come upon a shepherd, call him three times. If he answers you, otherwise eat and drink without spoiling. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days; what is after that is charity."
"11835","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah narrated to me, and they are two men of the Ansar of Banu Mazin ibn al-Najjar, and they were trustworthy, from Yahya ibn Umarah ibn Abi Hasan and Abbad ibn Tamim, and they are of their clan, and they were trustworthy, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no charity in less than five awaq of silver, and there is no charity in less than five camels, and there is no charity in less than five awsuq of dates."
"11836","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih - Ibn Shihab said: Abu Umamah ibn Sahl narrated to me that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was sleeping I saw people presented, wearing shirts, some reaching the breasts and some reaching below that, and Umar ibn al-Khattab passed by me wearing a shirt dragging it. They said: How did you interpret it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Religion. Ya'qub said: I cannot count how many times I heard him saying: Salih narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab."
"11837","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Salit ibn Ayyub ibn al-Hakam al-Ansari narrated to me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi' al-Ansari, then one of Banu Adi ibn al-Najjar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, how is water drawn for you from the well of Buda'ah, the well of Banu Sa'idah, when it is a well into which women's menstrual cloths, dogs' flesh, and people's impurities are thrown? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water is pure; nothing makes it impure."
"11838","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Qusayt narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yasar or his brother Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressing the people on his pulpit, saying: O people, I was shown Laylat al-Qadr, then I was made to forget it, and I saw that on my forearm were two bracelets of gold, and I disliked them and blew them and they flew away, and I interpreted them as these two liars, the one of Yemen and the one of Yamamah."
"11839","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn Ka'b ibn Ujrah, from his aunt Zaynab bint Ka'b, and she was with Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: People complained about Ali. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us as a preacher, and I heard him saying: O people, do not complain about Ali, for by Allah he is rough in the matter of Allah, or in the path of Allah."
"11840","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Kathir, he said: Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me that Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi' narrated to him that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating that it was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, do you perform ablution from the well of Buda'ah, when it is a well into which menstruation cloths, dogs' flesh, and stench are thrown? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Water is pure; nothing makes it impure."
"11841","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'ah narrated to me that he heard Yahya ibn Umarah ibn Abi Hasan and Abbad ibn Tamim narrating that they heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrating that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no charity in less than five awsuq of dates, nor in less than five awaq of silver, nor in less than five camels."
"11842","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Jabir, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Qarazah narrating from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri that he bought a ram to sacrifice, and a wolf ate of its tail, or its tail, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, and he said: Sacrifice it."
"11843","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Mujalid ibn Sa'id, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mudar will surely strike the servants of Allah until no name is worshipped for Allah, and the believers will surely strike them until they do not withhold the tail of a ravine."
"11844","Abu Sa'id narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Khabbab, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade continuous fasting. He said: Whoever must continue the fast, let him continue from dawn to dawn. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, you continue fasting. He said: I am not like you; I spend the night fed, one feeds me, and given drink, one gives me drink."
"11845","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Sa'id, and Qays ibn Wahb from Abu al-Waddak from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the expedition of Awtas: A pregnant woman is not to be approached until she delivers, nor one who is not pregnant until she menstruates one menstruation."
"11846","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad al-Qurdusi narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily, let not fear of people prevent a man, if he knows the truth, from standing by it."
"11847","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Atiyyah ibn Qays narrated to me, from one who narrated to him, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us of departure in the year of the Conquest on two nights passed of Ramadan, so we went out fasting, until when we reached al-Kadid, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to break the fast, and people woke, some fasting and some breaking, until when he reached the nearest stopping place facing the enemy, he ordered us to break the fast, and we all broke it."
"11848","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Atiyyah ibn Qays, from Qaza'ah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to depart in the year of the Conquest on two nights passed of Ramadan, so we went out fasting, until we reached al-Kadid, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to break the fast, and people woke divided, some fasting and some breaking."
"11849","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Atiyyah ibn Qays narrated to me, from one who narrated to him, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, he said: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling what You will of anything after, O Possessor of praise and glory, the truest of what the servant says, and we are all Your servants: None withholds what You give, and the fortune of the fortunate does not benefit him against You."
"11850","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Atiyyah ibn Qays, from Qaza'ah ibn Yahya, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, he said: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling what You will of anything after, O Possessor of praise and glory, the truest of what the servant says, and we are all Your servants: None withholds what You give, and the fortune of the fortunate does not benefit him against You."
"11851","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The chambers of those who love one another will surely be seen in Paradise like a rising star in the east or the west. It will be said: Who are these? It will be said: These are those who loved one another for Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"11852","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you doubts in his prayer, let him cast aside the doubt and build upon certainty, and pray two prostrations. If they were five, he intercedes by them, and if he had prayed four, they were a humiliation for Satan."
"11853","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily, let not fear of people prevent one of you from speaking the truth when he sees it."
"11854","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khulayd ibn Ja'far, he said: I heard Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: Musk was mentioned before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Is it not among the best of perfume?"
"11855","Hashim narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Ibn Abi Utbah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a virgin in her chamber, and when he disliked something we knew it in his face."
"11856","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah informed us, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No caliph is appointed except he has two entourages: an entourage commanding him to good and urging him to it, and an entourage commanding him to evil and urging him to it, so the protected is whom Allah protects."
"11857","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah informed us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah says to the people of Paradise: O people of Paradise. They say: At Your service, our Lord, and glad tidings. He says: Are you pleased? They say: Why should we not be pleased when You have given us what You have not given anyone of Your creation? He says: I give you better than that. They say: O our Lord, what is better than that? He said: I bestow upon you My pleasure, and I will not be angry after it ever."
"11858","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Yazid Abu Shuja' informed us, from Abu al-Samh, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: And they therein are frowning. He said: The Fire scorches him, so his upper lip contracts until it reaches the middle of his head, and his lower lip hangs down until it strikes his navel."
"11859","Bishr ibn Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, my father informed me, he said: Muhammad, meaning al-Zuhri, informed me, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw spittle in the wall of the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a pebble and scraped it off, then said: When one of you spits while praying, let him not spit before his face nor to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his left foot."
"11860","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ata ibn Yazid narrated to me that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to him that it was said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are best? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A believer striving in the path of Allah with himself and his wealth. They said: Then who? He said: A believer in a mountain pass among the passes, fearing Allah and sparing people his evil."
"11861","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Abd Allah ibn Muhayriz al-Jumahi informed me that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri informed him that while he was sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man of the Ansar came and said: O Messenger of Allah, we take captives and we love wealth; what do you think about withdrawal? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you really do that? It does not matter if you do not do that, for it is no soul that Allah has decreed to come out except it will come out."
"11862","Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which people are best? And he mentioned the meaning of Shu'ayb's hadith."
"11863","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shu'ayb informed us, Abd Allah ibn Abi Husayn narrated to me, Shahr narrated to me that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: While a Bedouin was in one of the outskirts of Madinah with his sheep, a wolf attacked him and took a sheep of his sheep, and the Bedouin caught up with it and rescued it from him and shouted at it, so the wolf opposed him, walking, then sat back tucking its tail, addressing him, and said: You took provision that Allah provided me. He said: How strange, a wolf sitting back tucking its tail addressing me. He said: By Allah, you leave something more strange than that. He said: What is more strange than that? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the two date-palms between the two lava tracts, narrating to the people about reports of what has passed and what will be after that. He said: So the Bedouin drove his sheep until he brought them to part of Madinah, then he walked to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he knocked on his door. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he said: Where is the Bedouin, the owner of the sheep? The Bedouin stood, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Narrate to the people what you heard and saw. So the Bedouin narrated to the people what he saw of the wolf and heard from it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said at that: He spoke the truth; signs that will be before the Hour. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the Hour will not come until one of you leaves his family and his sandal, his whip, or his staff informs him of what his family did after him."
"11864","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, al-Fudayl ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, he said: Abu Sa'id said: A man of the Ansar said to his companions: By Allah, I used to narrate to you that if matters became settled he would prefer others over you. He said: So they answered him harshly. He said: That reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he came to them and said things to them that I do not remember. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So you used not to ride horses. He said: Whenever he said something to them they said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: When he saw them not answering him with anything, he said: Will you not say: Your people fought you and we aided you, and your people expelled you and we sheltered you? They said: We do not say that, O Messenger of Allah; you say it. He said: O company of Ansar, are you not pleased that people go with this world and you go with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: O company of Ansar, are you not pleased that if people took a valley and you took a valley, I would take the valley of the Ansar? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Were it not for the Hijrah I would be a man of the Ansar; my inner garment and household and chest in which I take refuge. Pardon their wrongdoer and accept from their good-doer. Abu Sa'id said: I said to Mu'awiyah: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that we would see after him preference. Mu'awiyah said: What did he command you? I said: He commanded us to be patient. He said: Then be patient."
"11865","Rawh narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will surely follow the ways of those before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, until if they entered the hole of a lizard you would follow them. We said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews and the Christians? He said: Then who?"
"11866","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid narrated to me, Shahr narrated to me, he said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to us, he said: While a man of Aslam was with his small flock, shaking leaves for them in the desert of Dhu al-Hulayfah, a wolf attacked him and seized a sheep of his sheep, and the man shouted at it and threw stones at it until he rescued his sheep from it. Then the wolf came until it sat back tucking its tail, facing the man, and he mentioned it like the hadith of Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah."
"11867","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Isra'il Isma'il al-Mula'i narrated to us, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A slain one, or a dead one, was found between two villages, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered and what was between the two villages was measured, to which of them he was closer, and he was found closer to one of them by a span. He said: It is as if I look at the span of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he assigned him to the one he was closer to."
"11868","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id, and Qutaybah narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father, he said: Two men disputed about the mosque founded upon piety. One of them said: It is the mosque of Quba, and the other said: It is the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is this mosque of mine."
"11869","Rawh, Abd al-Samad, and Abu Amir said: Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Ibrahim - Abu Amir said: from Abu Ibrahim al-Ansari - from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions shaved their heads in the year of Hudaybiyah, except Uthman ibn Affan and Abu Qatadah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for those who shaved three times, and for those who shortened once."
"11870","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, that Abu Ibrahim al-Ansari of Banu Abd al-Ashhal said: Abu Sa'id said, and he mentioned the hadith."
"11871","Rawh narrated to us, Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing raisins and dates, and unripe dates and dates."
"11872","Rawh and Muhammad ibn Bakr both said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba, hantam, naqir, and muzaffat, and mixing raisins and dates, and unripe dates and dates."
"11873","Rawh narrated to us, Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba, hantam, naqir, and muzaffat, and mixing raisins and dates, and unripe dates and dates."
"11874","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba, naqir, and muzaffat, and said: Make nabidh in your waterskin and tie its mouth."
"11875","Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: One who met the delegation that came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Abd al-Qays, among them al-Ashajj, narrated to me. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a tribe of Rabi'ah, and between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar. And he mentioned like the hadith of Yahya, and he did not mention that in you are two traits."
"11876","Rawh narrated to us, al-Muthanna al-Qasir narrated to us, Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking in hantamah, dubba, and naqir."
"11877","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me, from Abu Sa'id, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People will come out of the Fire, having burned, and they were like charcoal, then the people of Paradise will keep sprinkling water upon them until they sprout like the sprouting of rubbish in the flood."
"11878","Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that Abu Sa'id informed him that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People will come out of the Fire, and he mentioned it."
"11879","Rawh narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A group will come out of the Fire, having been charcoal. He said: It will be said: Scatter them in Paradise and sprinkle water upon them. He said: So they sprout as a grain sprouts in the flood's carried debris. A man of the people said: It is as if you were of the people of the desert, O Messenger of Allah."
"11880","Rawh narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah, that Rafi' ibn Ishaq informed him, he said: I and Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah entered upon Abu Sa'id al-Khudri visiting him, and Abu Sa'id said to us: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us that the angels do not enter a house in which there are statues or an image. Ishaq doubted; he does not know which of them Abu Sa'id said."
"11881","Al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, my father narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Umayr al-Ansari, he said: I sat with Abd Allah ibn Umar and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and one of them said to his companion: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning that the sweat will reach people on the Day of Resurrection. One of them said: To his earlobe, and the other said: It bridles him. Ibn Umar drew a line, and Abu Asim pointed with his finger from below his earlobes to his mouth, and said: I do not see that except the same."
"11882","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik and Yunus ibn Yazid informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear the mu'adhdhin - and Malik said: the caller - say like what he says. Malik added: the mu'adhdhin."
"11883","Mahbub ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Khalid, from Ikrimah, that Ibn Abbas said to him and to his son Ali: Go to Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and hear from his hadith. He said: So we went, and he was in a wall of his. When he saw us he took his cloak and came to us and sat, and began narrating to us until he came to the mention of building the mosque. He said: We used to carry a brick at a time, and Ammar ibn Yasir used to carry two bricks at a time. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him and began wiping the dust from him, saying: O Ammar, will you not carry a brick as your companions carry? He said: I want the reward from Allah. He said: So he began wiping the dust from him, saying: Woe to Ammar, the rebellious party will kill him; he calls them to Paradise and they call him to the Fire. He said: So Ammar began saying: I seek refuge with the Most Merciful from trials."
"11884","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Abi Utbah narrating from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a virgin in her chamber, and when he disliked something we knew it in his face."
"11885","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, Unays ibn Abi Yahya narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us in his illness in which he died, binding his head. He said: So I followed him until he ascended the pulpit. He said: He said: I am now standing upon the Hawd. He said: Then he said: A servant was offered this world and its adornment, and he chose the Hereafter, and none of the people understood it except Abu Bakr, and he said: May my father and mother be ransom for you; rather we ransom you with our wealth, ourselves, and our children. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended from the pulpit, and he was not seen upon it until now."
"11886","Safwan narrated to us, Unays ibn Abi Yahya narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that a man of Banu Amr ibn Awf and a man of Banu Khudrah disputed about the mosque founded upon piety. The Awfi said: It is the mosque of Quba, and the Khudri said: It is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that, and he said: It is this mosque of mine, and in that there is much good."
"11887","Isma'il narrated to us, al-Dastuwai narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Abi Maymunah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon the pulpit and we sat around him, and he said: What I fear for you after me is what will be opened for you of the bloom of this world and its adornment. A man said: Does good bring evil, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was silent toward him. It was said to him: What is with you, speaking to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he does not speak to you? He said: And we saw that revelation was descending upon him. He said: So he recovered, wiping sweat from him, and said: Where is this questioner? It is as if he praised him. He said: Good does not bring evil. Among what spring rain grows is what kills or nearly does, except the eater of green herbage, for it ate until when its flanks filled it faced the sun, then dropped dung and urinated, then grazed. This wealth is green and sweet, and how good a companion of the Muslim it is, for one who gives of it to the orphan, the poor, and the wayfarer, or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. One who takes it without its right is like one who eats and is not satiated, and it will be a witness against him on the Day of Resurrection."
"11888","Surayj narrated to us, Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said upon the pulpit one day: What I fear for you. And he mentioned the hadith, and said: It kills by surfeit or nearly does."
"11889","Isma'il narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to me, and Rawh narrated to us, Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Abu Sa'id, the freedman of al-Mahri, narrated to me, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition to Banu Lahyan of Banu Hudhayl - Rawh said: of Hudhayl - he said: Let one of every two men go forth, and the reward is between them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless for us our mudd and our sa', and make with blessing two blessings."
"11890","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from a man, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you belittle himself when he sees a matter of Allah upon which there is a saying, and does not speak by it, and meets Allah having neglected that, and He says: What prevented you? He says: I feared people. He says: I was more entitled to be feared."
"11891","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj narrated to me, Shu'bah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let not fear of people prevent one of you from speaking a truth when he knows it. He said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: Trial kept upon us until we fell short, and we reach into evil. And Hajjaj in his hadith said: I heard Abu Nadrah."
"11892","Hajjaj narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with eighteen passed of Ramadan, and fasters fasted and breakers broke, and these did not blame these, nor these these. Shu'bah said: Four narrated this hadith to me, one of them Qatadah, and this is the hadith of Qatadah."
"11893","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj narrated to me, Shu'bah narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Mutawakkil - Hajjaj in his hadith said: I heard Abu al-Mutawakkil - from Abu Sa'id, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My brother's stomach has become loose. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give him honey to drink. So he gave him to drink, and said: I gave him to drink and it only increased him in looseness. He said that to him three times, then he came to him the fourth time and said: Give him honey to drink. He said: I gave him and it only increased him in looseness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah spoke the truth and your brother's stomach lied. So he gave him to drink and he recovered."
"11894","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Sa'id, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned its meaning."
"11895","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Sulayman or Abu Sulayman - and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to me, and said: a man of Quraysh - from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There will be rulers whom crowds or entourages of people frequent, wronging and lying. Whoever aids them in their wrongdoing and believes them in their lying is not of me nor am I of him, and whoever does not believe them in their lying nor aids them in their wrongdoing, I am of him and he is of me."
"11896","Bahz narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, and Hajjaj narrated to me, Shu'bah narrated to me, Qatadah informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Utbah - Hajjaj said: Ibn Utbah, the freedman of Anas ibn Malik - he said: I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was more modest than a virgin in her chamber, and when he disliked something we knew it in his face."
"11897","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, that he said: I bear witness upon Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id that they bore witness upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: No people sit remembering Allah except the angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquillity descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."
"11898","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, that Marwan preached before the prayer, and a man said to him: The prayer is before the sermon. Marwan said to him: That was left, O Abu so-and-so. Abu Sa'id said: As for this, he has fulfilled what was upon him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Whoever among you sees a wrong, let him deny it with his hand; if he cannot, with his tongue; if he cannot, with his heart, and that is the weakest of faith."
"11899","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Na'amah al-Sa'di narrated to us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us one day, and when he was in part of his prayer he took off his sandals and placed them to his left. When the people saw that they took off their sandals. When he finished his prayer he said: What is with you that you cast off your sandals? They said: We saw you cast off your sandals, so we cast off our sandals. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril came to me and informed me that in them was filth, or he said: harm, so I cast them off. When one of you comes to the mosque, let him look in his sandals; if he sees in them filth, or he said: harm, let him wipe them and pray in them. My father said: In this hadith there did not come an explanation of what was in the sandal."
"11900","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about withdrawal, and he said: If you do that, it does not matter if you do not do it, for it is no soul that Allah has decreed to be except it will be."
"11901","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abu Said informed him, and Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw phlegm on the wall of the mosque, so he took a pebble and scraped it off, then he said: When one of you clears his throat, let him not clear it toward his front nor to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his left foot."
"11902","Sakan ibn Nafi narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw phlegm in the direction of the qiblah, so he took a pebble and scraped it off with it, then he said: Let no one clear his throat toward the qiblah nor to his right, but let him spit to his left or under his left foot."
"11903","Marwan ibn Shuja narrated to us, Khusayf narrated to me, from Mujahid, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, twice on the minbar saying: Gold for gold and silver for silver, weight for weight."
"11904","Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Salim, meaning Ibn Abi Hafsah, and al-Amash and Abdullah ibn Suhban and Kathir al-Nawwa and Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people of the highest ranks will be seen by those beneath them as you see the rising star on a horizon of the horizons of the sky. And indeed Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and blessed be they."
"11905","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Shahr, he said: We met Abu Said while we were intending to go to al-Tur, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: al-Masjid al-Haram, the mosque of al-Madinah, and Bayt al-Maqdis."
"11906","Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked about coitus interruptus, and he said: Not from all fluid comes offspring; when Allah intends to create a thing, nothing can prevent Him."
"11907","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, and Hashim, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No man who believes in Allah and His Messenger hates the Ansar. And Hashim said: believes in Allah and the Last Day."
"11908","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Amash, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you fights his brother, let him avoid the face."
"11909","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Abi Said, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us not to let anyone pass in front of us, and if he refuses except that we push him back, or something like this."
"11910","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah, and Abd al-Ala, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, and Abd al-Ala said: from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade drinking by bending the mouths of waterskins."
"11911","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you yawns, let him place his hand over his mouth, for Satan enters with yawning."
"11912","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Some people from the Ansar came and asked him, and he gave them. He continued, no one among them asked him except he gave him, until what he had was exhausted. Then he said to them when he had spent everything in his hand: Whatever good we have, we will not withhold it from you. Whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste, and whoever seeks independence, Allah will make him independent, and whoever strives to be patient, Allah will make him patient. And you will never be given a gift better and more encompassing than patience."
"11913","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: I heard Malik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, and he mentioned the like of its meaning."
"11914","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: No people gather remembering Allah except angels surround them, mercy covers them, tranquility descends upon them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him. And he said: Allah gives respite until when it is the last third of the night, Allah Almighty descends to this heaven and calls out: Is there a repentant sinner, is there one seeking forgiveness, is there a supplicant, is there a petitioner, until dawn."
"11915","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from a man, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: A man placed his hand on the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: By Allah, I cannot bear to place my hand on you due to the severity of your fever. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: We, the company of prophets, tribulation is multiplied for us as reward is multiplied for us. If a prophet among the prophets is afflicted with lice until it kills him, and if a prophet among the prophets is afflicted with poverty until he takes a cloak and cuts it, and they used to rejoice in tribulation as you rejoice in ease."
"11916","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, al-Thawri informed us, from al-Amash, from Dhakwan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you hurries in intercourse or does not ejaculate, let him not perform ghusl."
"11917","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he saw mud on the nose of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the tip of his nose, from the trace of prostration, and it had rained during the night."
"11918","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, observed itikaf in the mosque, and heard them raising their voices in recitation while he was in his dome, so he uncovered the curtains and said: Each of you is conversing privately with his Lord, so let none of you harm another, nor let one raise his voice over another in recitation, or he said: in prayer."
"11919","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from a man, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You will surely follow the ways of the Children of Israel, span by span and cubit by cubit, until if a man among the Children of Israel entered a lizard hole, you would follow them in it. And once he said: you would follow him in it."
"11920","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the believers are saved from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection and feel secure, none of you disputing with his companion concerning a right due to him in this world disputes more intensely than the believers disputing with their Lord concerning their brothers who were admitted to the Fire. He said: They say: Our Lord, our brothers used to pray with us and fast with us and perform Hajj with us, yet You admitted them to the Fire. He said: Then He says: Go and bring out whomever you recognize. So they come to them and recognize them by their forms, the Fire does not consume their forms. Among them are those whom the Fire has taken up to the middle of their shins, and among them are those whom it has taken up to their ankles. So they bring them out and say: Our Lord, we have brought out whomever You commanded us. Then He says: Bring out whoever had in his heart the weight of a dinar of faith, then whoever had in his heart the weight of half a dinar, until He says: whoever had in his heart the weight of an atom. Abu Said said: Whoever does not believe this, let him recite this verse: Indeed Allah does not wrong the weight of an atom, and if it is a good deed He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward. He said: Then they say: Our Lord, we have brought out whomever You commanded us, and there remains in the Fire no one in whom there is good. He said: Then Allah says: The angels have interceded, the prophets have interceded, and the believers have interceded, and there remains the Most Merciful of the merciful. He said: Then He takes a handful from the Fire, or he said: two handfuls, of people who never did any good for Allah at all, who have burned until they became charred. He said: They are brought to a water called the water of life, and it is poured over them, and they grow as a seed grows in the silt of a flood. They come out of their bodies like pearls, with a seal on their necks, the freed ones of Allah. He said: It is said to them: Enter Paradise; whatever you wish for or see of anything, it is yours, and I have for you better than this. He said: They say: Our Lord, what is better than that. He says: My pleasure upon you, I will never be angry with you again."
"11921","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to me, Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Amr ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade mulamasah, and mulamasah is touching a garment without looking at it, and munabadhah, which is the throwing of the garment by a man in a sale before turning it over and looking at it."
"11922","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr both said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Jundai, he heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: There is no prayer after the dawn prayer until the sun rises, and Ibn Bakr said: until the sun ascends, and there is no prayer after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets."
"11923","Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr both said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Ata ibn Abi al-Khuwar informed me, from Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad and Ata ibn Bukht, both informing Umar ibn Ata, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that they heard him saying: I heard Abu al-Qasim saying: There is no prayer after the dawn prayer until the sun rises, and there is no prayer after the afternoon prayer until night."
"11924","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Salih, and Ibn Shihab narrated, from Amir ibn Sad, he informed him that Abu Said al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade mulamasah, and mulamasah is touching a garment without looking at it, and munabadhah, and munabadhah is a man throwing his garment to a man before turning it over."
"11925","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, Ibn Shihab said: Ata ibn Yazid al-Jundai narrated to me that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned the like of it, meaning the like of the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq and Ibn Bakr, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, and he said: until the sun ascends."
"11926","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade two kinds of dress and two kinds of sale. As for the two kinds of dress: wrapping in one garment, that he wraps himself in a single garment placing both ends of the garment on his left shoulder and covering himself with its right side, and the other, that he sits with his knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing else on him, exposing his private part to the sky. As for the two sales: munabadhah and mulamasah. Munabadhah is that he says: when you throw this garment, the sale is concluded. And mulamasah is that he touches it with his hand without wearing it or turning it over; when he touches it, the sale is concluded."
"11927","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, and he said: al-Thawri said: Abu Ishaq narrated to me that al-Agharr narrated to him, from Abu Said al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: A caller will call out: You shall live and never die, you shall be healthy and never fall ill, you shall be young and never grow old, you shall enjoy bliss and never suffer misery. That is the saying of Allah Almighty: And they will be called: That is Paradise which you have inherited for what you used to do."
"11928","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, he said: I heard Abu Said al-Khudri that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The Hour will not come until two great parties fight, their claim being one, and a renegade group splits off between them, killed by the one of them closer to the truth."
"11929","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The servant remains in prayer as long as he remains in his prayer place waiting for the prayer. The angels say: O Allah, forgive him, O Allah, have mercy on him, until he leaves or breaks his ablution. So I said: What is breaking it. He said: Such. I said to Abu Said, and he said: Passing wind loudly or quietly."
"11930","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Abu al-Sahba narrated to us, he said: I heard Said ibn Jubayr narrating from Abu Said al-Khudri, I do not know it except that he raised it, he said: When the son of Adam wakes in the morning, his limbs humble themselves before the tongue, saying: Fear Allah concerning us, for if you are upright we are upright, and if you deviate we deviate."
"11931","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, he said: Qatadah informed us, from al-Hasan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you create him, do you provide for him. Leave him in his place, for it was only decree."
"11932","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade fasting two days, the day of Fitr and the day of Adha, and forbade two kinds of dress, the samma, and that a man sit with knees drawn up in a single garment, and forbade prayer at two times, after dawn and after afternoon."
"11933","Affan and Hasan both said: Hammad narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Harb, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to supplicate at Arafah. Hasan said: And he raised his hands thus, making their backs above and their palms below. And Hammad described, and Hammad raised his hands with his palms toward the ground."
"11934","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer, takes a hair from his backside and pulls it, so he imagines he has broken his ablution. Let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."
"11935","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Satan comes to one of you while he is in his prayer, takes a hair from his backside and pulls it, so he imagines he has broken his ablution. Let him not leave until he hears a sound or finds a smell."
"11936","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah Almighty will surely send in this ummah a caliph who scoops up wealth scooping and does not count it counting."
"11937","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, al-Mualla ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: al-Ala, a man from Banu Muzaynah, narrated to me, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that they were sitting reciting the Quran and supplicating. He said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to them. He said: When we saw him we fell silent. He said: Were you not doing such and such. We said: Yes. He said: Do as you were doing. And he sat with us. Then he said: Give glad tidings to the poor Muhajirun of triumph on the Day of Resurrection over the rich by five hundred, I think he said: years."
"11938","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Suhayl narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When one of you yawns, let him hold his hand over his mouth, for Satan enters."
"11939","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Bishr ibn Harb informed us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he forbade continuous fasting in fasting, and his companions kept pressing him until he permitted them from sahar to sahar."
"11940","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Artah informed us, from Atiyyah ibn Sad, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The people of camels and the people of sheep boasted before the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pride and arrogance are among the people of camels, and tranquility and dignity are among the people of sheep. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Musa, peace be upon him, was sent while he was herding sheep for his family, and I was sent while I was herding sheep for my family at Jiyad."
"11941","Abu Muawiyah al-Ghilabi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Ansari, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The whole earth is a mosque except the bathhouse and the graveyard."
"11942","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever comes to a funeral among its family and follows it until he prays over it, he has a qirat, and whoever accompanies it onward, he has two qirats like Uhud."
"11943","Affan narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl informed us, Abu Nadrah narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A renegade group will split off at a division among the Muslims, killed by the party of the two factions closer to the truth."
"11944","Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: Our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to recite the Opening of the Book and whatever is easy."
"11945","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Said al-Jurayri informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We performed Hajj and stopped under the shade of a tree, and Ibn Said came and stopped beside me. He said: So I said: What has Allah afflicted me with. Then he came to me and said: O Abu Said, do you not see what I meet from the people, they say you are the Dajjal. Did you not hear the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The Dajjal will have no child born to him, and will not enter al-Madinah nor Makkah. And I have now come from al-Madinah, and here I am going to Makkah. And Hammad said: And he had entered Makkah, and a child was born to me. Until I felt pity for him. Then he said: By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of people of his place now. So I said: Perish you all day."
"11946","Affan narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Said al-Asha, from Ayyub ibn Bushayr, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever raises three daughters, disciplines them, shows them mercy, and treats them well, he has Paradise. Abd Allah said: My father, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah, meaning al-Tahhan, and Malik ibn Anas and Abu al-Ahwas and Hammad ibn Zayd died in the year one hundred ninety-nine, except that Malik died shortly before Hammad ibn Zayd. My father said: In that year I sought hadith. We were at the door of Hushaym while he was dictating to us, either he said: Funerals, or Rites, when a Basran man came and said: Hammad ibn Zayd has died, may Allah have mercy on them all."
"11947","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he said: I heard my father narrating, he said: I asked Abu Said about the lower garment, and he said: You have come upon one well informed. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The lower garment of the believer is to mid-calf, and there is no harm, or no blame, in what is between it and the ankles. What is below the ankles is in the Fire. And whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him."
"11948","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to Ibn Said: What do you see. He said: I see a throne upon the sea with snakes around it. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: That is the throne of Iblis."
"11949","Waki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that he was sitting with Marwan when a funeral passed, and Abu Said passed by him, and he said: Stand, O commander, for this one knows that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he followed a funeral, did not sit until it was placed down."
"11950","Waki narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim al-Abdi narrated to us, Abu al-Mutawakkil al-Naji narrated to us, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, salt for salt, like for like, hand to hand. Whoever adds or seeks addition has dealt in usury; the taker and the giver therein are alike."
"11951","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Charity is not lawful for a rich man except for three: in the path of Allah, or a wayfarer, or a man who had a neighbor to whom charity was given and he gifted some to him."
"11952","Waki narrated to us, Idris ibn Yazid al-Awdi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no charity on less than five awsaq."
"11953","Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, from Yahya ibn Umarah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no charity on less than five awsaq of dates or grain."
"11954","Waki narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra narrated to us, from Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Sarh, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: We used to give the charity of Fitr when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was among us, a sa of food, or a sa of dates, or a sa of barley, or a sa of raisins, or a sa of dried yogurt. We continued thus until Muawiyah came to us."
"11955","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays al-Farra informed us, he said: I heard Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Sarh that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri saying: We used to give, and he mentioned the hadith."
"11956","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Hashim narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Riyah, from his father or from another, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he finished his food, said: Praise be to Allah who fed us and gave us drink and made us Muslims."
"11957","Waki narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Mansur, from a man, from Abu Said, from the Prophet, the like of it."
"11958","Waki narrated to us, from Yunus, Abu al-Waddak Jabir ibn Nawf narrated to us, from Abu Said, he said: We captured donkeys on the day of Khaybar, and the pots were boiling with them. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is this. We said: Donkeys we captured. He said: Wild or domestic. He said: We said: No, but domestic. He said: Overturn them. He said: So we overturned them."
"11959","Waki narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a man for a prescribed punishment. He said: So we struck with two sandals forty times. Misar said: I think it was for drink."
"11960","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, concerning His saying: On the day when some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith. He said: The rising of the sun from its setting place."
"11961","Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Atiyyah ibn Sad, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people of the highest ranks will be seen by those below them as you see the rising star on the horizon of the horizons of the sky. And Abu Bakr and Umar are among them, and blessed be they."
"11962","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Mujalid narrated to us, from Abu al-Waddak, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: I said: By Allah, no commander comes to us except he is worse than the one before, and no year except it is worse than the one before. He said: Were it not for something I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I would say the like of what you say. But I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Among your commanders will be a commander who scoops up wealth scooping and does not count it counting. A man comes to him and asks him, and he says: Take. So the man spreads out his garment and he scoops into it. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spread out a thick sheet that was upon him, imitating the action of the man, then gathered its sides to him. He said: Then he takes it and goes away."
